/* Lecture 11 video lecture data: chapters, slide start times, timed bilingual transcript (generated). */
window.LEC = {"num":11,"videoBase":"https://wabyking.github.io/nlp2026-videos-2/lecture11/","parts":[{"n":1,"title":"Why Efficiency? Scaling Laws, Costs and the Memory Gap","blurb":"Models, data and usage grow faster than hardware: scaling laws, the gap between model size and GPU memory, what frontier models cost, and a map of the methods to come.","file":"lecture11_part1.mp4","poster":"lecture11_part1.jpg","duration":809.9,"first":1,"last":15,"slides":[{"n":1,"title":"Title: Lecture 11","t":0.8},{"n":2,"title":"Contents","t":72.22},{"n":3,"title":"1 Why Efficiency?","t":153.81},{"n":4,"title":"Today's Main Course: Efficiency","t":182.18},{"n":5,"title":"Why do we need efficiency?","t":218.43},{"n":6,"title":"LLMs follow Scaling Laws","t":244.23},{"n":7,"title":"Model size of LMs is growing exponentially, yet the hardware…","t":324.1},{"n":8,"title":"Bridge the gap between the supply and demand of AI computing","t":392.37},{"n":9,"title":"The Guessed Sizes for Anthropic Claude","t":438.76},{"n":10,"title":"Using (expensive) AI largely improves working efficiency","t":491.49},{"n":11,"title":"Type I: Efficiency within Transformer","t":539.93},{"n":12,"title":"Type II: Efficiency beyond Transformer","t":597.27},{"n":13,"title":"Efficiency after LLMs","t":647.4},{"n":14,"title":"Space Efficiency: From Parameters to Memory","t":690.9},{"n":15,"title":"Time Efficiency vs. Space Efficiency","t":749.42}],"sents":[[0.8,6.7,1,"Good morning, everyone, and welcome to Lecture eleven, our last regular lecture of the semester.","大家早上好，欢迎来到第十一讲，这是本学期最后一次常规课。"],[7.05,17.61,1,"Last time we looked at multimodal LLMs: how we plug a vision encoder into a language model, and turn images and other signals into tokens.","上一讲我们学习了多模态大模型：如何把视觉编码器接到语言模型上，把图像和其他信号变成 token。"],[17.96,21.96,1,"That lets one model reason across text, pictures and more.","这样一个模型就能在文字、图片等多种信息之间进行推理。"],[22.31,24.88,1,"You may have noticed a side effect there.","你们可能注意到了其中的一个副作用。"],[25.23,34.59,1,"An image can easily become hundreds or thousands of tokens, so multimodal models make sequences longer and serving more expensive.","一张图像很容易就变成几百甚至几千个 token，所以多模态模型让序列更长，服务成本也更高。"],[34.94,37.88,1,"That brings us to today's topic: efficiency.","这就引出了今天的主题：效率。"],[38.23,47.33,1,"Everything we've built this semester, from Transformers to pre-training, RL post-training, agents and multimodal models, has a price tag.","这学期我们构建的一切，从 Transformer 到预训练、强化学习后训练、智能体和多模态模型，都是有代价的。"],[47.68,52.0,1,"That price is paid in GPU hours, memory and electricity.","这个代价体现在 GPU 时长、显存和电力上。"],[52.35,58.98,1,"Today we ask how to make LLMs smaller, faster and cheaper, without making them worse.","今天我们要问：如何让大模型更小、更快、更便宜，同时又不变差。"],[59.33,61.71,1,"This is not just an engineering detail.","这可不只是一个工程细节。"],[62.06,70.82,1,"Efficiency decides who can train a model, who can serve it to millions of users, and whether you can run one on your own laptop for your final project.","效率决定了谁能训练模型、谁能把它服务给数百万用户，以及你能否在自己的笔记本上为期末项目跑一个模型。"],[72.07,73.99,2,"Here's our roadmap for today.","这是我们今天的路线图。"],[74.34,77.91,2,"We'll start with foundations: why efficiency matters at all.","我们从基础开始：效率究竟为什么重要。"],[78.26,84.77,2,"We'll look at scaling laws, and the growing gap between what models need and what hardware gives us.","我们会看看规模定律，以及模型需求和硬件供给之间不断扩大的差距。"],[85.12,88.1,2,"Then come two big families of methods.","接下来是两大类方法。"],[88.45,91.44,2,"The first family changes the model itself.","第一类方法改变模型本身。"],[91.79,99.54,2,"That means efficient architectures, like sparse attention, shared key-value heads and Mixture of Experts.","也就是高效架构，比如稀疏注意力、共享键值头，以及混合专家模型。"],[99.89,105.35,2,"It also means model compression: quantization, pruning and distillation.","还包括模型压缩：量化、剪枝和蒸馏。"],[105.7,109.09,2,"The second family keeps the model but changes how we run it.","第二类方法保留模型不变，而是改变我们运行它的方式。"],[109.44,116.25,2,"That covers efficient training, with LoRA, adapters, and distributed training with ZeRO.","这包括高效训练，比如 LoRA、适配器，以及使用 ZeRO 的分布式训练。"],[116.6,126.58,2,"And it covers efficient inference, with the KV cache, PagedAttention, speculative decoding, FlashAttention and vLLM.","还包括高效推理，比如 KV 缓存、PagedAttention、投机解码、FlashAttention 和 vLLM。"],[126.93,131.47,2,"We'll finish with an outlook on where things are heading in two thousand twenty-six.","最后我们会展望一下二零二六年的发展趋势。"],[131.82,137.63,2,"Keep the question on the right in mind for the whole lecture: where does the time and memory actually go?","整节课请记住右边这个问题：时间和内存究竟花在了哪里？"],[137.98,139.44,2,"It's not only FLOPs.","不只是浮点运算量。"],[139.79,148.38,2,"Very often the real bottleneck is moving bytes around, storing optimizer states or the KV cache, and communicating between GPUs.","很多时候，真正的瓶颈是搬运数据、存储优化器状态或 KV 缓存，以及 GPU 之间的通信。"],[148.73,152.41,2,"Almost every trick today attacks one of these four costs.","今天讲的几乎每一个技巧，都是在对付这四种开销中的某一种。"],[153.66,155.68,3,"Let's begin with the motivation.","我们先从动机讲起。"],[156.03,162.12,3,"The one-line summary is on the slide: models, data and usage are growing much faster than hardware.","一句话总结就在幻灯片上：模型、数据和使用量的增长远远快于硬件。"],[162.47,166.3,3,"If we simply wait for better GPUs, we'll always be behind.","如果我们只是等待更好的 GPU，就会永远落后。"],[166.65,173.1,3,"So efficiency isn't a nice-to-have. It decides who gets to participate in this field at all.","所以效率不是锦上添花，它决定了谁能参与这个领域。"],[173.45,180.78,3,"In this first part, we'll look at why the demand keeps growing, and then build a simple map of the efficiency methods we'll cover.","在第一部分，我们先看为什么需求不断增长，然后为今天要讲的效率方法画一张简单的地图。"],[182.03,188.83,4,"I like to describe today's goal with a Chinese saying: we want the horse to run fast, but we don't want to feed it.","我喜欢用一句中国俗语来形容今天的目标：又要马儿跑，又要马儿不吃草。"],[189.18,194.11,4,"Normally that's impossible, but in deep learning we can get surprisingly close.","通常这是不可能的，但在深度学习里，我们能出人意料地接近这个目标。"],[194.46,199.83,4,"The picture shows Bert from Sesame Street shrinking, which is a nod to compressing BERT.","图里是《芝麻街》里的 Bert 在变小，这是在暗指压缩 BERT 模型。"],[200.18,204.03,4,"The idea is that the small version should still behave like the big one.","意思是，小版本仍然应该表现得像大版本一样。"],[204.38,207.24,4,"Keep this horse in mind, because I'll come back to it.","记住这匹马，因为我后面还会回到它。"],[207.59,217.03,4,"Almost every method today is a different way of getting the same quality, or nearly the same, for much less compute, memory or money.","今天几乎每一种方法，都是用少得多的算力、内存或金钱，换来相同或几乎相同质量的不同途径。"],[218.28,221.29,5,"So why do we need efficiency in the first place?","那么，我们为什么需要效率呢？"],[221.64,224.28,5,"You might think: just buy more GPUs.","你可能会想：多买些 GPU 不就行了。"],[224.63,229.22,5,"Over the next few slides, I'll show you three reasons why that doesn't work.","接下来几页，我会给出三个理由，说明这行不通。"],[229.57,235.64,5,"Scaling laws keep pushing models bigger, and hardware memory grows far more slowly than model size.","规模定律不断推动模型变大，而硬件显存的增长远远慢于模型规模的增长。"],[235.99,242.83,5,"And the cost of using the strongest models is becoming a real issue for people and companies.","而且，使用最强模型的成本，正在成为个人和公司面临的现实问题。"],[244.08,246.83,6,"The first reason is scaling laws.","第一个理由是规模定律。"],[247.18,256.94,6,"Kaplan and colleagues at OpenAI showed in two thousand twenty that the test loss of a language model goes down smoothly as we scale up.","OpenAI 的 Kaplan 等人在二零二零年发现，随着规模扩大，语言模型的测试损失会平滑地下降。"],[257.29,264.43,6,"It looks almost like a straight line on a log-log plot, as you increase model size, dataset size and training compute.","随着模型规模、数据集规模和训练算力的增加，它在双对数坐标图上几乎是一条直线。"],[264.78,269.93,6,"Look at the big plot in the middle: the x-axis is compute on a log scale.","看中间这张大图：横轴是对数刻度的算力。"],[270.28,273.65,6,"Each step to the right is ten times more compute.","每向右走一格，算力就增加十倍。"],[274.0,276.44,6,"Notice the green bracket.","注意这个绿色的大括号。"],[276.79,281.26,6,"Getting just one unit lower in loss costs you orders of magnitude more compute.","损失只降低一个单位，就要多花几个数量级的算力。"],[281.61,287.41,6,"That's the bad news hiding inside the good news: improvement is predictable, but it's expensive.","这就是好消息里藏着的坏消息：提升是可预测的，但代价高昂。"],[287.76,297.63,6,"Also note the remark that architecture details like depth versus width matter much less than sheer scale, at least within reasonable limits.","还要注意这条备注：至少在合理范围内，深度和宽度这类架构细节远不如规模本身重要。"],[297.98,303.62,6,"So the incentive in industry is clear: if you want a better model, scale it up.","所以业界的动力很明确：想要更好的模型，就扩大规模。"],[303.97,307.91,6,"And that's exactly why efficiency becomes urgent.","而这正是效率变得紧迫的原因。"],[308.26,314.96,6,"If quality is bought with compute, then every trick that saves compute is effectively buying you a better model.","如果质量是用算力买来的，那么每一个节省算力的技巧，实际上都在帮你换来更好的模型。"],[315.31,322.7,6,"The Chinchilla paper listed below refines how to split a budget between parameters and data, if you want to read further.","如果想深入阅读，下面列出的 Chinchilla 论文进一步研究了如何在参数和数据之间分配预算。"],[323.95,328.32,7,"Here's the second reason, and I think this plot tells the story very clearly.","这是第二个理由，我觉得这张图把问题讲得非常清楚。"],[328.67,330.43,7,"The red line is model size.","红线是模型规模。"],[330.78,340.88,7,"It goes from the original Transformer at zero point zero five billion parameters in two thousand seventeen, to GPT-3 at one hundred seventy-five billion.","它从二零一七年最初只有零点零五 B、也就是五千万参数的 Transformer，增长到 GPT-3 的一千七百五十亿参数。"],[341.23,345.48,7,"And then to MT-NLG at five hundred thirty billion.","再到 MT-NLG 的五千三百亿参数。"],[345.83,352.2,7,"Note the y-axis is a log scale, so that's growing by roughly ten times every year or so.","注意纵轴是对数刻度，所以模型规模大约每年增长十倍左右。"],[352.55,360.14,7,"The green line is GPU memory, from sixteen gigabytes on a TPUv2 to eighty gigabytes on an A100.","绿线是 GPU 显存，从 TPUv2 的 16GB 到 A100 的 80GB。"],[360.49,361.57,7,"It barely moves.","它几乎没怎么动。"],[361.92,367.33,7,"The black arrow on the right shows the gap, and it's more than an order of magnitude.","右边的黑色箭头显示了这个差距，超过了一个数量级。"],[367.68,373.53,7,"Even just storing the weights of a big model in FP16 doesn't fit on one card anymore.","即使只是用 FP16 存储一个大模型的权重，一张卡也已经放不下了。"],[373.88,378.52,7,"That's why the photo on the right is a rack of servers, not a single GPU.","这就是为什么右边的照片是一整机柜的服务器，而不是一块 GPU。"],[378.87,386.03,7,"Once a model doesn't fit on one device, we have to split it, and then communication between devices becomes a cost too.","一旦模型在一个设备上放不下，我们就必须把它拆分，这时设备之间的通信也成了一项开销。"],[386.38,390.97,7,"Hold on to that thought; it comes back when we discuss distributed training.","记住这一点，我们讲分布式训练时还会回到这里。"],[392.22,396.68,8,"So how do we bridge the gap between the supply and demand of AI computing?","那么，我们如何弥合 AI 算力供给与需求之间的差距？"],[397.03,399.09,8,"The figure shows one classic answer.","这张图给出了一个经典答案。"],[399.44,405.16,8,"Before, we trained a big network and deployed that same big network for inference.","以前，我们训练一个大网络，然后直接把这个大网络部署用于推理。"],[405.51,409.61,8,"After, we insert a step in the middle: model compression.","现在，我们在中间插入一步：模型压缩。"],[409.96,416.75,8,"Pruning, sparsity, quantization and so on turn the big trained network into a small one that is cheap to deploy.","剪枝、稀疏化、量化等方法，把训练好的大网络变成一个部署成本很低的小网络。"],[417.1,425.37,8,"This picture is from the era before LLMs, mostly from Song Han's group at MIT, whose course materials I've borrowed from today.","这张图来自大模型之前的时代，主要出自 MIT 韩松老师的团队，今天我也借用了他们的一些课程材料。"],[425.72,431.55,8,"It's a good starting point, but as we'll see, for LLMs compression is only one piece.","这是一个很好的起点，但我们会看到，对大模型来说，压缩只是其中一部分。"],[431.9,437.36,8,"We also need to make training itself cheaper, and we need to make inference systems smarter.","我们还需要让训练本身更便宜，让推理系统更聪明。"],[438.61,443.03,9,"Let me make the cost question concrete with today's frontier models.","让我用当今的前沿模型把成本问题讲得更具体一些。"],[443.38,450.89,9,"Companies like Anthropic don't publish parameter counts, so treat these numbers as guesses circulating in the community, not facts.","像 Anthropic 这样的公司不公布参数量，所以请把这些数字当作社区里流传的猜测，而不是事实。"],[451.24,457.44,9,"The rough idea is that a mid-tier model like Sonnet might be on the order of a trillion parameters.","大致的想法是，像 Sonnet 这样的中端模型可能有一万亿参数量级。"],[457.79,466.68,9,"The top model, Opus, might be several times that, and a next-generation model like Mythos even larger, perhaps ten trillion.","顶级模型 Opus 可能是它的好几倍，而像 Mythos 这样的下一代模型更大，可能有十万亿参数。"],[467.03,470.16,9,"Whether the exact numbers are right doesn't matter much.","具体数字对不对并不太重要。"],[470.51,478.76,9,"The point is the trend: the most capable models are very large, and every token they generate costs real money in GPU time.","重点在于趋势：最强的模型都非常大，它们生成的每一个 token 都要花费真金白银的 GPU 时间。"],[479.11,484.29,9,"That's why API prices for the top models are much higher than for small ones.","这就是为什么顶级模型的 API 价格远高于小模型。"],[484.64,490.09,9,"And it's why serving efficiency is a core business problem, not just an academic one.","这也是为什么推理服务的效率是一个核心商业问题，而不仅仅是学术问题。"],[491.34,498.13,10,"And here's why people still pay for these expensive models: they make skilled people dramatically more productive.","那人们为什么还愿意为这些昂贵的模型买单？因为它们能让有技能的人生产力大幅提升。"],[498.48,507.27,10,"The salary numbers on this slide have been reported or rumoured for top AI researchers in China and abroad, so don't quote them as precise facts.","这页上的薪资数字，是关于国内外顶尖 AI 研究者的报道或传闻，请不要把它们当作精确事实引用。"],[507.62,513.53,10,"What they show is how much the market values people who can build and use these systems well.","它们说明的是，市场有多么看重能够构建并用好这些系统的人。"],[513.88,519.87,10,"The last line is the one I want you to remember: AI has widened the productivity gap between people.","最后一行是我希望大家记住的：AI 拉大了人与人之间的生产力差距。"],[520.22,524.71,10,"Someone who uses strong models well can now do the work of a small team.","一个善用强大模型的人，现在能完成一个小团队的工作。"],[525.06,529.33,10,"That makes access to cheap, efficient AI a fairness issue too.","这使得能否用上便宜、高效的 AI，也成了一个公平问题。"],[529.68,532.82,10,"If only a few can afford it, the gap grows.","如果只有少数人用得起，差距就会扩大。"],[533.17,538.53,10,"Efficient models help close it, and that's part of why this lecture matters for all of you.","高效的模型有助于缩小这个差距，这也是这节课对你们每个人都很重要的原因之一。"],[539.78,543.18,11,"With the motivation clear, let's build a map of the methods.","动机讲清楚了，我们来画一张方法地图。"],[543.53,551.18,11,"I'll split them into two types. Type one is efficiency within the Transformer: we change the architecture itself.","我把它们分成两类。第一类是 Transformer 内部的效率：我们改变架构本身。"],[551.53,559.4,11,"There are two examples here. The first is sparsity, like Mixture of Experts, shown in the Switch Transformer figure.","这里有两个例子。第一个是稀疏性，比如混合专家模型，如 Switch Transformer 的图所示。"],[559.75,568.2,11,"Instead of one big feed-forward layer, there are several expert FFNs, and a router sends each token to just one of them.","它不再是一个大的前馈层，而是有多个专家 FFN，由一个路由器把每个 token 只发给其中一个。"],[568.55,573.2,11,"You get more parameters, but each token only pays for one expert.","参数变多了，但每个 token 只需要为一个专家付出计算代价。"],[573.55,576.13,11,"The second is efficiency for long contexts.","第二个是长上下文的效率。"],[576.48,583.61,11,"Self-attention costs on the order of N squared times D, where N is the sequence length and D is the hidden size.","自注意力的计算量约为 N 的平方乘以 D，其中 N 是序列长度，D 是隐藏层维度。"],[583.96,588.34,11,"Double the context and the attention cost roughly quadruples.","上下文长度翻倍，注意力的开销大约变成四倍。"],[588.69,593.45,11,"That quadratic term is what sparse and efficient attention try to remove.","这个二次项正是稀疏注意力和高效注意力想要消除的。"],[593.8,595.87,11,"We'll go into both in Part two.","这两点我们都会在第二部分深入讲解。"],[597.12,605.55,12,"Type two is efficiency beyond the Transformer: methods that work on almost any trained network, no matter its architecture.","第二类是 Transformer 之外的效率：这些方法几乎适用于任何训练好的网络，不管它是什么架构。"],[605.9,607.39,12,"Bert shows them nicely.","Bert 把它们展示得很形象。"],[607.74,613.67,12,"Quantization is like lowering the resolution of a picture: we store each weight with fewer bits.","量化就像降低图片的分辨率：我们用更少的比特来存储每个权重。"],[614.02,618.1,12,"So Bert becomes pixelated, but is still clearly Bert.","于是 Bert 变得像素化了，但一眼还能看出是 Bert。"],[618.45,624.93,12,"Pruning removes weight connections that don't matter much, so Bert gets holes in him but keeps his shape.","剪枝去掉那些不太重要的权重连接，于是 Bert 身上出现了很多洞，但轮廓还在。"],[625.28,632.42,12,"Knowledge distillation trains a smaller model to imitate a bigger one, so we get a little Bert who behaves like the big one.","知识蒸馏训练一个小模型去模仿大模型，于是我们得到一个表现像大 Bert 的小 Bert。"],[632.77,637.37,12,"These three are the classic compression toolbox, and they're the topic of Part three.","这三种方法是经典的压缩工具箱，也是第三部分的主题。"],[637.72,646.0,12,"They're complementary, too. In practice, people often combine them, for example distilling a small model and then quantizing it.","它们还是互补的。实践中人们经常把它们组合起来用，比如先蒸馏出一个小模型，再对它进行量化。"],[647.25,652.81,13,"So what changes once we move from BERT-sized models to LLMs?","那么，从 BERT 这种规模的模型转向大模型后，有什么变化呢？"],[653.16,658.35,13,"All the older methods, within and beyond the Transformer, still apply.","以前所有的方法，无论是 Transformer 内部的还是外部的，依然适用。"],[658.7,660.7,13,"But new costs become dominant.","但新的开销开始占据主导。"],[661.05,665.63,13,"Communication costs appear because the model is spread across many GPUs.","因为模型分布在许多 GPU 上，通信开销就出现了。"],[665.98,672.99,13,"Memory saving becomes critical, not just for weights, but for gradients, optimizer states and the KV cache.","节省内存变得至关重要，不只是权重，还有梯度、优化器状态和 KV 缓存。"],[673.34,677.01,13,"Distributed training becomes necessary rather than optional.","分布式训练从可选项变成了必需品。"],[677.36,684.34,13,"And there's a new family of tricks specifically for autoregressive decoding, like speculative decoding.","此外还有一类专门针对自回归解码的新技巧，比如投机解码。"],[684.69,689.5,13,"That's because generating one token at a time is the main inference bottleneck.","这是因为一次只生成一个 token，是推理的主要瓶颈。"],[690.75,696.16,14,"This picture shows why space efficiency is a new story in the LLM era.","这张图说明了为什么在大模型时代，空间效率成了一个新问题。"],[696.51,705.15,14,"On the left is the classic setting: a small model sits comfortably inside one GPU's memory, shown as the red box.","左边是经典的情形：一个小模型舒舒服服地放在一块 GPU 的显存里，也就是这个红框。"],[705.5,707.48,14,"Everything is local and fast.","一切都在本地，速度很快。"],[707.83,715.34,14,"On the right, a large model doesn't fit in one GPU, so we cut it into Part one and Part two on two devices.","右边是一个大模型，一块 GPU 放不下，所以我们把它切成第一部分和第二部分，放在两个设备上。"],[715.69,723.18,14,"Now every forward and backward pass has to send activations or gradients across the blue arrows.","这样每一次前向和反向传播，都要通过蓝色箭头传送激活值或梯度。"],[723.53,729.7,14,"That communication can easily become the bottleneck, even if each GPU is computing quickly.","即使每块 GPU 都算得很快，这种通信也很容易成为瓶颈。"],[730.05,736.0,14,"So in the LLM world, efficiency is no longer only about counting parameters or FLOPs.","所以在大模型的世界里，效率不再只是数参数量或浮点运算量。"],[736.35,741.99,14,"It's about memory per device, and the bytes moving between devices.","它还关乎每个设备的内存，以及设备之间传输的数据量。"],[742.34,748.02,14,"Those are the bytes stored and the communication costs from our big question on the contents slide.","这正是目录页那个大问题里的“存储的数据量”和“通信开销”。"],[749.27,754.84,15,"There's one more cost to think about: what happens when we adapt one big model to many tasks.","还有一种开销值得思考：当我们把一个大模型适配到很多任务上时，会发生什么。"],[755.19,764.8,15,"In the classic BERT recipe, we pre-train once and then fine-tune the whole model for each task, like MNLI, NER or SQuAD.","在经典的 BERT 做法里，我们预训练一次，然后针对每个任务，比如 MNLI、NER 或 SQuAD，微调整个模型。"],[765.15,771.08,15,"So each task has a fully fine-tuned model, a complete copy of every parameter.","所以每个任务都有一个完全微调的模型，也就是所有参数的一份完整拷贝。"],[771.43,776.56,15,"That costs training time, and it costs storage space for every task you add.","这既耗费训练时间，又会让你每增加一个任务就多占一份存储空间。"],[776.91,783.16,15,"So the natural question is the one on the right: can we just fine-tune a few parameters for a new task?","所以自然的问题就是右边这个：对于新任务，我们能不能只微调一小部分参数？"],[783.51,786.59,15,"That idea is parameter-efficient fine-tuning.","这个想法就是参数高效微调。"],[786.94,796.51,15,"It reduces the computational demands of training, and lets us deploy on devices with limited resources, like mobile or edge devices.","它降低了训练的计算需求，也让我们能在资源有限的设备上部署，比如手机或边缘设备。"],[796.86,803.51,15,"It cuts costs, and it tries to maintain or even improve performance on downstream tasks.","它节省成本，同时努力保持甚至提升在下游任务上的表现。"],[803.86,808.07,15,"We'll come back to it in detail with LoRA and adapters in Part four.","我们会在第四部分结合 LoRA 和适配器详细讲解。"]]},{"n":2,"title":"Redundancy and Efficient Attention: Sparse, GQA and MLA","blurb":"A Transformer recap, why trained models are redundant and decomposable, then sparse attention in Longformer and Big Bird and the KV-sharing family from MHA through GQA and MQA to MLA.","file":"lecture11_part2.mp4","poster":"lecture11_part2.jpg","duration":910.2,"first":16,"last":33,"slides":[{"n":16,"title":"2 Efficient Architectures","t":0.8},{"n":17,"title":"Recap: Transformers","t":29.68},{"n":18,"title":"Recap: Transformers - Multi-head Self-Attention (MHSA)","t":78.41},{"n":19,"title":"Recap: Transformers - Feed-Forward Network (FFN)","t":138.37},{"n":20,"title":"Efficient Transformers","t":189.57},{"n":21,"title":"Could we make it efficient and also maintain the performance?","t":255.64},{"n":22,"title":"Motivation: Parameter redundancy existed","t":279.88},{"n":23,"title":"Decomposability","t":335.54},{"n":24,"title":"Self-attention is decomposable","t":384.66},{"n":25,"title":"Feed-forward network is also decomposable","t":436.22},{"n":26,"title":"2.1 Efficient Attention","t":484.69},{"n":27,"title":"Sparse Attention - LongFormer","t":519.66},{"n":28,"title":"Sparse Attention - LongFormer","t":572.27},{"n":29,"title":"Sparse Attention - Big Bird","t":621.76},{"n":30,"title":"Sparse Attention - Lite Transformer","t":674.83},{"n":31,"title":"Sharing KV Heads: MQA and GQA","t":724.81},{"n":32,"title":"Multi-Head Latent Attention (DeepSeek-V2)","t":789.65},{"n":33,"title":"Sharing Keys and Values: MHA → GQA → MQA → MLA","t":850.06}],"sents":[[0.8,6.38,16,"That completes our map of why efficiency matters and what kinds of methods exist.","到这里，我们就画完了这张地图：为什么效率重要，以及有哪些类型的方法。"],[6.73,11.64,16,"Now we start changing the model itself. Part two is about efficient architectures.","现在我们开始改变模型本身。第二部分讲的是高效架构。"],[11.99,19.51,16,"In a Transformer block, attention is quadratic in sequence length, and the feed-forward network holds most of the parameters.","在一个 Transformer 块中，注意力的开销随序列长度呈二次增长，而前馈网络拥有大部分参数。"],[19.86,23.72,16,"So we'll ask: can each of them do less work per token?","所以我们要问：它们能不能在每个 token 上少做一些工作？"],[24.07,28.28,16,"First efficient attention, then Mixture of Experts.","先讲高效注意力，再讲混合专家模型。"],[29.53,36.43,17,"Before we change the architecture, let's quickly remind ourselves what's inside, since you saw this back in Lecture four.","在改变架构之前，我们先快速回顾一下它的内部结构，大家在第四讲已经见过了。"],[36.78,43.64,17,"A Transformer block has two main sub-layers: multi-head self-attention, and a position-wise feed-forward network.","一个 Transformer 块有两个主要子层：多头自注意力，和逐位置的前馈网络。"],[43.99,48.08,17,"Each is wrapped in a residual connection and layer normalization.","每个子层都包裹在残差连接和层归一化之中。"],[48.43,55.35,17,"The decoder also has cross-attention to the encoder, and it generates outputs one token at a time, autoregressively.","解码器还有对编码器的交叉注意力，并且以自回归的方式一次生成一个 token。"],[55.7,58.25,17,"For efficiency, keep two facts in mind.","从效率的角度，请记住两个事实。"],[58.6,64.36,17,"Attention is where tokens talk to each other, and its cost grows with the square of the length.","注意力是 token 之间相互交流的地方，它的开销随长度的平方增长。"],[64.71,71.35,17,"The feed-forward network processes each token independently, but it's where most of the parameters live.","前馈网络独立处理每个 token，但大部分参数都在这里。"],[71.7,77.01,17,"Modern LLMs are decoder-only, but these two sub-layers are the same.","现代大模型都是仅解码器结构，但这两个子层是一样的。"],[78.26,81.79,18,"Here is multi-head self-attention in more detail.","这是多头自注意力的更多细节。"],[82.14,90.0,18,"We project the queries, keys and values with h different learned linear maps, the red boxes.","我们用 h 组不同的、可学习的线性映射来投影查询、键和值，也就是红色的框。"],[90.35,93.9,18,"Each head runs scaled dot-product attention in parallel.","每个头并行地执行缩放点积注意力。"],[94.25,100.25,18,"We concatenate the results, and a final linear layer, the blue box, mixes them back together.","我们把结果拼接起来，再由最后一个线性层，也就是蓝色的框，把它们重新混合。"],[100.6,109.34,18,"On the right is the core formula: softmax of Q times K transpose, divided by the square root of d k, times V.","右边是核心公式：Q 乘以 K 的转置，除以 d k 的平方根，取 softmax，再乘以 V。"],[109.69,117.46,18,"The Q K-transpose product compares every token with every other token, which gives an N by N matrix.","Q 乘 K 转置这一步，把每个 token 和其他所有 token 做比较，得到一个 N 乘 N 的矩阵。"],[117.81,121.5,18,"That matrix is the source of the quadratic cost.","这个矩阵就是二次开销的来源。"],[121.85,129.13,18,"Later today, when we get to FlashAttention, it's exactly this N by N matrix we'll try never to write to memory.","今天稍后讲到 FlashAttention 时，我们要努力做到的，正是永远不把这个 N 乘 N 的矩阵写入显存。"],[129.48,136.97,18,"Notice too that each head works independently until the concatenation. That will matter in a few slides.","还要注意，每个头在拼接之前都是独立工作的。这一点在后面几页会很重要。"],[138.22,141.21,19,"The other sub-layer is the feed-forward network.","另一个子层是前馈网络。"],[141.56,149.06,19,"It's applied to each position separately and identically: two linear layers with a non-linearity in between.","它独立且相同地作用于每个位置：两个线性层，中间夹一个非线性激活。"],[149.41,155.95,19,"The hidden layer in the middle is usually about four times wider than the model dimension, an inverted bottleneck.","中间的隐藏层通常比模型维度宽四倍左右，这叫倒瓶颈结构。"],[156.3,157.81,19,"Look at the table on the right.","看右边这张表。"],[158.16,168.33,19,"As models go from one hundred twenty-five million to one hundred seventy-five billion parameters, d model grows from seven hundred sixty-eight to twelve thousand two hundred eighty-eight.","随着模型从一亿两千五百万参数增长到一千七百五十亿参数，d model 从 768 增长到 12288。"],[168.68,173.55,19,"The FFN has two matrices of size d model by four d model.","FFN 有两个大小为 d model 乘四倍 d model 的矩阵。"],[173.9,178.99,19,"So it ends up holding roughly two thirds of the parameters in each block.","所以它最终占据了每个块里大约三分之二的参数。"],[179.34,188.17,19,"So if we want to cut parameters or compute per token, the FFN is the obvious target, and that's exactly what Mixture of Experts does.","所以如果我们想减少每个 token 的参数量或计算量，FFN 就是显而易见的目标，而这正是混合专家模型要做的。"],[189.42,198.47,20,"This Venn diagram, from the survey by Tay and colleagues, gives you a sense of how many people have tried to make Transformers efficient.","这张维恩图来自 Tay 等人的综述，能让你感受到有多少人尝试过让 Transformer 变得更高效。"],[198.82,202.06,20,"Don't try to remember every name. Just look at the families.","不用记住每个名字，只看这些大类就好。"],[202.41,211.1,20,"Fixed or random patterns, in green, restrict which tokens attend to which, like Longformer and Big Bird.","绿色的固定或随机模式，限制了哪些 token 可以关注哪些 token，比如 Longformer 和 Big Bird。"],[211.45,218.86,20,"Low-rank and kernel methods, in blue, approximate the attention matrix, like Linformer and Performer.","蓝色的低秩和核方法，用来近似注意力矩阵，比如 Linformer 和 Performer。"],[219.21,224.66,20,"Recurrence, in teal, carries memory across segments, like Transformer-XL.","青色的循环机制，在片段之间传递记忆，比如 Transformer-XL。"],[225.01,231.9,20,"Learnable patterns, in yellow, cluster tokens so similar ones attend to each other, like Reformer.","黄色的可学习模式，把 token 聚类，让相似的 token 相互关注，比如 Reformer。"],[232.25,240.37,20,"And sparse models, in purple, are mostly Mixture-of-Experts models like Switch Transformer and GLaM.","紫色的稀疏模型主要是混合专家模型，比如 Switch Transformer 和 GLaM。"],[240.72,246.29,20,"Many of these ideas came before LLMs, and only a few survived at scale.","这些想法很多都出现在大模型之前，只有少数在大规模下存活了下来。"],[246.64,254.24,20,"In this part we'll focus on the ones that did: sparse attention patterns, shared key-value heads and Mixture of Experts.","在这一部分，我们重点讲那些存活下来的：稀疏注意力模式、共享键值头和混合专家模型。"],[255.49,259.13,21,"Here's our horse again. Can it run fast without being fed?","我们的马又回来了。它能不吃草还跑得快吗？"],[259.48,264.18,21,"Put more precisely: can we cut the computation and still keep the performance?","更准确地说：我们能否减少计算量，同时保持性能？"],[264.53,269.35,21,"That only works if the big model is doing some work it doesn't really need to do.","只有当大模型在做一些其实不必做的工作时，这才行得通。"],[269.7,272.27,21,"In other words, there has to be redundancy.","换句话说，必须存在冗余。"],[272.62,278.48,21,"The next few slides argue that there is, both in the weights themselves and in the structure of the Transformer.","接下来几页将论证冗余确实存在，既存在于权重本身，也存在于 Transformer 的结构中。"],[279.73,288.28,22,"This figure is from one of my own papers at ICLR two thousand twenty-two, on extreme compression of pre-trained language models.","这张图来自我自己在 ICLR 2022 发表的一篇论文，研究的是预训练语言模型的极限压缩。"],[288.63,296.75,22,"We took each weight matrix in BERT-base, which is seven hundred sixty-eight by seven hundred sixty-eight, and ran PCA on it.","我们取出 BERT-base 中的每个权重矩阵，大小是 768 乘 768，对它做主成分分析。"],[297.1,301.39,22,"The y-axis is how much variance is captured by the top components.","纵轴是前若干个主成分捕获的方差比例。"],[301.74,307.97,22,"Look at the curve. You don't need all seven hundred sixty-eight components to capture most of the information.","看这条曲线。要捕获大部分信息，并不需要全部 768 个主成分。"],[308.32,312.0,22,"A few hundred already get you around ninety percent.","几百个主成分就已经能达到大约百分之九十。"],[312.35,316.34,22,"The right panel pairs matrices together and shows the same pattern.","右图把矩阵两两配对，也呈现出同样的规律。"],[316.69,322.98,22,"That tells us the weights live, approximately, in a lower-dimensional space than their size suggests.","这告诉我们，权重近似地处在一个比其尺寸所显示的更低维的空间里。"],[323.33,327.0,22,"That's the empirical basis for a lot of today's methods.","这是今天很多方法的经验基础。"],[327.35,334.14,22,"Low-rank factorization, LoRA, MLA and pruning all quietly rely on this kind of redundancy.","低秩分解、LoRA、MLA 和剪枝，都在悄悄地依赖这种冗余。"],[335.39,339.89,23,"There's also a structural reason for redundancy, which I call decomposability.","冗余还有一个结构上的原因，我称之为可分解性。"],[340.24,348.71,23,"A module f is decomposable if it's made of sub-components g one to g H that can be computed independently.","如果一个模块 f 由可以独立计算的子组件 g1 到 gH 组成，那么它就是可分解的。"],[349.06,354.58,23,"They are then combined by some cheap operation delta, like a sum or a concatenation.","然后再通过某个廉价的操作 delta 把它们组合起来，比如求和或拼接。"],[354.93,357.39,23,"The picture of the lungs is my analogy.","这张肺的图是我打的一个比方。"],[357.74,362.01,23,"You have two lungs that work in parallel, and you can actually live with one.","你有两个并行工作的肺，而其实只有一个也能活。"],[362.36,369.6,23,"Having parallel, independent parts gives you backup, and backup means some of the capacity is redundant.","拥有并行且独立的部分就有了备份，而备份意味着部分能力是冗余的。"],[369.95,378.12,23,"When a network is built from many parallel parts, it's likely that some of them can be removed or shared without losing much.","当一个网络由许多并行部分构成时，其中一些很可能可以被删掉或共享，而不会损失太多。"],[378.47,383.26,23,"Let's check that the two parts of a Transformer block are both decomposable.","我们来验证一下，Transformer 块的这两个部分都是可分解的。"],[384.51,387.4,24,"Self-attention is clearly decomposable.","自注意力显然是可分解的。"],[387.75,392.71,24,"Each head h has its own query, key, value and output projections.","每个头 h 都有自己的查询、键、值和输出投影。"],[393.06,397.81,24,"The formula shows that head h can be computed entirely on its own.","公式表明，头 h 完全可以独立计算。"],[398.16,405.32,24,"It's a softmax over X W Q times W K transposed times X transposed, scaled by one over root d.","它是对 X 乘 W Q、乘 W K 转置、再乘 X 转置，并乘以根号 d 分之一的结果做 softmax。"],[405.67,410.33,24,"That is then multiplied by X W V and the output projection.","然后再乘以 X W V 和输出投影。"],[410.68,413.06,24,"The full layer is just the sum of all heads.","整个层就是所有头的和。"],[413.41,418.73,24,"Because the heads don't interact until that final sum, many of them end up redundant.","因为各个头直到最后求和之前都没有交互，所以其中很多最终是冗余的。"],[419.08,427.04,24,"In fact, well-known studies showed you can remove a large fraction of attention heads in a trained model with only a small drop in quality.","事实上，一些著名的研究表明，在训练好的模型里去掉很大一部分注意力头，质量只会略有下降。"],[427.39,434.82,24,"That's one motivation for head pruning, and also for sharing keys and values across heads, which we'll see shortly with GQA and MQA.","这是剪枝注意力头的动机之一，也是跨头共享键和值的动机，我们很快会在 GQA 和 MQA 中看到。"],[436.07,440.17,25,"Perhaps more surprising: the feed-forward network is decomposable too.","也许更令人意外的是：前馈网络也是可分解的。"],[440.52,448.52,25,"Look at the formula. The hidden layer has four D neurons, and we can write the FFN as a sum over those neurons.","看这个公式。隐藏层有 4D 个神经元，我们可以把 FFN 写成对这些神经元的求和。"],[448.87,458.09,25,"Each neuron h takes the input, applies its own column of W in and a GeLU, then writes out along its own row of W out.","每个神经元 h 接收输入，用它自己那一列 W in 并经过 GeLU，然后沿着它自己那一行 W out 输出。"],[458.44,463.6,25,"So each hidden neuron is like a tiny head, and the output is just their sum.","所以每个隐藏神经元就像一个小小的头，输出就是它们的和。"],[463.95,465.28,25,"This view is powerful.","这个视角非常有力。"],[465.63,471.35,25,"It means we can group neurons into blocks and treat each block as an expert.","它意味着我们可以把神经元分组成块，把每一块当作一个专家。"],[471.7,476.51,25,"If we only activate the blocks that matter for a given token, we save compute.","如果对每个 token 只激活与之相关的块，我们就能节省计算。"],[476.86,483.29,25,"That's exactly the intuition behind Mixture of Experts, which we'll get to after we look at attention.","这正是混合专家模型背后的直觉，我们讲完注意力之后就会讲到它。"],[484.54,491.27,26,"We've established that there's redundancy in both attention and the FFN. Let's start with attention.","我们已经确认，注意力和 FFN 中都存在冗余。先从注意力开始。"],[491.62,498.38,26,"Full attention compares every token with every other one, so the cost is of order N squared.","完整的注意力要把每个 token 与其他所有 token 比较，所以开销是 N 平方量级。"],[498.73,504.03,26,"For a one-hundred-thousand-token context, that's ten billion pairs, per head, per layer.","对于十万个 token 的上下文，这意味着每一层的每一个头都要计算一百亿对。"],[504.38,506.98,26,"This sub-section asks two questions.","这一小节要回答两个问题。"],[507.33,512.17,26,"Can each token attend to fewer tokens? That's sparse attention.","每个 token 能不能只关注更少的 token？这就是稀疏注意力。"],[512.52,518.26,26,"And can heads share their keys and values? That's GQA, MQA and MLA.","多个头能不能共享它们的键和值？这就是 GQA、MQA 和 MLA。"],[519.51,525.94,27,"Longformer, from Beltagy and colleagues at AI2, is a clean example of sparse attention.","Longformer 出自 AI2 的 Beltagy 等人，是稀疏注意力的一个简洁例子。"],[526.29,531.7,27,"Look at the four matrices. Panel a is full attention: every cell is filled, N squared.","看这四个矩阵。图 a 是完整注意力：每个格子都被填满，N 平方。"],[532.05,539.18,27,"Panel b is a sliding window: each token only looks at W neighbours around it, like a convolution in a CNN.","图 b 是滑动窗口：每个 token 只看它周围的 W 个邻居，就像 CNN 里的卷积。"],[539.53,543.96,27,"The cost drops from N squared to N times W, which is linear in length.","开销从 N 平方降到 N 乘以 W，与长度成线性关系。"],[544.31,551.38,27,"Panel c is a dilated sliding window, with gaps between attended positions, just like dilated convolutions.","图 c 是空洞滑动窗口，被关注的位置之间留有间隔，就像空洞卷积一样。"],[551.73,558.79,27,"With the same number of attended positions you see further, so the receptive field grows from W to W times D.","在关注位置数量相同的情况下，你能看得更远，感受野从 W 扩大到 W 乘以 D。"],[559.14,566.12,27,"And because we stack many layers, information can still travel across the whole document, a few hops at a time.","而且因为我们堆叠了很多层，信息仍然可以一跳一跳地传遍整篇文档。"],[566.47,570.87,27,"The faded panel d is the last ingredient, and that's on the next slide.","淡化的图 d 是最后一个组成部分，我们下一页来看。"],[572.12,576.93,28,"Local windows alone have a weakness: some tokens really need to see everything.","仅靠局部窗口有一个弱点：有些 token 确实需要看到全部内容。"],[577.28,584.3,28,"So Longformer adds global attention on a few pre-selected positions, shown as the full rows and columns in panel d.","所以 Longformer 在少数预先选定的位置上加了全局注意力，就是图 d 中整行整列的部分。"],[584.65,587.18,28,"Which positions? It depends on the task.","选哪些位置？这取决于任务。"],[587.53,592.96,28,"For classification, it's the CLS token, which needs to summarize the whole sequence.","对于分类任务，是 CLS 这个特殊 token，它需要概括整个序列。"],[593.31,600.25,28,"For question answering, it's the question tokens, so the model can compare the question against every part of the document.","对于问答任务，是问题中的所有 token，这样模型就能把问题与文档的每个部分进行比较。"],[600.6,607.13,28,"Global attention is symmetric: a global token attends to everyone, and everyone attends to it.","全局注意力是对称的：全局 token 关注所有 token，所有 token 也都关注它。"],[607.48,612.4,28,"Because there are only a handful of global tokens, the cost stays roughly linear.","因为全局 token 只有寥寥几个，开销仍然大致是线性的。"],[612.75,620.36,28,"The lesson is general: a sparse pattern plus a few hub tokens can approximate full attention surprisingly well.","这个经验是通用的：稀疏模式加上几个枢纽 token，就能出奇好地逼近完整注意力。"],[621.61,627.4,29,"Big Bird, from Google, takes the same idea one step further. It combines three patterns.","Google 的 Big Bird 把这个思路又往前推进了一步。它结合了三种模式。"],[627.75,633.28,29,"Random attention, in orange: each query also attends to r randomly chosen keys.","橙色的随机注意力：每个查询还会关注 r 个随机选出的键。"],[633.63,636.86,29,"Window attention, in blue, as in Longformer.","蓝色的窗口注意力，和 Longformer 一样。"],[637.21,641.36,29,"And global attention, in green, for a few special tokens.","以及绿色的全局注意力，用于少数特殊 token。"],[641.71,644.28,29,"Panel d is the union of all three.","图 d 是这三者的并集。"],[644.63,647.84,29,"Why add randomness? Think of a social network.","为什么要加入随机性？想想社交网络。"],[648.19,651.77,29,"If everyone only knows their neighbours, news travels slowly.","如果每个人只认识自己的邻居，消息就传得很慢。"],[652.12,658.22,29,"Add a few random long-distance friendships, and suddenly any two people are only a few steps apart.","加上几段随机的远距离友谊，任意两个人之间突然就只隔几步了。"],[658.57,665.47,29,"Random edges make the attention graph mix quickly, so information flows between any pair of tokens in a few layers.","随机边让注意力图快速混合，于是信息在几层之内就能在任意两个 token 之间流动。"],[665.82,673.43,29,"The Big Bird paper actually showed this kind of sparse attention keeps important theoretical properties of full attention.","Big Bird 论文实际上证明了，这种稀疏注意力保留了完整注意力的重要理论性质。"],[674.68,678.97,30,"Lite Transformer, from Song Han's group, makes a nice observation.","韩松老师团队的 Lite Transformer 有一个很好的观察。"],[679.32,685.97,30,"Look at the left heat map: in an ordinary Transformer, much of the attention is concentrated near the diagonal.","看左边的热力图：在普通的 Transformer 里，大部分注意力集中在对角线附近。"],[686.32,692.47,30,"So attention spends a lot of effort on local patterns, which a convolution can capture much more cheaply.","所以注意力在局部模式上花了很多力气，而卷积能以低得多的代价捕捉这些模式。"],[692.82,697.89,30,"Their solution is Long-Short Range Attention. They split the channels into two branches.","他们的解决方案是长短程注意力，把通道分成两个分支。"],[698.24,704.11,30,"One branch is a convolution, the local extractor, handling nearby words.","一个分支是卷积，也就是局部提取器，负责处理邻近的词。"],[704.46,710.8,30,"The other branch is attention, the global extractor, now free to focus on long-range relationships.","另一个分支是注意力，也就是全局提取器，现在可以专注于长距离关系。"],[711.15,715.14,30,"You can see that in the middle heat map, which is much more spread out.","从中间的热力图可以看到这一点，它的分布要分散得多。"],[715.49,719.16,30,"The general principle: use the cheapest tool that can do each job.","通用原则是：每项工作都用能胜任的最便宜的工具。"],[719.51,723.41,30,"Don't waste expensive attention on what a convolution can do.","不要把昂贵的注意力浪费在卷积就能做好的事情上。"],[724.66,728.15,31,"Sparse attention reduces how many tokens we look at.","稀疏注意力减少的是我们要看的 token 数量。"],[728.5,735.45,31,"A different idea, and the one that won in today's LLMs, is to reduce how much we store per token.","另一个思路，也是在当今大模型中胜出的思路，是减少每个 token 需要存储的内容。"],[735.8,743.12,31,"This matters because during generation we keep the keys and values of every past token in memory.","这很重要，因为在生成过程中，我们要把之前每个 token 的键和值都保存在显存里。"],[743.47,747.29,31,"That's the KV cache, which we'll study in detail in Part five.","这就是 KV 缓存，我们会在第五部分详细学习。"],[747.64,753.82,31,"In standard multi-head attention, on the left, every query head has its own key and value head.","在左边的标准多头注意力中，每个查询头都有自己的键头和值头。"],[754.17,761.98,31,"Multi-query attention, on the right, proposed by Noam Shazeer, lets all query heads share a single key and value head.","右边的多查询注意力由 Noam Shazeer 提出，让所有查询头共享同一个键头和值头。"],[762.33,766.88,31,"That shrinks the KV cache a lot, but can hurt quality.","这让 KV 缓存大幅缩小，但可能损害质量。"],[767.23,771.06,31,"Grouped-query attention, in the middle, is the compromise.","中间的分组查询注意力是一个折中方案。"],[771.41,776.66,31,"Query heads are split into groups, and each group shares one key-value head.","查询头被分成若干组，每组共享一个键值头。"],[777.01,782.65,31,"GQA has become the default in many open models, like Llama 2 and 3, and Qwen.","GQA 已经成为许多开源模型的默认选择，比如 Llama 2、Llama 3 和 Qwen。"],[783.0,788.25,31,"That's because it gets most of MQA's savings with almost no quality loss.","因为它获得了 MQA 的大部分节省，而质量几乎没有损失。"],[789.5,795.75,32,"DeepSeek-V2 went a step further with Multi-head Latent Attention, or MLA.","DeepSeek-V2 更进一步，提出了多头潜在注意力，简称 MLA。"],[796.1,801.3,32,"Compare the four panels. The hatched boxes are what's cached during inference.","比较这四个面板。带斜线的方框就是推理时被缓存的内容。"],[801.65,808.43,32,"MHA caches full keys and values for every head. GQA and MQA cache fewer heads.","MHA 为每个头缓存完整的键和值。GQA 和 MQA 缓存的头更少。"],[808.78,813.96,32,"MLA caches something different: one small compressed latent vector per token.","MLA 缓存的东西不同：每个 token 只缓存一个小的压缩潜在向量。"],[814.31,820.77,32,"At attention time, that latent is projected back up into full keys and values for every head.","在计算注意力时，这个潜在向量会被投影回每个头的完整键和值。"],[821.12,828.32,32,"So the model still has many distinct heads, which keeps its expressiveness close to MHA, but the memory footprint is tiny.","所以模型仍然有很多不同的头，表达能力接近 MHA，但内存占用非常小。"],[828.67,834.63,32,"This is a direct application of the low-rank idea we saw a few slides ago with PCA.","这直接应用了我们前几页用 PCA 看到的低秩思想。"],[834.98,839.35,32,"Keys and values are redundant, so store a compressed version.","键和值是冗余的，所以只存一个压缩版本。"],[839.7,848.66,32,"DeepSeek reported that MLA actually performed better than MHA in their experiments, while using much less KV cache.","DeepSeek 报告说，在他们的实验中，MLA 的效果实际上比 MHA 更好，同时 KV 缓存用量少得多。"],[849.91,855.28,33,"This slide puts the whole family side by side, with eight query heads as an example.","这一页把整个家族并排放在一起，以八个查询头为例。"],[855.63,861.38,33,"In MHA, each token stores sixteen vectors: eight keys and eight values.","在 MHA 中，每个 token 存储十六个向量：八个键和八个值。"],[861.73,867.08,33,"GQA with two key-value heads stores four vectors, so it's four times smaller.","有两个键值头的 GQA 存储四个向量，所以小了四倍。"],[867.43,872.84,33,"MQA stores just two, so eight times smaller, at some cost in quality.","MQA 只存两个，所以小了八倍，但质量会有一些损失。"],[873.19,878.9,33,"MLA stores one small latent and reconstructs keys and values on the fly.","MLA 只存储一个小的潜在向量，并在运行时即时重建键和值。"],[879.25,882.93,33,"It aims for roughly GQA's cost with MHA's quality.","它的目标是大约 GQA 的成本，加上 MHA 的质量。"],[883.28,886.48,33,"The red sentence at the bottom is the one to remember.","底部的红色句子是需要记住的。"],[886.83,891.21,33,"Decoding speed is bound by how fast we can read the KV cache from memory.","解码速度受限于我们从显存中读取 KV 缓存的速度。"],[891.56,898.53,33,"Fewer KV bytes per token means faster decoding, and room for longer contexts or bigger batches.","每个 token 的 KV 字节越少，解码就越快，也能腾出空间支持更长的上下文或更大的批次。"],[898.88,901.39,33,"That wraps up efficient attention.","高效注意力就讲到这里。"],[901.74,908.33,33,"We've made attention cheaper; now let's turn to the other half of the block, the FFN, where most of the parameters live.","我们已经让注意力更便宜了；现在转向块的另一半，也就是大部分参数所在的 FFN。"]]},{"n":3,"title":"Mixture of Experts: Routing, Experts and DeepSeekMoE","blurb":"How each token visits only a few experts: routers, top-k and hash routing, fine-grained and shared experts, auxiliary losses, DeepSeekMoE and DeepSeek-V2, and sparse upcycling.","file":"lecture11_part3.mp4","poster":"lecture11_part3.jpg","duration":887.0,"first":34,"last":49,"slides":[{"n":34,"title":"2.2 Mixture of Experts","t":0.8},{"n":35,"title":"Mixture of Experts","t":34.11},{"n":36,"title":"Mixture of Experts: Each Token Visits Only a Few Experts","t":78.39},{"n":37,"title":"MoE in Transformer","t":145.38},{"n":38,"title":"Routing Algorithms","t":195.95},{"n":39,"title":"An Example of Hash Routing","t":248.82},{"n":40,"title":"Random hash also works","t":290.3},{"n":41,"title":"MoE Models","t":342.75},{"n":42,"title":"MoE Design Choices","t":402.02},{"n":43,"title":"Fine-grained and Shared Experts","t":455.04},{"n":44,"title":"MoE Experts Design","t":519.67},{"n":45,"title":"Auxiliary Loss","t":580.15},{"n":46,"title":"Training MoE - Deepseek (example)","t":650.12},{"n":47,"title":"Training MoE - Deepseek (example)","t":692.42},{"n":48,"title":"Training MoE - Deepseek (example)","t":753.23},{"n":49,"title":"Sparse Upcycling - Qwen-MoE","t":815.26}],"sents":[[0.8,8.03,34,"We've just seen how to make attention cheaper, by attending to fewer tokens or storing fewer keys and values.","我们刚刚看到了如何让注意力更便宜：关注更少的 token，或存储更少的键和值。"],[8.38,13.03,34,"Now we turn to the feed-forward network, which holds most of the parameters.","现在我们转向前馈网络，它拥有大部分参数。"],[13.38,17.64,34,"Remember that the FFN is decomposable into many small pieces.","还记得吗，FFN 可以分解成许多小块。"],[17.99,24.84,34,"Mixture of Experts uses that: we keep many expert FFNs, but each token only visits a few of them.","混合专家模型正是利用了这一点：我们保留很多专家 FFN，但每个 token 只访问其中少数几个。"],[25.19,32.71,34,"The question for this sub-section is how to get the capacity of a huge model at the compute cost of a small one.","这一小节的问题是：如何用小模型的计算成本，获得超大模型的容量。"],[33.96,40.29,35,"Mixture of Experts is actually an old idea, going back to the early nineteen nineties.","混合专家其实是一个老想法，可以追溯到二十世纪九十年代初。"],[40.64,47.76,35,"The setup is simple. You have k expert networks, and a gating network that looks at the input x.","设置很简单。你有 k 个专家网络，还有一个门控网络来查看输入 x。"],[48.11,51.47,35,"The gate outputs weights g one to g k.","门控网络输出权重 g1 到 gk。"],[51.82,55.9,35,"The final output y is the weighted combination of the experts' outputs.","最终输出 y 是各个专家输出的加权组合。"],[56.25,62.8,35,"In the classic version, all experts run and the gate just mixes them. That doesn't save any compute.","在经典版本中，所有专家都要运行，门控只是把它们混合起来。这并不节省任何计算。"],[63.15,69.43,35,"The modern trick, which makes MoE an efficiency method, is to make the gate sparse.","让 MoE 成为一种效率方法的现代技巧，是让门控变得稀疏。"],[69.78,74.73,35,"We keep only the top one or two experts per input, and skip the rest entirely.","对每个输入只保留排名前一或前二的专家，其余的完全跳过。"],[75.08,76.99,35,"That's what the next slide shows.","这就是下一页要展示的内容。"],[78.24,80.27,36,"The modern version fits in one picture.","现代版本用一张图就能说清楚。"],[80.62,87.17,36,"We have three tokens, The, cat and sat, and eight experts, each a normal FFN.","我们有三个 token：The、cat 和 sat，还有八个专家，每个都是普通的 FFN。"],[87.52,95.71,36,"A router, which is just a linear layer followed by a softmax, scores all eight experts for each token and keeps the top two.","路由器就是一个线性层加一个 softmax，它为每个 token 给八个专家打分，并保留前两名。"],[96.06,103.28,36,"Follow the red boxes. The goes to expert two with weight zero point seven, and expert seven with zero point three.","跟着红色方框看。The 被送到专家 2，权重 0.7，以及专家 7，权重 0.3。"],[103.63,109.82,36,"Cat goes to experts four and five. Sat goes to experts one and seven.","cat 去了专家 4 和专家 5。sat 去了专家 1 和专家 7。"],[110.17,113.84,36,"The output is the weighted sum of just those two experts.","输出就是这两个专家的加权和。"],[114.19,118.21,36,"Experts three, six and eight do nothing for this batch.","专家 3、6 和 8 在这一批中什么都不做。"],[118.56,123.67,36,"So we have the capacity of eight experts, but the compute of two.","所以我们拥有八个专家的容量，却只用两个专家的计算量。"],[124.02,132.93,36,"At scale this is dramatic: DeepSeek-V3 has six hundred seventy-one billion parameters, but only thirty-seven billion are active for each token.","在大规模下效果非常惊人：DeepSeek-V3 有六千七百一十亿参数，但每个 token 只激活三百七十亿。"],[133.28,139.32,36,"One catch: if the router learns to send everything to one favourite expert, the others never train.","有一个问题：如果路由器学会把所有 token 都送给一个最喜欢的专家，其他专家就永远得不到训练。"],[139.67,143.98,36,"That's why we need a load-balancing loss or bias, which we'll come back to.","这就是为什么我们需要负载均衡损失或偏置，我们后面会再讲到。"],[145.23,152.13,37,"This is how MoE sits inside a Transformer, from the Switch Transformer paper by Fedus, Zoph and Shazeer.","这是 MoE 在 Transformer 中的位置，来自 Fedus、Zoph 和 Shazeer 的 Switch Transformer 论文。"],[152.48,154.11,37,"Attention stays the same.","注意力保持不变。"],[154.46,160.69,37,"Only the FFN is replaced by a switching FFN layer, with several experts and a router.","只有 FFN 被替换成了一个切换式 FFN 层，包含多个专家和一个路由器。"],[161.04,164.16,37,"Look at the two tokens, More and Parameters.","看这两个 token：More 和 Parameters。"],[164.51,166.72,37,"Each one has its own router decision.","每个 token 都有自己的路由决策。"],[167.07,175.08,37,"More goes to FFN two with probability zero point six five, and Parameters goes to FFN one with probability zero point eight.","More 以 0.65 的概率被送到 FFN 2，Parameters 以 0.8 的概率被送到 FFN 1。"],[175.43,178.12,37,"That's what token-specific routing means.","这就是“按 token 路由”的含义。"],[178.47,183.19,37,"Different tokens in the same sentence can use completely different experts.","同一个句子里的不同 token，可以使用完全不同的专家。"],[183.54,188.73,37,"Switch Transformer used top-one routing, sending each token to a single expert.","Switch Transformer 使用 top-1 路由，把每个 token 只送给一个专家。"],[189.08,194.55,37,"That made the system simpler, and showed you can scale to over a trillion parameters this way.","这让系统更简单，也证明了用这种方式可以扩展到超过一万亿参数。"],[195.8,201.82,38,"How many experts should each token visit? Compare top-one and top-two routing side by side.","每个 token 应该访问几个专家？我们把 top-1 和 top-2 路由并排比较一下。"],[202.17,208.68,38,"On the left, each token goes to exactly one expert: The to FFN two, Dog to FFN one.","左边，每个 token 只去一个专家：The 去 FFN 2，Dog 去 FFN 1。"],[209.03,217.9,38,"On the right, each token goes to two experts, and their outputs are added with the router weights, like zero point six five and zero point three.","右边，每个 token 去两个专家，它们的输出按路由权重相加，比如 0.65 和 0.3。"],[218.25,223.8,38,"The trade-off is straightforward. Top-one is cheapest in compute and communication.","其中的权衡很直接。top-1 在计算和通信上最便宜。"],[224.15,229.11,38,"Top-two, or top-k in general, gives each token a richer combination.","top-2，或者一般的 top-k，给每个 token 提供了更丰富的组合。"],[229.46,234.42,38,"It also gives a smoother training signal for the router, since it can compare experts.","它还给路由器提供了更平滑的训练信号，因为路由器可以比较不同的专家。"],[234.77,240.5,38,"Many recent models use more, smaller experts with larger k, as we'll see with DeepSeek.","很多新模型使用更多、更小的专家，并配合更大的 k，我们在 DeepSeek 中会看到。"],[240.85,247.42,38,"You might wonder: does the router even need to be learned? The next slide tests something surprisingly simple.","你可能会问：路由器真的需要学习吗？下一页测试了一个出奇简单的方案。"],[248.67,257.03,39,"Hash routing, from Roller and colleagues at Facebook, replaces the learned router with a fixed hash function on the token ID.","Facebook 的 Roller 等人提出的哈希路由，用一个基于 token ID 的固定哈希函数取代了可学习的路由器。"],[257.38,265.91,39,"In the figure, the word taco is hashed to the number three, so it always goes to FFN three, no matter the context.","图中，单词 taco 被哈希成数字 3，所以无论上下文如何，它总是被送到 FFN 3。"],[266.26,273.88,39,"There's no router to train, and no load imbalance to fight, because a good hash spreads tokens evenly by design.","不需要训练路由器，也不需要对付负载不均衡，因为好的哈希本身就会把 token 均匀分散。"],[274.23,276.13,39,"This sounds almost too simple.","这听起来简单得有点过分。"],[276.48,282.73,39,"The point of the experiment is to ask how much of MoE's benefit comes from clever routing.","这个实验的目的是问：MoE 的收益有多少来自聪明的路由？"],[283.08,288.9,39,"And how much comes just from having more parameters that are used sparsely.","又有多少仅仅来自拥有更多被稀疏使用的参数？"],[290.15,296.95,40,"And here's the answer, on a Reddit language modeling task. Lower perplexity is better.","答案就在这里，这是一个 Reddit 语言建模任务。困惑度越低越好。"],[297.3,300.92,40,"The baseline dense Transformer gets about twenty-five.","基线的稠密 Transformer 大约是 25。"],[301.27,309.08,40,"Hash layers with balanced, or even fixed random assignment, get about twenty-three point two, clearly better.","使用均衡分配，甚至固定随机分配的哈希层，大约是 23.2，明显更好。"],[309.43,317.31,40,"Fancier schemes, like clustering tokens, hashing on position or using bigrams, don't beat the simple random hash.","更花哨的方案，比如 token 聚类、按位置哈希或使用二元组，都没有超过简单的随机哈希。"],[317.66,325.19,40,"Ignore the future token oracle row at one point nine seven. It cheats by peeking at the answer, so it's just a sanity check.","忽略 1.97 那一行的未来 token 神谕方法。它偷看了答案，所以只是一个合理性检查。"],[325.54,333.47,40,"The takeaway is humbling: much of the gain from MoE comes from the extra sparse capacity itself, not from a smart router.","结论令人谦卑：MoE 的大部分收益来自额外的稀疏容量本身，而不是聪明的路由器。"],[333.82,341.35,40,"That said, today's large MoE models still use learned routers, because at scale and with good balancing they do work better.","话虽如此，如今的大型 MoE 模型仍然使用可学习的路由器，因为在大规模和良好均衡的情况下，它们确实效果更好。"],[342.6,347.43,41,"This timeline, from a recent MoE survey, shows how the idea took off.","这条时间线来自一篇最新的 MoE 综述，展示了这个想法是如何腾飞的。"],[347.78,351.5,41,"Open-source models are above the arrow, private ones below.","开源模型在箭头上方，闭源模型在箭头下方。"],[351.85,359.08,41,"It starts slowly, with Google's sparsely gated MoE in two thousand seventeen, then GShard and Switch Transformer.","一开始进展缓慢：二零一七年 Google 的稀疏门控 MoE，然后是 GShard 和 Switch Transformer。"],[359.43,363.35,41,"Then around late two thousand twenty-three it explodes.","然后在二零二三年底前后，它迎来了爆发。"],[363.7,375.58,41,"Mixtral 8x7B, DeepSeekMoE, Qwen1.5-MoE, DBRX, Grok-1, Jamba, DeepSeek-V2 and many more arrived within a few months.","Mixtral 8x7B、DeepSeekMoE、Qwen1.5-MoE、DBRX、Grok-1、Jamba、DeepSeek-V2 等等，在短短几个月内相继出现。"],[375.93,378.03,41,"You don't need to memorize the names.","这些名字不需要记住。"],[378.38,384.86,41,"The message is that MoE went from a research curiosity to the standard recipe for large open models.","要传达的信息是：MoE 已经从研究上的新奇玩意儿，变成了大型开源模型的标准配方。"],[385.21,393.92,41,"Today, most frontier-scale open models, including DeepSeek-V3, Qwen3's big models and Kimi K2, are MoE.","如今大多数前沿规模的开源模型，包括 DeepSeek-V3、Qwen3 的大模型和 Kimi K2，都是 MoE。"],[394.27,400.62,41,"Once everyone uses it, the interesting questions become design questions, which is our next slide.","当大家都在用它时，有意思的问题就变成了设计问题，这就是下一页的内容。"],[401.87,408.04,42,"So if you were designing an MoE yourself, what would you have to decide? This table lists the main knobs.","如果你要自己设计一个 MoE，需要决定哪些事情？这张表列出了主要的调节项。"],[408.39,415.48,42,"Which network to make sparse: usually the FFN, though some work also makes attention sparse.","让哪种网络变稀疏：通常是 FFN，不过也有工作让注意力变稀疏。"],[415.83,423.36,42,"How fine-grained the experts are: a few big experts, or sixty-four, one hundred twenty-eight or more small ones.","专家的粒度有多细：是几个大专家，还是六十四个、一百二十八个甚至更多的小专家。"],[423.71,429.59,42,"Whether to have shared experts that every token always uses, or keep all experts isolated.","是设置每个 token 都会使用的共享专家，还是让所有专家彼此隔离。"],[429.94,435.26,42,"Which activation function to use inside each expert: ReLU, GEGLU or SwiGLU.","每个专家内部使用哪种激活函数：ReLU、GEGLU 还是 SwiGLU。"],[435.61,443.6,42,"How often to place an MoE layer: every other layer, as in early models, or every layer, as in most recent ones.","多久放一个 MoE 层：像早期模型那样隔一层放一个，还是像大多数新模型那样每层都放。"],[443.95,449.49,42,"And which auxiliary losses to use during training, to keep things balanced and stable.","以及训练时使用哪些辅助损失，来保持负载均衡和训练稳定。"],[449.84,453.64,42,"We'll go through the most important of these on the next few slides.","接下来几页，我们会讲其中最重要的几项。"],[454.89,460.18,43,"This figure from the DeepSeekMoE paper shows two of the most influential design ideas.","这张图来自 DeepSeekMoE 论文，展示了两个最有影响力的设计思想。"],[460.53,465.17,43,"Panel a is conventional top-two routing over N big experts.","图 a 是在 N 个大专家上进行常规的 top-2 路由。"],[465.52,468.92,43,"Panel b is fine-grained expert segmentation.","图 b 是细粒度专家切分。"],[469.27,479.26,43,"Each expert is split into smaller ones, so we have two N experts, each half the size, and the router picks four instead of two.","每个专家被拆成更小的专家，于是有 2N 个专家，每个只有原来一半大，路由器选四个而不是两个。"],[479.61,485.56,43,"The compute is the same, but the number of possible combinations of experts is much larger.","计算量不变，但专家可能的组合数量大大增加。"],[485.91,488.41,43,"So experts can specialize more precisely.","因此专家可以更精确地实现专业化。"],[488.76,491.43,43,"Panel c adds shared expert isolation.","图 c 加入了共享专家隔离。"],[491.78,497.62,43,"Expert one, in green, is always on for every token, and the router picks three more from the rest.","绿色的专家 1 对每个 token 始终开启，路由器再从其余专家中选出三个。"],[497.97,502.78,43,"The intuition is that some knowledge, like basic grammar, is needed by every token.","直觉是：有些知识，比如基本语法，是每个 token 都需要的。"],[503.13,510.46,43,"If a shared expert handles that, the routed experts don't each have to relearn it, and can focus on specialized knowledge.","如果由共享专家来处理这些知识，路由专家就不必各自重新学一遍，可以专注于专门的知识。"],[510.81,518.27,43,"Note the last sentence of the caption: across all three, total parameters and compute stay the same. Only the structure changes.","注意图注的最后一句：在这三种结构中，总参数量和计算量保持不变，变的只是结构。"],[519.52,524.04,44,"This big table compares the expert configurations of many MoE models.","这张大表比较了许多 MoE 模型的专家配置。"],[524.39,534.32,44,"It runs from GShard in two thousand twenty, to DeepSeekMoE, Qwen1.5-MoE, DBRX, Jamba and others in two thousand twenty-four.","从二零二零年的 GShard，到二零二四年的 DeepSeekMoE、Qwen1.5-MoE、DBRX、Jamba 等。"],[534.67,538.08,44,"Don't try to read every number. Look at three columns.","不用读每一个数字，只看三列。"],[538.43,540.58,44,"First, placement frequency.","第一，放置频率。"],[540.93,546.7,44,"Early models like GShard and Switch used MoE in every other layer, shown as one half.","像 GShard 和 Switch 这样的早期模型隔一层用一次 MoE，表中记为二分之一。"],[547.05,550.57,44,"Most recent models put an MoE in every layer.","大多数新模型每一层都放 MoE。"],[550.92,559.99,44,"Second, activation function: the field moved from ReLU and GeLU to SwiGLU, which you also see in dense models like Llama.","第二，激活函数：这个领域从 ReLU 和 GeLU 转向了 SwiGLU，在 Llama 这样的稠密模型中也能看到。"],[560.34,563.24,44,"Third, the last column, shared experts.","第三，最后一列，共享专家。"],[563.59,569.83,44,"Older models have zero, while DeepSeekMoE and Qwen1.5-MoE use one or more.","老模型都是零，而 DeepSeekMoE 和 Qwen1.5-MoE 使用一个或多个。"],[570.18,572.59,44,"That's what the two bullets on the right summarize.","这就是右边两条要点所总结的。"],[572.94,578.75,44,"The design has been converging on MoE everywhere, fine-grained experts, and often some shared ones.","设计正在趋同于：处处使用 MoE、细粒度专家，并且常常带有一些共享专家。"],[580.0,585.23,45,"Now, training. We said the router might collapse onto a few favourite experts.","现在讲训练。我们说过，路由器可能会坍缩到少数几个偏爱的专家上。"],[585.58,592.22,45,"Auxiliary losses are how we fight that, and this table shows which models used which.","辅助损失就是我们对付这个问题的手段，这张表展示了哪些模型用了哪种损失。"],[592.57,597.93,45,"The importance loss encourages each expert to receive a similar total gate weight.","重要性损失鼓励每个专家获得相近的门控权重总和。"],[598.28,602.5,45,"The load loss encourages a similar number of tokens per expert.","负载损失鼓励每个专家处理相近数量的 token。"],[602.85,614.57,45,"Many later models, like Switch, GShard, Mixtral and DeepSeek-V2, use a single combined auxiliary loss with a small coefficient, around zero point zero one.","许多后来的模型，比如 Switch、GShard、Mixtral 和 DeepSeek-V2，使用单一的组合辅助损失，系数很小，大约 0.01。"],[614.92,622.55,45,"The Z-loss, introduced in ST-MoE, penalizes very large router logits, which helps numerical stability.","ST-MoE 引入的 Z 损失会惩罚过大的路由 logits，有助于数值稳定。"],[622.9,628.37,45,"And the MI-loss encourages a meaningful alignment between experts and tasks.","而互信息损失则鼓励专家与任务之间建立有意义的对应关系。"],[628.72,634.58,45,"The key point: these losses are deliberately tiny compared with the language modeling loss.","关键在于：与语言建模损失相比，这些损失被刻意设得很小。"],[634.93,638.38,45,"They should nudge the router, not dominate training.","它们应该只是轻推一下路由器，而不是主导训练。"],[638.73,648.72,45,"Some newer models, such as DeepSeek-V3, mostly replace the auxiliary loss with a simple per-expert bias adjustment for balancing.","一些较新的模型，比如 DeepSeek-V3，基本上用一个简单的、针对每个专家的偏置调整来代替辅助损失，以实现均衡。"],[649.97,653.87,46,"Let's look at a concrete case: DeepSeekMoE 16B.","我们来看一个具体例子：DeepSeekMoE 16B。"],[654.22,660.32,46,"It has sixteen point four billion parameters in total, but only two point eight billion are activated per token.","它总共有 164 亿参数，但每个 token 只激活 28 亿。"],[660.67,670.17,46,"Each MoE layer has two shared experts that every token uses, plus sixty-four fine-grained routed experts, of which the router picks six.","每个 MoE 层有两个所有 token 都会用到的共享专家，外加六十四个细粒度路由专家，路由器从中选出六个。"],[670.52,674.15,46,"So this is design c from the figure, in practice.","所以这就是图中设计 c 的实际应用。"],[674.5,681.71,46,"Every token gets the common knowledge from the shared experts, and specialized knowledge from its six chosen experts.","每个 token 从共享专家那里获得通用知识，从它选中的六个专家那里获得专门知识。"],[682.06,684.84,46,"Meanwhile, the other fifty-eight sit idle.","与此同时，其余五十八个专家处于空闲状态。"],[685.19,691.02,46,"In compute terms, each token costs roughly the same as a model under three billion parameters.","从计算量来看，每个 token 的开销大约相当于一个不到三十亿参数的模型。"],[692.27,695.65,47,"Does it pay off? Look at the scatter plot on the left.","这样做值得吗？看左边的散点图。"],[696.0,704.22,47,"The x-axis is activated parameters, which roughly means compute per token; the y-axis is average performance.","横轴是激活参数量，大致代表每个 token 的计算量；纵轴是平均性能。"],[704.57,707.59,47,"The dense models follow the red dashed trend line.","稠密模型沿着红色虚线的趋势分布。"],[707.94,712.57,47,"DeepSeekMoE 16B, the red star, sits far above that line.","DeepSeekMoE 16B，也就是那颗红色星星，远远高于这条线。"],[712.92,718.69,47,"With about two point eight billion active parameters, it performs roughly like LLaMA2 7B.","它只有大约 28 亿激活参数，性能却与 LLaMA2 7B 相当。"],[719.04,722.25,47,"The table on the right makes the comparison more direct.","右边的表格让比较更加直接。"],[722.6,730.12,47,"DeepSeek's own dense 7B model and DeepSeekMoE 16B were both trained on two trillion tokens.","DeepSeek 自己的 7B 稠密模型和 DeepSeekMoE 16B 都在两万亿 token 上训练。"],[730.47,738.44,47,"The MoE uses about seventy-four teraFLOPs per four thousand tokens, versus one hundred eighty-three for the dense model.","MoE 每四千个 token 大约用 74 万亿次浮点运算，而稠密模型是 183 万亿次。"],[738.79,745.67,47,"So that's about forty percent of the compute, yet it matches or beats the dense model on most benchmarks.","也就是大约百分之四十的计算量，却在大多数基准上持平或超过了稠密模型。"],[746.02,751.83,47,"That's the MoE promise in one table: similar quality, much less compute per token.","这一张表就体现了 MoE 的承诺：质量相近，每个 token 的计算量却少得多。"],[753.08,755.6,48,"DeepSeek then scaled this recipe up.","随后，DeepSeek 把这套配方扩展到了更大规模。"],[755.95,762.67,48,"DeepSeek-V2 has two hundred thirty-six billion parameters, but only twenty-one billion are active per token.","DeepSeek-V2 有 2360 亿参数，但每个 token 只激活 210 亿。"],[763.02,768.77,48,"It has two shared experts and one hundred sixty routed experts, with six selected each time.","它有两个共享专家和一百六十个路由专家，每次选六个。"],[769.12,777.53,48,"On the left plot, MMLU against activated parameters, DeepSeek-V2 is the red star in the top-left corner.","左边的图是 MMLU 与激活参数量的关系，DeepSeek-V2 就是左上角的那颗红色星星。"],[777.88,786.76,48,"It scores higher than most models, while using far fewer active parameters than LLaMA 3 70B or Qwen1.5 72B.","它的得分高于大多数模型，而激活参数却远少于 LLaMA 3 70B 或 Qwen1.5 72B。"],[787.11,796.02,48,"On the right, DeepSeek-Coder-V2 continued pre-training from a V2 checkpoint, with another six trillion tokens, mostly code and math.","右边，DeepSeek-Coder-V2 从 V2 的一个检查点继续预训练，又训练了六万亿 token，主要是代码和数学。"],[796.37,804.31,48,"At release, it was competitive with top closed models like GPT-4 Turbo on several coding and math benchmarks.","在发布时，它在多项代码和数学基准上可以与 GPT-4 Turbo 等顶级闭源模型一较高下。"],[804.66,813.86,48,"DeepSeek-V3, which you hear about everywhere, follows the same line: six hundred seventy-one billion total, thirty-seven billion active.","大家到处都能听到的 DeepSeek-V3 也沿袭了同样的路线：总共 6710 亿参数，激活 370 亿。"],[815.11,818.43,49,"One more practical trick: sparse upcycling.","再介绍一个实用技巧：稀疏升级改造。"],[818.78,821.87,49,"Training an MoE from scratch is expensive.","从零开始训练一个 MoE 代价很高。"],[822.22,831.84,49,"Instead, you can take an existing dense model and upcycle it: copy its FFN into several experts, add a router, and continue training.","你可以换个做法：拿一个现成的稠密模型来升级改造，把它的 FFN 复制成多个专家，加上路由器，然后继续训练。"],[832.19,842.55,49,"Qwen1.5-MoE-A2.7B did exactly this, starting from Qwen-1.8B.","Qwen1.5-MoE-A2.7B 正是这样做的，它从 Qwen-1.8B 出发。"],[842.9,848.91,49,"It ended up with fourteen point three billion total parameters and two point seven billion active.","最终它有 143 亿总参数，激活 27 亿。"],[849.26,855.64,49,"It uses sixty-four fine-grained experts: four shared, and sixty routed, choosing four.","它使用六十四个细粒度专家：四个共享专家，六十个路由专家，每次选四个。"],[855.99,867.37,49,"In the table, it's close to Qwen1.5-7B and Mistral-7B on MMLU and GSM8K, with far fewer active parameters.","在表中，它在 MMLU 和 GSM8K 上接近 Qwen1.5-7B 和 Mistral-7B，而激活参数要少得多。"],[867.72,873.07,49,"And the Qwen team reported about a seventy-five percent reduction in training cost.","而且 Qwen 团队报告说，训练成本降低了大约百分之七十五。"],[873.42,879.63,49,"That wraps up efficient architectures. We changed the design of attention and the FFN.","高效架构就讲到这里。我们改变了注意力和 FFN 的设计。"],[879.98,885.17,49,"Next, we take a model that's already trained, and ask how to shrink it.","接下来，我们拿一个已经训练好的模型，看看如何把它缩小。"]]},{"n":4,"title":"Quantization: Fewer Bits per Weight","blurb":"Scale and zero point, INT4 rounding and the outlier problem, LLM.int8(), mixed-precision training formats, and the post-training methods GPTQ and AWQ you meet in downloaded models.","file":"lecture11_part4.mp4","poster":"lecture11_part4.jpg","duration":511.1,"first":50,"last":57,"slides":[{"n":50,"title":"3 Model Compression","t":0.8},{"n":51,"title":"Quantization - What is Quantization?","t":34.37},{"n":52,"title":"Quantization","t":91.91},{"n":53,"title":"Quantization: Snap Every Weight to a Small Grid","t":154.69},{"n":54,"title":"Quantization - LLM.int8()","t":239.53},{"n":55,"title":"Mixed Precision Training","t":304.97},{"n":56,"title":"Post-Training Quantization for LLMs","t":376.94},{"n":57,"title":"Quantization Methods Comparison","t":446.18}],"sents":[[0.8,4.35,50,"So far, we've redesigned the architecture before training.","到目前为止，我们是在训练之前重新设计架构。"],[4.7,10.3,50,"Part three takes a different angle: you already have a trained model, and it's too big.","第三部分换一个角度：你已经有了一个训练好的模型，但它太大了。"],[10.65,13.5,50,"Remember that trained models are redundant.","记住，训练好的模型是有冗余的。"],[13.85,17.22,50,"Compression gives us three ways to exploit that.","压缩为我们提供了三种利用冗余的方式。"],[17.57,21.48,50,"Store the weights in fewer bits, which is quantization.","用更少的比特存储权重，这就是量化。"],[21.83,24.97,50,"Remove what isn't used, which is pruning.","去掉没用的部分，这就是剪枝。"],[25.32,30.35,50,"Or teach a smaller model to imitate the big one, which is knowledge distillation.","或者教一个小模型去模仿大模型，这就是知识蒸馏。"],[30.7,32.97,50,"We'll go through them in that order.","我们按这个顺序逐一讲解。"],[34.22,36.41,51,"What does quantization mean?","量化是什么意思？"],[36.76,43.78,51,"In general, it means mapping values from a continuous or very large set onto a small discrete set.","一般来说，它是指把连续的或非常大的取值集合，映射到一个小的离散集合上。"],[44.13,51.64,51,"On the left, a smooth signal in blue is sampled and snapped to a few allowed levels, shown in orange.","左边，一个平滑的蓝色信号被采样，并被吸附到几个允许的电平上，用橙色表示。"],[51.99,56.55,51,"The gap between the true value and the snapped value is the quantization error.","真实值和吸附后的值之间的差距，就是量化误差。"],[56.9,59.35,51,"On the right is the same idea for images.","右边是同样的想法在图像上的应用。"],[59.7,67.29,51,"The original photo of the cat uses millions of colours, while the quantized version uses only sixteen.","原始的猫咪照片使用了数百万种颜色，而量化后的版本只用了十六种。"],[67.64,72.33,51,"Zoom in and you see blocky patches, but you still clearly see a cat.","放大看会发现一块块的色块，但你仍然能清楚地看出这是一只猫。"],[72.68,76.92,51,"For neural networks, the signal is the weights and activations.","对神经网络来说，这个“信号”就是权重和激活值。"],[77.27,85.3,51,"They're normally stored as sixteen- or thirty-two-bit floats, and we want to store them with eight, four or even fewer bits.","它们通常以十六位或三十二位浮点数存储，而我们想用八位、四位甚至更少的比特来存储。"],[85.65,90.51,51,"And we want the model to stay recognizably the same, just like the cat.","同时还要让模型保持一眼就能认出的样子，就像这只猫一样。"],[91.76,95.28,52,"This is the standard recipe for linear quantization.","这是线性量化的标准做法。"],[95.63,101.48,52,"The top axis, r, is the real floating-point values, ranging from r min to r max.","上面的轴 r 是真实的浮点数值，范围从 r min 到 r max。"],[101.83,106.87,52,"The bottom axis, q, is the small set of integers we're allowed to use.","下面的轴 q 是我们可以使用的一小组整数。"],[107.22,109.05,52,"Two numbers connect them.","有两个数把它们联系起来。"],[109.4,114.27,52,"The scale S says how much real value one integer step represents.","缩放因子 S 表示一个整数步长代表多少真实数值。"],[114.62,118.68,52,"The zero point Z is the integer that corresponds to real zero.","零点 Z 是对应真实数值零的那个整数。"],[119.03,123.92,52,"Then r is approximately S times the quantity q minus Z.","于是 r 约等于 S 乘以 q 减 Z。"],[124.27,131.77,52,"To quantize, you divide by the scale, round, and add the zero point. To dequantize, you reverse it.","量化时，除以缩放因子、取整、再加上零点；反量化时，把这个过程反过来。"],[132.12,139.26,52,"The bottom example is two-bit quantization: just four levels, minus two, minus one, zero and one.","最下面的例子是两比特量化：只有四个电平，负二、负一、零和一。"],[139.61,142.29,52,"They are stored as the binary codes in the table.","它们以表中的二进制码存储。"],[142.64,147.91,52,"With four bits you'd get sixteen levels, and with eight bits, two hundred fifty-six.","四比特就有十六个电平，八比特就有二百五十六个。"],[148.26,153.29,52,"Fewer bits means less memory, but a coarser grid and more rounding error.","比特越少，占用内存越少，但网格越粗，舍入误差也越大。"],[154.54,159.54,53,"Let's make that concrete with INT4, which is what many people use for local models.","我们用 INT4 来具体说明，很多人在本地运行模型时用的就是它。"],[159.89,161.58,53,"We have sixteen levels.","我们有十六个电平。"],[161.93,170.57,53,"A simple symmetric scheme sets the scale to the largest absolute weight divided by seven, and each weight becomes round of w over scale.","一个简单的对称方案是：把缩放因子设为最大权重绝对值除以七，每个权重变为 w 除以缩放因子后取整。"],[170.92,178.37,53,"In the top row, the red FP16 weights are spread fairly evenly, so each one moves by at most half a grid step.","在上面一行，红色的 FP16 权重分布得比较均匀，所以每个权重最多只移动半个网格步长。"],[178.72,183.27,53,"The error is small, and we use four times fewer bytes than FP16.","误差很小，而且所需字节数只有 FP16 的四分之一。"],[183.62,186.61,53,"The second row shows the real danger: outliers.","第二行展示了真正的危险：离群值。"],[186.96,193.55,53,"If one weight is eight point zero while the others are small, the scale stretches to fit that outlier.","如果有一个权重是 8.0，而其他权重都很小，缩放因子就会被拉伸以容纳这个离群值。"],[193.9,197.95,53,"Then all the normal weights collapse onto just one or two levels.","于是所有正常的权重都挤到了仅仅一两个电平上。"],[198.3,200.8,53,"You've basically destroyed the information in them.","这基本上就把它们承载的信息给毁掉了。"],[201.15,207.87,53,"LLMs do have such outliers, so every serious LLM quantization method is about handling them.","大模型确实存在这样的离群值，所以每一种严肃的大模型量化方法都在设法处理它们。"],[208.22,217.29,53,"LLM.int8 keeps outlier channels in FP16. Group-wise quantization gives small groups their own scale.","LLM.int8 把离群通道保留为 FP16。分组量化让每个小组有自己的缩放因子。"],[217.64,225.75,53,"AWQ protects the salient weights, and GPTQ compensates for rounding errors. We'll see these over the next slides.","AWQ 保护重要的权重，GPTQ 补偿舍入误差。接下来几页我们会看到这些方法。"],[226.1,238.13,53,"And look at the last line: today, people use INT4 weights for local models, FP8 for training as in DeepSeek-V3, and even FP4 inference on new GPUs.","再看最后一行：如今，本地模型用 INT4 权重，训练用 FP8，比如 DeepSeek-V3，新 GPU 上甚至用 FP4 做推理。"],[239.38,247.94,54,"LLM.int8, by Tim Dettmers and colleagues, is where the outlier problem was first made really visible.","Tim Dettmers 等人的 LLM.int8，第一次让离群值问题真正显现出来。"],[248.29,256.04,54,"Look at the plot on the left: the y-axis is zero-shot accuracy, the x-axis is model size.","看左边的图：纵轴是零样本准确率，横轴是模型规模。"],[256.39,265.35,54,"A naive eight-bit baseline, the orange line, works fine up to a few billion parameters, then collapses at around six point seven billion.","朴素的八比特基线，也就是橙色线，在几十亿参数以内都没问题，但在大约 67 亿参数处突然崩溃。"],[265.7,270.62,54,"That's exactly where large outlier features emerge in certain hidden dimensions.","这恰恰是某些隐藏维度上开始出现大幅离群特征的地方。"],[270.97,275.51,54,"Their fix is mixed-precision decomposition, shown on the right.","他们的解决方法是混合精度分解，如右图所示。"],[275.86,284.12,54,"Find the few feature dimensions with outliers, with magnitude above a threshold of six, and multiply them in FP16.","找出少数含有离群值、幅度超过阈值六的特征维度，用 FP16 对它们做矩阵乘法。"],[284.47,291.53,54,"Everything else, which is the vast majority, is quantized to INT8, with per-token and per-channel scales.","其余部分，也就是绝大多数，被量化为 INT8，并使用按 token 和按通道的缩放因子。"],[291.88,293.34,54,"Then add the two results.","然后把两部分结果相加。"],[293.69,303.57,54,"The outcome: eight-bit inference that matches the sixteen-bit model even at one hundred seventy-five billion parameters, cutting weight memory in half.","结果是：即使在 1750 亿参数规模下，八比特推理也能与十六比特模型持平，权重内存减半。"],[304.82,307.63,55,"Quantization isn't only for inference.","量化不只用于推理。"],[307.98,313.57,55,"We also use lower precision during training, which is called mixed-precision training.","我们在训练中也会使用较低的精度，这叫混合精度训练。"],[313.92,318.59,55,"Here are the formats. FP32 is the full-precision baseline.","这里列出了几种格式。FP32 是全精度基线。"],[318.94,328.24,55,"FP16 halves the memory but has a narrow range, so very small gradients can underflow to zero and large values can overflow.","FP16 让内存减半，但数值范围窄，很小的梯度可能下溢为零，很大的值可能上溢。"],[328.59,336.86,55,"BF16 keeps the same exponent range as FP32 but with fewer mantissa bits, so it's much more stable.","BF16 保留了与 FP32 相同的指数范围，但尾数位更少，所以稳定得多。"],[337.21,340.8,55,"It's the default for nearly all LLM training today.","它是当今几乎所有大模型训练的默认格式。"],[341.15,350.51,55,"FP8 is the new frontier on H100 and newer GPUs, and DeepSeek-V3 was famously trained largely in FP8.","FP8 是 H100 及更新 GPU 上的新前沿，DeepSeek-V3 就以大量使用 FP8 训练而闻名。"],[350.86,353.98,55,"The classic recipe is from Micikevicius and colleagues.","经典的做法来自 Micikevicius 等人。"],[354.33,360.57,55,"Keep an FP32 master copy of the weights, and do forward and backward in sixteen bits.","保留一份 FP32 的主权重副本，前向和反向传播用十六位计算。"],[360.92,368.79,55,"And use loss scaling, multiplying the loss by a large number, so small gradients don't vanish.","并使用损失缩放，把损失乘以一个大数，使小梯度不至于消失。"],[369.14,375.54,55,"Remember the FP32 master weights, because they'll show up again when we count memory for ZeRO.","请记住 FP32 主权重，因为我们在计算 ZeRO 的内存时还会遇到它们。"],[376.79,383.7,56,"Back to inference. These are the post-training quantization methods you'll actually meet if you download quantized models.","回到推理。如果你下载量化模型，实际会遇到的就是这些训练后量化方法。"],[384.05,387.62,56,"GPTQ quantizes the weights one layer at a time.","GPTQ 一次量化一层的权重。"],[387.97,395.96,56,"It uses approximate second-order information to adjust the remaining weights, so they compensate for rounding errors.","它利用近似的二阶信息来调整剩余的权重，以补偿舍入误差。"],[396.31,404.65,56,"It reaches four or even three bits with small accuracy loss, and it's widely used through tools like AutoGPTQ and ExLlama.","它能达到四位甚至三位，准确率损失很小，并通过 AutoGPTQ 和 ExLlama 等工具被广泛使用。"],[405.0,411.25,56,"AWQ, from Song Han's group, starts from the observation that not all weights matter equally.","韩松老师团队的 AWQ，出发点是这样一个观察：并非所有权重都同样重要。"],[411.6,416.81,56,"A small fraction of weight channels see large activations, and those are the salient ones.","一小部分权重通道会遇到很大的激活值，这些就是重要的通道。"],[417.16,426.01,56,"AWQ scales those channels to protect them before quantizing, and it gets better accuracy than GPTQ at the same bit-width.","AWQ 在量化之前对这些通道进行缩放来保护它们，在相同位宽下比 GPTQ 精度更高。"],[426.36,430.21,56,"GGUF is the file format of llama.cpp.","GGUF 是 llama.cpp 的文件格式。"],[430.56,439.09,56,"Names like Q4 K M are four-bit schemes with different block structures, and it lets you run models on a laptop CPU or a Mac.","像 Q4_K_M 这样的名字，指的是不同块结构的四位方案，它让你能在笔记本 CPU 或 Mac 上运行模型。"],[439.44,444.78,56,"If you've used Ollama or LM Studio, you've probably used GGUF without knowing it.","如果你用过 Ollama 或 LM Studio，你很可能在不知不觉中就用过 GGUF 了。"],[446.03,449.88,57,"If you remember one table from this section, make it this one.","如果这一节你只记住一张表，那就记这一张。"],[450.23,455.75,57,"The precise speed numbers depend heavily on hardware and kernels, so focus on the pattern.","具体的速度数字很大程度上取决于硬件和计算内核，所以请关注整体规律。"],[456.1,459.48,57,"FP16 or BF16 is the baseline.","FP16 或 BF16 是基线。"],[459.83,466.43,57,"LLM.int8 is almost lossless at eight bits, but not much faster.","LLM.int8 在八位下几乎无损，但速度并没有快多少。"],[466.78,475.77,57,"GPTQ and AWQ at four bits give a decent speedup on GPUs, because decoding is memory-bound and you're reading four times fewer bytes.","四位的 GPTQ 和 AWQ 在 GPU 上能带来不错的加速，因为解码受限于内存，而你读取的字节只有原来的四分之一。"],[476.12,479.74,57,"GGUF is the go-to for CPU and local use.","GGUF 是 CPU 和本地使用的首选。"],[480.09,483.38,57,"The rule of thumb at the bottom is the most useful part.","底部的经验法则是最有用的部分。"],[483.73,487.16,57,"INT8: almost free, half the memory.","INT8：几乎没有代价，内存减半。"],[487.51,494.8,57,"INT4: a small quality loss, a quarter of the memory, and the sweet spot for most local deployments.","INT4：质量略有损失，内存只需四分之一，是大多数本地部署的最佳平衡点。"],[495.15,500.41,57,"Below four bits, things usually start to break, unless you use special techniques.","低于四位，除非使用特殊技术，否则模型通常就开始崩坏了。"],[500.76,509.26,57,"For your final projects, if you want to run a 7B or 14B model on a single consumer GPU, four-bit is usually the answer.","对于你们的期末项目，如果想在单张消费级 GPU 上运行 7B 或 14B 的模型，四位量化通常就是答案。"]]},{"n":5,"title":"Pruning and Knowledge Distillation","blurb":"Removing weights, neurons and layers, from magnitude pruning to LLM-Shearing, then teaching a small student with soft labels: TinyBERT, MiniLLM and data distillation for LLMs.","file":"lecture11_part5.mp4","poster":"lecture11_part5.jpg","duration":938.7,"first":58,"last":74,"slides":[{"n":58,"title":"3.2 Pruning","t":0.8},{"n":59,"title":"Neural Network Pruning - What is Pruning?","t":24.67},{"n":60,"title":"Neural Network Pruning - What is Pruning?","t":68.13},{"n":61,"title":"Neural Network Pruning - What is Pruning?","t":124.39},{"n":62,"title":"Pruning: Remove What Does Not Matter","t":188.46},{"n":63,"title":"Neural Network Pruning - How should we formulate pruning","t":257.94},{"n":64,"title":"LLM-Shearing: Accelerating via Structured Pruning","t":310.82},{"n":65,"title":"LLM-Shearing: Accelerating via Structured Pruning","t":372.38},{"n":66,"title":"LLM-Shearing: Accelerating via Structured Pruning","t":436.93},{"n":67,"title":"3.3 Knowledge Distillation","t":492.59},{"n":68,"title":"Framework of knowledge distillation","t":520.01},{"n":69,"title":"Knowledge Distillation: Learn from the Teacher's Soft Labels","t":556.44},{"n":70,"title":"TinyBERT","t":621.15},{"n":71,"title":"Benefits of KD compared to directly training","t":673.25},{"n":72,"title":"A few works on KD in LLMs","t":718.52},{"n":73,"title":"Data Distillation: A New Paradigm of KD for LLMs","t":779.02},{"n":74,"title":"More on Knowledge Distillation","t":855.66}],"sents":[[0.8,5.84,58,"That's quantization: keep every weight, but store it with fewer bits.","这就是量化：保留每一个权重，但用更少的比特存储。"],[6.19,9.97,58,"Pruning asks a different question: do we need every weight at all?","剪枝问的是另一个问题：我们真的需要每一个权重吗？"],[10.32,12.28,58,"Many weights barely matter.","很多权重几乎无关紧要。"],[12.63,18.58,58,"We can remove them one by one, or remove whole structures like heads, neurons, and even layers.","我们可以逐个删除它们，也可以删除整个结构，比如注意力头、神经元，甚至整层。"],[18.93,23.27,58,"Let's see how, and which choice actually makes things faster.","我们来看看怎么做，以及哪种选择才能真正提速。"],[24.52,29.1,59,"Interestingly, pruning happens in our own brains. Look at this curve.","有趣的是，剪枝也发生在我们自己的大脑里。看这条曲线。"],[29.45,33.27,59,"A newborn has about two thousand five hundred synapses per neuron.","新生儿每个神经元大约有两千五百个突触。"],[33.62,37.35,59,"By age two to four, it shoots up to around fifteen thousand.","到两到四岁时，这个数字猛增到大约一万五千个。"],[37.7,44.34,59,"Then, through adolescence and into adulthood, it drops to about seven thousand.","然后，经过青春期进入成年，它下降到大约七千个。"],[44.69,49.39,59,"So the brain first over-connects, then prunes away the connections it doesn't use.","所以大脑先是过度连接，然后剪掉那些用不上的连接。"],[49.74,56.98,59,"And adults are not less capable than toddlers; quite the opposite. The pruning makes the brain more efficient.","而成年人并不比幼儿能力差，恰恰相反。剪枝让大脑更加高效。"],[57.33,59.28,59,"Neural networks are similar.","神经网络也是类似的。"],[59.63,66.73,59,"We train a big, over-parameterized network because it's easier to optimize, and then we remove what it doesn't need.","我们训练一个大的、过度参数化的网络，因为它更容易优化，然后再去掉它不需要的部分。"],[67.98,70.36,60,"Neural networks work the same way.","神经网络的工作方式也是一样的。"],[70.71,76.34,60,"On the left, a fully connected network before pruning. On the right, after pruning.","左边是剪枝前的全连接网络。右边是剪枝后的网络。"],[76.69,78.41,60,"There are two kinds of removal.","删除有两种方式。"],[78.76,85.09,60,"Pruning synapses means removing individual connections, so individual weights are set to zero.","剪枝突触是指删除单个连接，也就是把单个权重置为零。"],[85.44,90.45,60,"Pruning neurons means removing whole nodes, along with all their connections.","剪枝神经元是指删除整个节点，以及它的所有连接。"],[90.8,92.11,60,"This idea is old.","这个想法由来已久。"],[92.46,100.11,60,"LeCun's Optimal Brain Damage from nineteen eighty-nine already used second-order information to decide which weights to cut.","LeCun 在一九八九年的“最优脑损伤”就已经利用二阶信息来决定剪掉哪些权重。"],[100.46,110.51,60,"Song Han's two thousand fifteen paper showed that you could remove most of the weights of networks like AlexNet and VGG with no accuracy loss.","韩松在二零一五年的论文表明，可以删掉 AlexNet 和 VGG 等网络的大部分权重而不损失准确率。"],[110.86,114.18,60,"That works as long as you fine-tune afterwards.","前提是之后要进行微调。"],[114.53,122.99,60,"The difference between pruning synapses and pruning neurons turns out to matter a lot in practice, which is the point of the next slide.","剪枝突触和剪枝神经元之间的差别在实践中非常重要，这正是下一页要讲的重点。"],[124.24,129.93,61,"How much can we prune, and how? This figure from Han and colleagues answers both.","我们能剪掉多少，又该怎么剪？Han 等人的这张图回答了这两个问题。"],[130.28,136.78,61,"The x-axis is the fraction of parameters removed; the y-axis is the accuracy loss.","横轴是被删除参数的比例；纵轴是准确率损失。"],[137.13,142.41,61,"The purple dashed line is pruning alone: remove the smallest weights and stop.","紫色虚线是只剪枝：删掉最小的权重就结束。"],[142.76,146.22,61,"Accuracy drops quickly beyond about fifty percent.","超过大约百分之五十后，准确率迅速下降。"],[146.57,151.91,61,"The green line is pruning followed by fine-tuning: the remaining weights adapt to fill the gap.","绿线是剪枝后再微调：剩下的权重会进行调整来弥补缺口。"],[152.26,156.47,61,"With that, you can remove around eighty percent with no loss.","这样就可以删掉大约百分之八十的参数而不损失准确率。"],[156.82,164.89,61,"The red line is iterative pruning and fine-tuning, the loop on the left: train, prune a bit, retrain, prune a bit more.","红线是迭代式剪枝和微调，也就是左边的循环：训练，剪一点，再训练，再剪一点。"],[165.24,171.0,61,"Now you can remove around ninety percent of the weights with essentially no accuracy loss.","这样就能删掉大约百分之九十的权重，而准确率基本没有损失。"],[171.35,175.75,61,"Two lessons. First, networks really are heavily over-parameterized.","两个教训。第一，网络确实是严重过度参数化的。"],[176.1,182.32,61,"Second, pruning is not a one-shot cut; the network needs a chance to recover after each cut.","第二，剪枝不是一刀切；每剪一次，网络都需要有机会恢复。"],[182.67,187.06,61,"That recovery idea will come back with LLM-Shearing.","这个恢复的思想在 LLM-Shearing 中还会再次出现。"],[188.31,191.99,62,"This slide organizes pruning into three ideas.","这一页把剪枝归纳为三个思路。"],[192.34,196.91,62,"The first is unstructured pruning: drop individual small-magnitude weights.","第一种是非结构化剪枝：删掉单个幅值很小的权重。"],[197.26,203.72,62,"You can reach very high sparsity, but the result is a sparse matrix with zeros scattered everywhere.","你可以达到非常高的稀疏度，但结果是一个零值散布各处的稀疏矩阵。"],[204.07,207.46,62,"GPUs are built for dense matrix multiplication.","GPU 是为稠密矩阵乘法而设计的。"],[207.81,214.11,62,"So unless you have special hardware or kernels, you often save memory but get little or no real speedup.","所以除非你有专门的硬件或计算内核，否则往往只能节省内存，却几乎得不到真正的加速。"],[214.46,221.28,62,"The second is structured pruning: remove whole neurons, attention heads, or even entire layers.","第二种是结构化剪枝：删除整个神经元、注意力头，甚至整层。"],[221.63,226.58,62,"The result is simply a smaller dense model, which runs faster on any hardware.","结果就是一个更小的稠密模型，在任何硬件上都跑得更快。"],[226.93,231.8,62,"That's why it's highlighted; it's the version that matters most in practice for LLMs.","这就是它被突出显示的原因；对大模型来说，这是实践中最重要的一种。"],[232.15,238.63,62,"The third is recovery: after pruning, continue training for a while so the model can repair itself.","第三是恢复：剪枝之后，再继续训练一段时间，让模型自我修复。"],[238.98,244.07,62,"For LLMs, that means continued pre-training, as in LLM-Shearing.","对大模型来说，这意味着继续预训练，就像 LLM-Shearing 那样。"],[244.42,249.2,62,"You may also have heard of the Lottery Ticket Hypothesis, cited below.","你们可能也听说过下面引用的彩票假说。"],[249.55,256.54,62,"It suggests that a big network contains a small sub-network that could have been trained well on its own.","它认为，一个大网络中包含一个小的子网络，这个子网络本身就能被训练得很好。"],[257.79,262.33,63,"To make pruning precise, we can write it as an optimization problem.","为了把剪枝说得更精确，我们可以把它写成一个优化问题。"],[262.68,268.6,63,"Normal training finds weights W that minimize the loss L on input x.","普通训练是寻找使输入 x 上的损失 L 最小的权重 W。"],[268.95,274.69,63,"Pruning finds pruned weights W P that minimize the same loss, but subject to a constraint.","剪枝则是寻找使同样损失最小的剪枝后权重 W P，但要满足一个约束。"],[275.04,281.85,63,"The L zero norm of W P, which just counts the non-zero entries, must be at most N, our budget.","W P 的 L0 范数，也就是非零元素的个数，必须不超过我们的预算 N。"],[282.2,288.63,63,"The difficulty is that the L zero norm is not differentiable; you either keep a weight or you don't.","难点在于 L0 范数不可微；一个权重要么保留，要么删除。"],[288.98,291.75,63,"So practical methods approximate this.","所以实际的方法都是对此进行近似。"],[292.1,300.82,63,"Magnitude pruning uses weight size as a proxy for importance. Others use gradients or second-order information.","幅值剪枝用权重大小来代表重要性。其他方法则使用梯度或二阶信息。"],[301.17,309.42,63,"And some, like LLM-Shearing on the next slides, learn soft masks that are relaxed versions of this zero-or-one decision.","还有一些方法，比如接下来要讲的 LLM-Shearing，会学习软掩码，也就是这种零或一决策的松弛版本。"],[310.67,313.91,64,"Now let's see structured pruning applied to LLMs.","现在我们来看结构化剪枝在大模型上的应用。"],[314.26,318.68,64,"LLM-Shearing, from Princeton, asks a practical question.","来自普林斯顿的 LLM-Shearing 提出了一个很实际的问题。"],[319.03,325.52,64,"If you want a good 2.7B model, is it cheaper to train one from scratch?","如果你想要一个好的 2.7B 模型，从头训练一个更便宜吗？"],[325.87,333.92,64,"Or is it cheaper to prune a bigger existing model like LLaMA-2 7B, and then continue pre-training it?","还是剪枝一个现成的更大模型，比如 LLaMA-2 7B，然后继续预训练更便宜？"],[334.27,341.59,64,"Look at the plot. The x-axis is training tokens on a log scale; the y-axis is average downstream accuracy.","看这张图。横轴是对数刻度的训练 token 数；纵轴是下游任务的平均准确率。"],[341.94,350.21,64,"The other open models of similar size, like OpenLLaMA, Pythia and OPT, were trained on hundreds of billions to a trillion tokens.","其他同等规模的开源模型，比如 OpenLLaMA、Pythia 和 OPT，都在几千亿到一万亿 token 上训练。"],[350.56,357.34,64,"Sheared-LLaMA, the blue line, beats them using only about fifty billion tokens, roughly thirty-two times less compute.","蓝线代表的 Sheared-LLaMA 只用了大约五百亿 token 就超过了它们，计算量大约少了三十二倍。"],[357.69,362.51,64,"And the curve is still climbing, so with more tokens it would keep improving.","而且曲线还在上升，所以用更多的 token，它还会继续提升。"],[362.86,366.49,64,"The lesson: a big pre-trained model is a great starting point.","经验是：一个大的预训练模型是很好的起点。"],[366.84,370.98,64,"Pruning plus continued training can be far cheaper than starting from zero.","剪枝加继续训练，可以比从零开始便宜得多。"],[372.23,378.53,65,"How does LLM-Shearing decide what to cut? The first ingredient is targeted structured pruning.","LLM-Shearing 如何决定剪掉什么？第一个要素是有目标的结构化剪枝。"],[378.88,385.77,65,"You pick a target architecture in advance, for example the configuration of an existing small model.","你预先选定一个目标架构，比如某个现有小模型的配置。"],[386.12,391.48,65,"That fixes the number of layers, the hidden size, the heads and the FFN width.","这样就确定了层数、隐藏维度、注意力头数和 FFN 宽度。"],[391.83,398.47,65,"In the figure, the source has three layers, hidden size six, four heads and intermediate size eight.","在图中，源模型有三层，隐藏维度为六，四个头，中间层大小为八。"],[398.82,403.17,65,"The target has two layers, hidden size three, two heads and size four.","目标模型有两层，隐藏维度为三，两个头，中间层大小为四。"],[403.52,408.62,65,"Then they learn masks, the z variables, at several granularities.","然后他们在几种粒度上学习掩码，也就是这些 z 变量。"],[408.97,420.35,65,"Z hidden for hidden dimensions, z head for attention heads, z inter for FFN neurons, and z layer for whole layers.","z hidden 对应隐藏维度，z head 对应注意力头，z inter 对应 FFN 神经元，z layer 对应整层。"],[420.7,427.68,65,"The pruning objective pushes the model to match the target shape exactly, while keeping the loss as low as possible.","剪枝目标会推动模型精确匹配目标形状，同时让损失尽可能低。"],[428.03,435.53,65,"What's left after pruning is a clean, dense, smaller model with a standard shape, which is easy to deploy.","剪枝后剩下的，是一个干净、稠密、更小且形状标准的模型，很容易部署。"],[436.78,439.31,66,"The second ingredient is dynamic batch loading.","第二个要素是动态批次加载。"],[439.66,443.66,66,"After pruning, the model doesn't lose ability evenly.","剪枝之后，模型的能力并不是均匀下降的。"],[444.01,449.6,66,"It might still be fine on web text, but have lost a lot on, say, code or books.","它在网页文本上可能还不错，但在代码或书籍等领域可能损失很大。"],[449.95,455.67,66,"So during continued pre-training, they periodically measure the loss on each domain.","所以在继续预训练期间，他们会定期测量每个领域上的损失。"],[456.02,462.55,66,"They compare it with a reference loss, the loss a well-trained model of the target size should reach.","并把它与参考损失进行比较，也就是目标规模下一个训练良好的模型应达到的损失。"],[462.9,468.42,66,"Domains where the gap is large get a higher sampling weight; domains that have recovered get less.","差距大的领域获得更高的采样权重；已经恢复的领域则权重更低。"],[468.77,475.66,66,"That's what the UpdateWeight subroutine does: an exponential update on the loss gap, then renormalize.","这就是 UpdateWeight 子程序做的事情：根据损失差距做指数更新，再重新归一化。"],[476.01,483.35,66,"It's a simple idea that works well beyond pruning: spend your training budget where the model is weakest.","这个简单的想法在剪枝之外也很好用：把训练预算花在模型最薄弱的地方。"],[483.7,486.22,66,"That closes our discussion of pruning.","关于剪枝的讨论就到这里。"],[486.57,491.19,66,"Next, the third compression method: let a big model teach a small one.","接下来是第三种压缩方法：让大模型来教小模型。"],[492.44,497.52,67,"Quantization kept the same model with fewer bits, and pruning cut parts out of it.","量化用更少的比特保留了同一个模型，剪枝则从模型中切掉了一部分。"],[497.87,504.4,67,"Knowledge distillation takes a different route: build a separate small model, and train it to imitate the big one.","知识蒸馏走的是另一条路：构建一个独立的小模型，训练它去模仿大模型。"],[504.75,508.45,67,"The big model is the teacher, and the small one is the student.","大模型是老师，小模型是学生。"],[508.8,513.13,67,"The question here is what exactly the student should learn from the teacher.","这里的问题是：学生到底应该从老师那里学什么。"],[513.48,518.61,67,"And, as we'll see, for LLMs the answer has shifted quite a lot.","而且我们会看到，对于大模型，这个答案已经发生了很大的变化。"],[519.86,524.7,68,"The general framework is simple. A large teacher model has already been trained.","总体框架很简单。一个大的教师模型已经训练好了。"],[525.05,528.38,68,"We feed data to both the teacher and the student.","我们把数据同时输入给教师和学生。"],[528.73,533.14,68,"The knowledge in the middle box is whatever signal we extract from the teacher.","中间框里的知识，就是我们从教师那里提取出来的任何信号。"],[533.49,540.12,68,"That could be its output probabilities, its hidden states, its attention maps, or even text it generates.","它可以是输出概率、隐藏状态、注意力图，甚至是它生成的文本。"],[540.47,545.77,68,"The student is trained to match that knowledge, usually in addition to the normal task labels.","学生被训练去匹配这些知识，通常还会同时使用正常的任务标签。"],[546.12,551.35,68,"The key insight is that a trained teacher's outputs contain more information than the raw labels do.","关键的洞察是：训练好的教师的输出，比原始标签包含更多信息。"],[551.7,555.04,68,"Let's see exactly what that extra information is.","我们来看看这些额外信息到底是什么。"],[556.29,562.28,69,"Take a photo of a cat. The hard label just says cat, one hundred percent, nothing else.","拿一张猫的照片来说。硬标签只说“猫”，百分之百，别的什么都没有。"],[562.63,570.64,69,"But the teacher's output distribution says something richer: mostly cat, a little bit like a dog or a tiger, and definitely not a car.","但教师的输出分布表达了更丰富的信息：主要是猫，有一点像狗或老虎，而且肯定不是汽车。"],[570.99,573.37,69,"Hinton called this dark knowledge.","Hinton 把这称为“暗知识”。"],[573.72,579.38,69,"It tells the student how the classes relate to each other: cats look more like tigers than like cars.","它告诉学生类别之间是如何关联的：猫更像老虎，而不是汽车。"],[579.73,582.57,69,"The loss on the slide combines two terms.","幻灯片上的损失函数由两项组成。"],[582.92,587.29,69,"The first is the usual cross-entropy with the hard label.","第一项是与硬标签之间常规的交叉熵。"],[587.64,593.89,69,"The second is the KL divergence between the teacher's and the student's distributions, both softened with a temperature T.","第二项是教师分布与学生分布之间的 KL 散度，两者都用温度 T 进行软化。"],[594.24,602.15,69,"A higher temperature flattens the distributions, so those small probabilities for dog and tiger become visible enough to learn from.","更高的温度会让分布更平坦，于是狗和老虎那些小概率就变得足够明显，可以被学习。"],[602.5,604.41,69,"Lambda balances the two terms.","lambda 用来平衡这两项。"],[604.76,611.0,69,"For LLMs, you can match logits, as in MiniLLM, or match hidden states, as in TinyBERT.","对于大模型，可以匹配 logits，比如 MiniLLM；也可以匹配隐藏状态，比如 TinyBERT。"],[611.35,614.9,69,"Or you can simply train the student on text the teacher generates.","或者，干脆让学生在教师生成的文本上训练。"],[615.25,619.75,69,"That last option, data distillation, has become the dominant one.","最后这种方式，也就是数据蒸馏，已经成为主流。"],[621.0,628.14,70,"TinyBERT, from Huawei Noah's Ark Lab, is a good example of distillation designed specifically for Transformers.","华为诺亚方舟实验室的 TinyBERT，是专门为 Transformer 设计的蒸馏方法的一个好例子。"],[628.49,633.5,70,"Instead of only matching the final outputs, the student matches the teacher layer by layer.","学生不只是匹配最终输出，而是逐层匹配教师。"],[633.85,635.7,70,"Look at the two loss arrows.","看这两个损失箭头。"],[636.05,644.04,70,"The attention loss makes the student's attention matrices look like the teacher's, so it learns where to look.","注意力损失让学生的注意力矩阵与教师的相似，从而学会该关注哪里。"],[644.39,648.78,70,"The hidden-state loss makes the student's hidden representations match the teacher's.","隐藏状态损失让学生的隐藏表示与教师的相匹配。"],[649.13,654.1,70,"That goes through a learned projection, since the student's hidden size is smaller.","这需要经过一个可学习的投影，因为学生的隐藏维度更小。"],[654.45,657.52,70,"They also match embeddings and final predictions.","他们还匹配了嵌入层和最终预测。"],[657.87,664.7,70,"The result was a model several times smaller and faster than BERT-base that kept most of its accuracy on GLUE.","结果得到的模型比 BERT-base 小好几倍、快好几倍，同时在 GLUE 上保留了大部分准确率。"],[665.05,671.85,70,"The idea is that the intermediate layers carry a lot of useful supervision, not just the final answer.","其思想是：中间层承载了大量有用的监督信号，而不只是最终答案。"],[673.1,679.22,71,"So why distill, instead of just training the small model directly on the data? There are three main reasons.","那为什么要蒸馏，而不是直接在数据上训练小模型呢？主要有三个原因。"],[679.57,682.0,71,"First, finer-grained supervision.","第一，更细粒度的监督。"],[682.35,692.27,71,"The student gets a signal from the teacher's hidden states in every layer, and from full probability distributions, not just one hard label per example.","学生能从教师每一层的隐藏状态和完整的概率分布中获得信号，而不只是每个样本一个硬标签。"],[692.62,695.43,71,"Second, you can use unlabeled data.","第二，可以利用无标注数据。"],[695.78,701.75,71,"The teacher can label as much raw text as you like, so you aren't limited by human annotation.","教师可以为任意多的原始文本打标签，所以你不受人工标注的限制。"],[702.1,705.17,71,"Third, data augmentation becomes very useful.","第三，数据增强变得非常有用。"],[705.52,710.97,71,"You can create new or perturbed inputs, and the teacher will provide sensible targets for them.","你可以构造新的或扰动过的输入，教师会为它们提供合理的目标。"],[711.32,717.12,71,"All three come down to the same thing: the teacher turns cheap data into rich supervision.","这三点归根结底是一回事：教师把廉价的数据变成了丰富的监督。"],[718.37,722.16,72,"For LLMs, what does classic distillation look like?","对于大模型，经典的蒸馏是什么样的呢？"],[722.51,728.48,72,"MiniLLM, from Microsoft Research and Tsinghua, is one well-known example.","来自微软研究院和清华大学的 MiniLLM 就是一个知名的例子。"],[728.83,738.9,72,"They noticed that the standard forward KL makes a small student try to cover every mode of the teacher's distribution, which it can't do well.","他们注意到，标准的前向 KL 会让小学生模型试图覆盖教师分布的每一个峰，而它做不好这一点。"],[739.25,744.41,72,"They use reverse KL instead, which lets the student focus on the teacher's main modes.","于是他们改用反向 KL，让学生专注于教师分布的主要峰。"],[744.76,756.0,72,"In the three plots, with GPT-2, GPT-J and OPT as teachers, MiniLLM, the solid line with stars, beats sequence-level KD, the dashed line, at every student size.","在这三张图中，分别以 GPT-2、GPT-J 和 OPT 为教师，带星号的实线 MiniLLM 在每种学生规模下都优于虚线表示的序列级蒸馏。"],[756.35,758.39,72,"But read the note at the bottom.","但请看底部的说明。"],[758.74,763.82,72,"In practice, classic logit-matching KD has had limited impact on LLMs.","在实践中，经典的 logit 匹配式蒸馏对大模型的影响有限。"],[764.17,770.58,72,"What has really worked is data distillation: using a large model to generate training data for a smaller one.","真正奏效的是数据蒸馏：用大模型为小模型生成训练数据。"],[770.93,777.62,72,"Many labs, including those behind GLM, Kimi and MiniMax, rely heavily on this.","许多实验室，包括 GLM、Kimi 和 MiniMax 背后的团队，都大量依赖这种方法。"],[778.87,784.61,73,"Data distillation is now probably the most important form of KD for LLMs.","数据蒸馏如今可能是大模型最重要的知识蒸馏形式。"],[784.96,792.36,73,"The idea is simple: use a powerful teacher LLM to write training data, then fine-tune a smaller student on it.","思路很简单：用一个强大的教师大模型来编写训练数据，然后在这些数据上微调一个较小的学生模型。"],[792.71,796.41,73,"Stanford Alpaca was the moment it went mainstream.","Stanford Alpaca 是它成为主流的标志性时刻。"],[796.76,808.71,73,"They used GPT-3.5 to generate fifty-two thousand instruction-following examples and fine-tuned LLaMA-7B on them, very cheaply.","他们用 GPT-3.5 生成了五万两千条指令跟随样本，并在此基础上以很低的成本微调了 LLaMA-7B。"],[809.06,817.26,73,"Microsoft's Phi series pushed it further, using GPT-4 to generate textbook-quality data for small models.","微软的 Phi 系列更进一步，用 GPT-4 为小模型生成“教科书级”的数据。"],[817.61,823.76,73,"And Phi-4, at fourteen billion parameters, competes with much larger models on reasoning benchmarks.","而只有一百四十亿参数的 Phi-4，在推理基准上可以与大得多的模型相抗衡。"],[824.11,830.01,73,"Orca trained on GPT-4's step-by-step explanations, rather than just its answers.","Orca 则在 GPT-4 的逐步解释上训练，而不只是学它的答案。"],[830.36,835.57,73,"Why does it work? The teacher gives richer supervision than human labels alone.","为什么有效？因为教师提供的监督比单纯的人工标签更丰富。"],[835.92,840.62,73,"That means reasoning chains, intermediate steps and diverse examples.","也就是推理链、中间步骤和多样化的样本。"],[840.97,847.22,73,"And it works across completely different architectures, because all you transfer is text.","而且它可以跨越完全不同的架构，因为你传递的只是文本。"],[847.57,854.26,73,"One caveat for your own projects: always check the terms of use of the model you distill from.","对你们自己的项目有一点提醒：一定要查看你所蒸馏的模型的使用条款。"],[855.51,858.8,74,"The line between teacher and student is now blurring.","教师和学生之间的界限正在变得模糊。"],[859.15,864.28,74,"In self-distillation, a model improves by training on its own refined outputs.","在自蒸馏中，模型通过在自己改进后的输出上训练来提升自己。"],[864.63,873.81,74,"Anthropic's Constitutional AI has a model critique and revise its own responses against a set of principles, then trains on the revised versions.","Anthropic 的 Constitutional AI 让模型依据一套原则批评并修改自己的回答，然后在修改后的版本上训练。"],[874.16,879.51,74,"SPIN and other self-play methods have the model generate its own training signal.","SPIN 等自我博弈方法让模型自己产生训练信号。"],[879.86,884.57,74,"This connects back to what you saw in Lecture six on RL post-training.","这与大家在第六讲强化学习后训练中看到的内容是相通的。"],[884.92,888.47,74,"At the other end, there's cross-model distillation at scale.","另一端则是大规模的跨模型蒸馏。"],[888.82,898.56,74,"DeepSeek distilled the reasoning ability of R1, a six-hundred-seventy-one-billion-parameter model, into much smaller Qwen and LLaMA models.","DeepSeek 把 R1 这个六千七百一十亿参数模型的推理能力，蒸馏到了小得多的 Qwen 和 LLaMA 模型中。"],[898.91,908.68,74,"Those students range from one point five to seventy billion parameters, and were made just by fine-tuning them on R1's reasoning traces.","这些学生模型从十五亿到七百亿参数不等，仅仅是在 R1 的推理轨迹上微调得到的。"],[909.03,913.9,74,"Those small distilled models reason far better than their original versions.","这些蒸馏出来的小模型，推理能力远远强于它们的原始版本。"],[914.25,920.04,74,"NVIDIA's Nemotron work builds whole synthetic data pipelines for instruction tuning.","NVIDIA 的 Nemotron 工作则为指令微调构建了完整的合成数据流水线。"],[920.39,927.6,74,"The takeaway: in the LLM era, distillation is more about data than about matching architectures.","结论是：在大模型时代，蒸馏更多关乎数据，而不是架构上的匹配。"],[927.95,930.03,74,"That completes model compression.","模型压缩就讲完了。"],[930.38,936.84,74,"We now move to the second half of the lecture: changing not the model, but how we train and run it.","现在我们进入这节课的后半部分：不改变模型，而是改变我们训练和运行它的方式。"]]},{"n":6,"title":"Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning: LoRA, Adapters, Modules","blurb":"Freeze the big model and train a thin update: LoRA's low-rank B·A, adapters and prefix-tuning, and how small task modules might be composed like Lego bricks.","file":"lecture11_part6.mp4","poster":"lecture11_part6.jpg","duration":775.5,"first":75,"last":92,"slides":[{"n":75,"title":"4 Efficient Training","t":0.8},{"n":76,"title":"From Fine-tuning to Parameter-efficient Fine-tuning","t":34.51},{"n":77,"title":"Where to Insert the Trainable Parameters","t":88.78},{"n":78,"title":"Low-Rank Approximations (LoRA)","t":137.22},{"n":79,"title":"Baseline Full Fine-tuning","t":185.78},{"n":80,"title":"LoRA Tuning","t":228.3},{"n":81,"title":"LoRA: Freeze W, Learn a Thin Update B·A","t":282.74},{"n":82,"title":"Other Parameter-efficient Tunings: Adapter Tuning","t":360.21},{"n":83,"title":"Other Parameter-efficient Tunings: Adapter Tuning","t":385.02},{"n":84,"title":"Other Parameter-efficient Tunings: Adapter Tuning","t":432.73},{"n":85,"title":"Other Parameter-efficient Tunings: Prefix-Tuning","t":479.32},{"n":86,"title":"4.2 Modularity and Composition","t":547.15},{"n":87,"title":"Parameter-efficient Fine-tuning","t":571.04},{"n":88,"title":"Modularity and Compositionality?","t":602.4},{"n":89,"title":"Modularity and Compositionality?","t":621.7},{"n":90,"title":"Modularity and Compositionality?","t":648.17},{"n":91,"title":"Parameter-efficient Fine-tuning","t":683.08},{"n":92,"title":"Modular Retrieval","t":719.53}],"sents":[[0.8,7.57,75,"We've now covered both ways of changing the model: designing efficient architectures, and compressing trained ones.","我们已经讲完了改变模型的两种方式：设计高效架构，以及压缩训练好的模型。"],[7.92,9.88,75,"Part four turns to training.","第四部分转向训练。"],[10.23,11.59,75,"Two problems come up.","这里有两个问题。"],[11.94,16.75,75,"Fine-tuning every parameter of a large model for every task is expensive.","为每个任务微调大模型的全部参数，代价很高。"],[17.1,21.68,75,"And simply replicating a model on each GPU doesn't fit in memory.","而简单地在每块 GPU 上复制一份模型，显存又放不下。"],[22.03,28.12,75,"So we'll learn to train fewer parameters with PEFT, and compose small modules.","所以我们将学习用参数高效微调来训练更少的参数，并组合小模块。"],[28.47,33.11,75,"And we'll split the rest across devices with distributed training.","再通过分布式训练把其余部分拆分到多个设备上。"],[34.36,36.31,76,"Let's start with the paradigm you know well.","我们从大家熟悉的范式开始。"],[36.66,44.12,76,"We pre-train a large model, like BERT, BART, ERNIE, GPT-3 or PaLM, on lots of unlabeled text.","我们在大量无标注文本上预训练一个大模型，比如 BERT、BART、ERNIE、GPT-3 或 PaLM。"],[44.47,51.58,76,"Then we adapt it to downstream tasks like classification, sequence labeling or question answering.","然后把它适配到下游任务上，比如分类、序列标注或问答。"],[51.93,56.45,76,"That uses a small amount of task data, the people icon at the bottom.","这一步使用少量的任务数据，也就是底部那个人群图标。"],[56.8,62.23,76,"Traditionally, that adaptation step was full fine-tuning: update every parameter.","传统上，这一适配步骤是全量微调：更新所有参数。"],[62.58,70.49,76,"As we saw on the time versus space efficiency slide earlier, that means storing a full copy of the model for every task.","正如我们之前在“时间效率与空间效率”那一页看到的，这意味着每个任务都要存一份完整的模型拷贝。"],[70.84,77.1,76,"That's fine for BERT, but impossible for a seventy-billion-parameter model with dozens of tasks or users.","对 BERT 来说还行，但对于一个七百亿参数、要服务几十个任务或用户的模型来说就不可能了。"],[77.45,82.76,76,"Parameter-efficient fine-tuning, or PEFT, replaces that arrow.","参数高效微调，也就是 PEFT，取代了这个箭头。"],[83.11,87.38,76,"Freeze the big model, and train only a small number of new parameters.","冻结大模型，只训练少量新参数。"],[88.63,94.21,77,"If we only train a few new parameters, where should we put them? There are several options.","如果只训练少量新参数，应该把它们放在哪里？有好几种选择。"],[94.56,100.16,77,"Globally, we can add a low-rank update to existing weight matrices; that's LoRA.","从全局来看，可以给已有的权重矩阵加上一个低秩更新，这就是 LoRA。"],[100.51,106.39,77,"Locally, we can insert small new layers inside each block; those are adapters.","从局部来看，可以在每个块内插入小的新层，这就是适配器。"],[106.74,115.4,77,"At the input, we can prepend a few learnable fake tokens whose embeddings are trained; that's soft prompts, or prefix tuning.","在输入端，可以在前面加上几个可学习的“假 token”，训练它们的嵌入，这就是软提示或前缀微调。"],[115.75,120.82,77,"And within MoE models, a new expert could also serve as the trainable part.","在 MoE 模型中，一个新专家也可以作为可训练的部分。"],[121.17,130.75,77,"All of them share the same principle: the pre-trained backbone stays frozen and shared, and each task only owns a small set of extra parameters.","它们都遵循同一个原则：预训练主干保持冻结并共享，每个任务只拥有一小组额外参数。"],[131.1,135.82,77,"Let's look at LoRA first, since it's by far the most widely used today.","我们先看 LoRA，因为它是当今使用最广泛的方法。"],[137.07,143.43,78,"LoRA builds on the idea of low-rank approximation, which we've already met with the PCA plot earlier.","LoRA 建立在低秩近似的思想之上，我们在前面的 PCA 图中已经见过它了。"],[143.78,155.26,78,"Any m by n matrix M can be approximated by the product of a tall thin matrix L, of size m by k, and a short wide matrix R transpose, of size k by n.","任何 m 乘 n 的矩阵 M，都可以近似为一个 m 乘 k 的高瘦矩阵 L，与一个 k 乘 n 的矮宽矩阵 R 转置的乘积。"],[155.61,157.15,78,"Here k is small.","这里的 k 很小。"],[157.5,162.94,78,"Instead of m times n numbers, you store k times the sum of m and n.","这样就不用存储 m 乘 n 个数，而只需存储 k 乘以 m 加 n 个数。"],[163.29,168.31,78,"The bullets on this slide mention low-rank approximation of the attention matrix.","这一页的要点提到了对注意力矩阵的低秩近似。"],[168.66,172.52,78,"That's the idea behind efficient-attention methods like Linformer.","这是 Linformer 等高效注意力方法背后的思想。"],[172.87,180.96,78,"LoRA applies the same tool somewhere else: not to the attention matrix, but to the update of the weight matrices during fine-tuning.","LoRA 把同样的工具用在了别处：不是用在注意力矩阵上，而是用在微调时权重矩阵的更新量上。"],[181.31,184.38,78,"Let's see why that update should be low-rank.","我们来看看为什么这个更新量应该是低秩的。"],[185.63,191.82,79,"In full fine-tuning, we start from the pre-trained weights W and learn an update, Delta W.","在全量微调中，我们从预训练权重 W 出发，学习一个更新量 Delta W。"],[192.17,195.45,79,"So the new weights are W plus Delta W.","于是新的权重就是 W 加上 Delta W。"],[195.8,200.13,79,"The problem is written on the right: Delta W has the same size as W.","问题写在右边：Delta W 和 W 一样大。"],[200.48,207.66,79,"For each weight matrix, it's d by d, possibly four thousand ninety-six by four thousand ninety-six or bigger.","对于每个权重矩阵，它是 d 乘 d 的，可能是 4096 乘 4096，甚至更大。"],[208.01,212.12,79,"And you need gradients and optimizer states for all of it.","而且你需要为它的全部参数保存梯度和优化器状态。"],[212.47,216.43,79,"But here's the intuition. The pre-trained model already knows a lot.","但直觉是这样的：预训练模型已经知道很多东西了。"],[216.78,221.83,79,"Adapting it to one task should only require a small, structured change.","把它适配到一个任务上，应该只需要一个小的、有结构的改变。"],[222.18,226.9,79,"So maybe Delta W, unlike W itself, doesn't need full rank.","所以也许 Delta W 与 W 本身不同，并不需要满秩。"],[228.15,230.6,80,"That's exactly LoRA's hypothesis.","这正是 LoRA 的假设。"],[230.95,236.32,80,"Instead of learning the full Delta W, we approximate it as B times A.","我们不学习完整的 Delta W，而是把它近似为 B 乘以 A。"],[236.67,244.45,80,"Here B is d by r and A is r by k, and the rank r is much smaller than d or k.","其中 B 是 d 乘 r，A 是 r 乘 k，秩 r 远小于 d 或 k。"],[244.8,249.79,80,"The forward pass becomes h equals W zero x plus B A x.","前向传播变为 h 等于 W0 x 加 B A x。"],[250.14,254.46,80,"That's the frozen pre-trained path, plus a thin trainable side path.","也就是冻结的预训练通路，加上一条细小的可训练旁路。"],[254.81,261.51,80,"Look at the right-hand figure, and notice the initialization: A starts random, and B starts at zero.","看右边的图，注意初始化方式：A 随机初始化，B 初始化为零。"],[261.86,267.86,80,"That means B times A is zero at the beginning, so the model starts exactly as the pre-trained model.","这意味着一开始 B 乘 A 等于零，所以模型的起点和预训练模型完全一样。"],[268.21,270.46,80,"And the update grows gradually from there.","然后更新量从这里开始逐渐增长。"],[270.81,274.36,80,"During training, gradients only flow into A and B.","训练时，梯度只流向 A 和 B。"],[274.71,281.34,80,"W zero gets no gradient and no optimizer state, which is where the huge memory savings come from.","W0 没有梯度，也没有优化器状态，巨大的内存节省就来自这里。"],[282.59,286.66,81,"Here's LoRA in one clean picture, with real numbers.","这是一张简洁的 LoRA 示意图，配上了真实的数字。"],[287.01,290.7,81,"The input x goes through the frozen d by d matrix W zero.","输入 x 经过冻结的 d 乘 d 矩阵 W0。"],[291.05,298.64,81,"In parallel, it goes through A, which squeezes it down to r dimensions, and then B, which expands it back to d.","同时，它并行地经过 A，被压缩到 r 维，再经过 B，扩展回 d 维。"],[298.99,301.12,81,"The two paths are added to give h.","两条通路相加得到 h。"],[301.47,311.91,81,"Now the arithmetic. With d equal to four thousand ninety-six and rank r equal to eight, A and B together have two times d times r parameters.","现在算一算。d 等于 4096，秩 r 等于 8，A 和 B 加起来有 2 乘 d 乘 r 个参数。"],[312.26,318.12,81,"That's about sixty-five thousand. The full matrix has d squared, about sixteen point eight million.","大约六万五千个。而完整矩阵有 d 的平方，大约一千六百八十万个。"],[318.47,326.59,81,"So we train roughly zero point four percent of the weights for that layer, and we only need optimizer states for that zero point four percent.","所以对这一层我们只训练大约百分之零点四的权重，也只需要为这百分之零点四保存优化器状态。"],[326.94,328.8,81,"Two more practical advantages.","还有两个实际的好处。"],[329.15,335.82,81,"After training, you can merge B times A into W, so there's zero extra latency at inference.","训练结束后，可以把 B 乘 A 合并进 W，这样推理时没有任何额外延迟。"],[336.17,344.03,81,"Or keep them separate, and swap a small LoRA file per task or per user on top of one shared base model.","或者把它们分开保存，在同一个共享的基座模型上，为每个任务或每个用户切换一个小的 LoRA 文件。"],[344.38,349.89,81,"QLoRA, cited below, combines this with a four-bit quantized base model.","下面引用的 QLoRA，把这一方法与四位量化的基座模型结合了起来。"],[350.24,355.63,81,"That's how many people fine-tune 7B to 70B models on a single GPU.","很多人就是这样在单张 GPU 上微调 7B 到 70B 的模型的。"],[355.98,358.81,81,"It's very likely what you'll use in your final project.","这很可能就是你们在期末项目中会用到的方法。"],[360.06,364.66,82,"LoRA is the most popular, but not the only PEFT method.","LoRA 是最流行的，但不是唯一的参数高效微调方法。"],[365.01,369.74,82,"Adapter tuning, which actually came earlier, takes a different approach.","适配器微调其实出现得更早，它采用了不同的思路。"],[370.09,377.17,82,"Instead of adding a parallel low-rank path, we insert a small new module after the pre-trained weights, in series.","它不是加一条并行的低秩通路，而是在预训练权重之后串联插入一个小的新模块。"],[377.52,383.62,82,"During training, the pre-trained W is frozen, and we only compute gradients for the adapter.","训练时，预训练的 W 被冻结，我们只计算适配器的梯度。"],[384.87,388.75,83,"Where exactly do adapters go? Inside each Transformer block.","适配器到底放在哪里？放在每个 Transformer 块内部。"],[389.1,395.89,83,"You can see two green adapter boxes: one after the attention sub-layer, and one after the feed-forward network.","你可以看到两个绿色的适配器框：一个在注意力子层之后，一个在前馈网络之后。"],[396.24,398.6,83,"Each one sits before the add-and-norm.","每个都位于残差相加和层归一化之前。"],[398.95,403.39,83,"Zoom into the adapter on the right. It's a tiny bottleneck network.","放大看右边的适配器。它是一个很小的瓶颈网络。"],[403.74,410.14,83,"First a down-projection from d to a small dimension, written m in the bullets and r in the figure.","先是一个从 d 到一个小维度的下投影，这个维度在要点中写作 m，在图中写作 r。"],[410.49,417.83,83,"Then a non-linearity, then an up-projection back to d, plus a residual connection around the whole thing.","然后是一个非线性激活，再上投影回 d 维，并在整个模块外加一个残差连接。"],[418.18,425.58,83,"Because of the residual, if the adapter weights are near zero, the block behaves exactly like the original pre-trained one.","因为有残差连接，如果适配器权重接近零，这个块的行为就和原来的预训练块完全一样。"],[425.93,431.33,83,"That's the same start-from-identity trick we saw with LoRA's B initialized at zero.","这和我们在 LoRA 中看到的把 B 初始化为零是同一个“从恒等映射出发”的技巧。"],[432.58,434.93,84,"How big are adapters in practice?","实际中适配器有多大？"],[435.28,442.56,84,"The bottleneck size is chosen much smaller than d, so adapters add only about zero point five to eight percent of the total parameters.","瓶颈维度被设得远小于 d，因此适配器只增加了总参数量的大约百分之零点五到百分之八。"],[442.91,445.67,84,"And all the original parameters stay fixed.","而原有的所有参数都保持不变。"],[446.02,449.51,84,"Compared with LoRA, the main downside is inference.","与 LoRA 相比，它的主要缺点在于推理。"],[449.86,457.58,84,"An adapter is an extra layer in series, so it adds a little latency on every forward pass.","适配器是一个串联的额外层，所以每次前向传播都会增加一点延迟。"],[457.93,462.09,84,"And it can't be merged back into the original weights the way LoRA can.","而且它不能像 LoRA 那样合并回原始权重中。"],[462.44,466.34,84,"That's a big reason LoRA became more popular for LLMs.","这是 LoRA 在大模型中更受欢迎的一个重要原因。"],[466.69,472.31,84,"But the core idea is the same: a small trainable piece, and a big frozen backbone.","但核心思想是一样的：一小块可训练的部分，加上一个大而冻结的主干。"],[472.66,477.92,84,"And there's a third family that changes the input side instead. Let's look at it next.","还有第三类方法，改动的是输入这一侧。我们接下来就看它。"],[479.17,484.38,85,"The third family is prefix-tuning, along with the closely related prompt tuning.","第三类方法是前缀微调（prefix-tuning），以及与之密切相关的提示微调（prompt tuning）。"],[484.73,492.55,85,"Instead of changing weights, we prepend a few trainable vectors, a prefix, to the keys and values in each Transformer layer.","我们不修改权重，而是在每个 Transformer 层的 key 和 value 前面拼接几个可训练的向量，也就是“前缀”。"],[492.9,497.85,85,"You can think of them as virtual tokens that steer the frozen model towards a task.","你可以把它们看作虚拟 token，引导冻结的模型去完成某个任务。"],[498.2,500.25,85,"Look at the comparison on the left.","看一下左边的对比。"],[500.6,507.71,85,"Full fine-tuning updates one hundred percent of the parameters, and you need a full copy of the model for every task.","全量微调要更新百分之百的参数，而且每个任务都需要保存一整份模型。"],[508.06,516.29,85,"Prefix-tuning trains only about zero point one percent, around two hundred fifty thousand parameters in this example.","前缀微调只训练大约千分之一的参数，在这个例子里约为二十五万个参数。"],[516.64,525.16,85,"And because each prefix is tiny, you can keep one per task, like summarization or table-to-text, and switch between them freely.","而且因为每个前缀都很小，你可以为每个任务保存一个，比如摘要或表格到文本，并在它们之间自由切换。"],[525.51,528.38,85,"You can even mix different tasks in one batch.","你甚至可以在同一个 batch 里混合不同的任务。"],[528.73,533.4,85,"So we now have three places to insert trainable parameters.","所以现在我们有三个可以插入可训练参数的位置。"],[533.75,540.74,85,"Alongside the weights with LoRA, between layers with adapters, and in front of the input with prefixes.","用 LoRA 放在权重旁边，用 adapter 放在层与层之间，用前缀放在输入的前面。"],[541.09,545.75,85,"That naturally raises a bigger question, which is our next sub-section.","这自然引出了一个更大的问题，也就是我们的下一个小节。"],[547.0,553.51,86,"We've seen that PEFT gives each task its own small module on top of a shared frozen model.","我们已经看到，PEFT 让每个任务在共享的冻结模型之上拥有自己的小模块。"],[553.86,555.88,86,"That suggests an exciting next step.","这引出了一个令人兴奋的下一步。"],[556.23,565.44,86,"If tasks and skills live in separate small modules, can we combine them, like Lego bricks, to handle new tasks we never trained on?","如果任务和技能存放在各自独立的小模块里，我们能不能像搭乐高积木一样把它们组合起来，去处理从未训练过的新任务？"],[565.79,569.64,86,"That's the question of modularity and composition.","这就是模块化与组合的问题。"],[570.89,575.44,87,"Let's start with the standard PEFT setup we have so far.","我们先从目前为止的标准 PEFT 设定说起。"],[575.79,581.01,87,"One large frozen LLM, and a separate parameter-efficient module for each task.","一个大的冻结 LLM，再加上每个任务各自独立的参数高效模块。"],[581.36,586.3,87,"Task one has its own LoRA, task two has its own, and so on.","任务一有自己的 LoRA，任务二也有自己的，依此类推。"],[586.65,588.45,87,"One task, one module.","一个任务，一个模块。"],[588.8,591.39,87,"This is already efficient in storage.","这在存储上已经很高效了。"],[591.74,595.57,87,"But each module is an island: nothing is shared between tasks.","但每个模块都是一座孤岛：任务之间什么也不共享。"],[595.92,601.0,87,"And if a new task arrives, we have to train a new module from scratch.","如果来了一个新任务，我们就得从头训练一个新模块。"],[602.25,603.98,88,"Let's think about this with Lego.","我们用乐高来思考这个问题。"],[604.33,609.13,88,"Suppose we've trained one module for skill or task one, the orange brick.","假设我们已经为技能或任务一训练了一个模块，就是这块橙色的积木。"],[609.48,613.24,88,"And another one for skill or task two, the blue brick.","又为技能或任务二训练了另一个模块，就是这块蓝色的积木。"],[613.59,615.47,88,"Each one is useful by itself.","每一块单独拿出来都有用。"],[615.82,620.3,88,"The question is: if we could snap them together, would we get something new?","问题是：如果把它们拼在一起，会不会得到某种新东西？"],[621.55,624.31,89,"Here they are, stacked together.","看，它们已经叠在一起了。"],[624.66,632.34,89,"Combining the module for skill one with the module for skill two gives us a new structure that neither brick could form on its own.","把技能一的模块和技能二的模块组合起来，就得到一个任何一块积木单独都无法构成的新结构。"],[632.69,639.98,89,"For language models, imagine one module that knows medical vocabulary, and another that knows how to write in Hindi.","对语言模型来说，想象一个模块懂医学词汇，另一个模块会用印地语写作。"],[640.33,646.77,89,"Put them together, and maybe you can handle Hindi medical text, even if you never trained on that combination.","把它们组合起来，也许你就能处理印地语的医学文本，即使你从未在这种组合上训练过。"],[648.02,657.23,90,"And that combination is effectively a new skill or task, task three, which we got for free, without any new training data for it.","而这个组合实际上就是一个新的技能或任务，任务三，我们是免费得到的，没有为它准备任何新的训练数据。"],[657.58,664.3,90,"That's the promise of compositionality: a small set of modules can cover a combinatorially large set of tasks.","这就是组合性的魅力：一小组模块可以覆盖组合爆炸式的大量任务。"],[664.65,671.35,90,"Of course, whether modules really compose this cleanly in neural networks is still an open research question.","当然，在神经网络里模块是否真能如此干净地组合，仍然是一个开放的研究问题。"],[671.7,675.72,90,"But it's a very appealing idea for efficiency.","但从效率角度看，这是一个非常有吸引力的想法。"],[676.07,681.68,90,"And it's also what humans do: we combine skills we already have to solve new problems.","这也正是人类的做法：我们组合已有的技能来解决新问题。"],[682.93,684.84,91,"Here's the contrast in one picture.","这张图展示了两者的对比。"],[685.19,689.81,91,"On the left, the standard setup: one task, one module.","左边是标准设定：一个任务，一个模块。"],[690.16,697.12,91,"On the right, a modular setup: a few shared modules, and each task is served by a combination of them.","右边是模块化设定：几个共享模块，每个任务由它们的某种组合来完成。"],[697.47,703.87,91,"Task two might use modules one and two, while task three uses only module three, and so on.","任务二可能用模块一和模块二，而任务三只用模块三，依此类推。"],[704.22,706.56,91,"This is more efficient in two ways.","这在两个方面更高效。"],[706.91,712.06,91,"Modules are reused across tasks, so we store fewer parameters in total.","模块在任务之间复用，所以总共存储的参数更少。"],[712.41,718.13,91,"And a new task might just need a new combination of existing modules, rather than a brand-new module.","而一个新任务可能只需要现有模块的新组合，而不是一个全新的模块。"],[719.38,723.35,92,"Here's a concrete example from my group, called Modular Retrieval.","这是我们课题组的一个具体例子，叫做 Modular Retrieval，模块化检索。"],[723.7,733.27,92,"On the left are the training tasks, each combining a domain and a language: English news, legal news, English medical, and Hindi legal.","左边是训练任务，每个任务都组合了一个领域和一种语言：英语新闻、法律新闻、英语医学和印地语法律。"],[733.62,740.64,92,"In the middle, we train separate modules for each attribute: news, medical, Hindi, legal, and English.","中间，我们为每个属性分别训练模块：新闻、医学、印地语、法律和英语。"],[740.99,747.18,92,"On the right are the unseen tasks: medical news, Hindi news, medical legal, and English legal.","右边是未见过的任务：医学新闻、印地语新闻、医学法律和英语法律。"],[747.53,752.23,92,"We never trained on those combinations, but we can handle them by composing the matching modules.","我们从未在这些组合上训练过，但可以通过组合相应的模块来处理它们。"],[752.58,757.38,92,"For example, Hindi plus news gives us the Hindi news task.","比如，印地语加新闻，就得到印地语新闻任务。"],[757.73,763.85,92,"Besides generalization, this also helps interpretation, because you know which modules were used for a decision.","除了泛化之外，这还有助于可解释性，因为你知道一个决策用到了哪些模块。"],[764.2,768.1,92,"That closes our discussion of parameter-efficient training.","参数高效训练的讨论就到这里。"],[768.45,773.68,92,"Next, a very different problem: what if the model itself is too big for one GPU?","接下来是一个完全不同的问题：如果模型本身大到一张 GPU 装不下，怎么办？"]]},{"n":7,"title":"Distributed Training: Data and Model Parallelism, ZeRO","blurb":"Why every LLM needs many GPUs, data versus model parallelism, the memory accounting of mixed-precision Adam, and how ZeRO stops storing the same states on every GPU.","file":"lecture11_part7.mp4","poster":"lecture11_part7.jpg","duration":827.3,"first":93,"last":111,"slides":[{"n":93,"title":"4.3 Distributed Training","t":0.8},{"n":94,"title":"Models are getting larger and larger","t":32.16},{"n":95,"title":"Distributed Training is almost Necessary for every LLM!","t":59.13},{"n":96,"title":"Parallelism in Distributed Training - Data Parallelism","t":112.46},{"n":97,"title":"Parallelism in Distributed Training - Data Parallelism","t":145.3},{"n":98,"title":"Parallelism in Distributed Training - Data Parallelism","t":180.53},{"n":99,"title":"Parallelism in Distributed Training - Model Parallelism","t":212.74},{"n":100,"title":"Parallelism in Distributed Training - Model Parallelism","t":254.93},{"n":101,"title":"Parallelism in Distributed Training - Model Parallelism","t":286.79},{"n":102,"title":"Parallelism in Distributed Training - Model Parallelism","t":302.61},{"n":103,"title":"Parallelism in Distributed Training - Model Parallelism","t":337.72},{"n":104,"title":"Parallelism in Distributed Training - DP vs MP","t":368.67},{"n":105,"title":"Distributed Training - ZeRO: Train Trillion-scale models","t":419.1},{"n":106,"title":"A Step Back: Training a Single Layer in Practice","t":443.93},{"n":107,"title":"Memory Consumptions for this example:","t":500.06},{"n":108,"title":"VRAM Estimation","t":556.14},{"n":109,"title":"ZeRO: Stop Storing the Same Thing on Every GPU","t":615.07},{"n":110,"title":"Parallel Strategy: ZeRO","t":687.94},{"n":111,"title":"ZeRO: More GPUs for Larger Models!","t":754.35}],"sents":[[0.8,4.28,93,"PEFT reduces how many parameters we train.","PEFT 减少了我们需要训练的参数数量。"],[4.63,10.87,93,"But even with PEFT, and certainly for pre-training, the model itself may be too big.","但即使用了 PEFT，更不用说预训练，模型本身也可能太大。"],[11.22,19.24,93,"A seventy-billion-parameter model doesn't fit on one GPU, even just to store its weights, gradients and optimizer states.","一个七百亿参数的模型，光是存放权重、梯度和优化器状态，一张 GPU 就装不下。"],[19.59,24.16,93,"So this sub-section asks: how do we split the work across many GPUs?","所以这一小节要问：我们如何把工作拆分到多张 GPU 上？"],[24.51,30.76,93,"We can split the data, the layers, the tensors, and finally the optimizer states, with ZeRO.","我们可以拆分数据、拆分层、拆分张量，最后用 ZeRO 拆分优化器状态。"],[32.01,33.92,94,"A little joke shows the problem.","一个小笑话就能说明这个问题。"],[34.27,36.83,94,"Your boss asks: what did you do last month?","老板问你：上个月你做了什么？"],[37.18,39.93,94,"You say: I trained the model for one epoch.","你说：我把模型训练了一个 epoch。"],[40.28,44.06,94,"And the plan for next month? Train the model for one more epoch.","那下个月的计划呢？再把模型训练一个 epoch。"],[44.41,48.49,94,"It's funny because, for large models on limited hardware, it's true.","好笑之处在于，对于在有限硬件上训练的大模型，这是真的。"],[48.84,51.62,94,"A single run can take weeks or months.","一次训练就可能要几周甚至几个月。"],[51.97,57.73,94,"That makes research painfully slow, because every idea takes a month to test.","这让研究慢得令人痛苦，因为每个想法都要花一个月来验证。"],[58.98,63.85,95,"That's why distributed training is basically necessary for every LLM.","这就是为什么分布式训练对每个 LLM 来说几乎都是必需的。"],[64.2,71.11,95,"The first bullet is the key point: the time of researchers and developers is more valuable than hardware.","第一条是关键：研究人员和开发者的时间比硬件更宝贵。"],[71.46,72.52,95,"Look at the example.","看这个例子。"],[72.87,82.09,95,"If a job takes ten GPU-days on one GPU, then with perfect scaling across one thousand twenty-four GPUs, it takes about fourteen minutes.","如果一个任务在一张 GPU 上需要十个 GPU 天，那么在一千零二十四张 GPU 上理想扩展，只需大约十四分钟。"],[82.44,91.1,95,"You can check: ten days is fourteen thousand four hundred minutes, and divided by one thousand twenty-four, that's about fourteen.","你可以验算一下：十天是一万四千四百分钟，除以一千零二十四，大约是十四。"],[91.45,95.92,95,"In practice, communication overhead means you never get perfect scaling.","实际上，由于通信开销，你永远得不到完美的线性扩展。"],[96.27,102.19,95,"But even a fraction of that speedup turns a month-long experiment into an afternoon.","但哪怕只拿到一部分加速，也能把一个月的实验变成一个下午。"],[102.54,106.47,95,"So the question is not whether to parallelize, but how.","所以问题不是要不要并行，而是怎么并行。"],[106.82,111.06,95,"There are two basic strategies, and we'll start with the simpler one.","有两种基本策略，我们先从简单的那个开始。"],[112.31,115.1,96,"The first strategy is data parallelism.","第一种策略是数据并行。"],[115.45,117.96,96,"We have one model and a big training dataset.","我们有一个模型和一个很大的训练数据集。"],[118.31,126.18,96,"Data parallelism makes a full copy of the model on each of N GPUs, and gives each GPU a different slice of the data.","数据并行在 N 张 GPU 上各放一份完整的模型副本，并给每张 GPU 分配不同的一部分数据。"],[126.53,130.57,96,"Each GPU does its own forward and backward pass on its slice.","每张 GPU 在自己的那份数据上做前向和反向传播。"],[130.92,136.63,96,"Then all the GPUs average their gradients, usually with an operation called all-reduce.","然后所有 GPU 对梯度求平均，通常用一种叫 all-reduce 的操作。"],[136.98,140.02,96,"So they all apply the same update and stay in sync.","这样它们都执行相同的更新，保持同步。"],[140.37,143.9,96,"The next two slides highlight the two halves of this idea.","接下来两页分别强调这个思想的两个方面。"],[145.15,147.84,97,"The first half: we split the data.","第一个方面：我们拆分数据。"],[148.19,151.05,97,"The training dataset is divided across GPUs.","训练数据集被分到各张 GPU 上。"],[151.4,159.36,97,"GPU one sees the blue batch, GPU two the green batch, and GPU N the orange batch.","GPU 一看到蓝色的 batch，GPU 二看到绿色的 batch，GPU N 看到橙色的 batch。"],[159.71,171.27,97,"If each GPU processes a batch of thirty-two, then with eight GPUs you're effectively training with a batch of two hundred fifty-six per step, in roughly the time of one.","如果每张 GPU 处理三十二个样本，那么用八张 GPU，每一步实际上就是在训练二百五十六个样本，而耗时大约只相当于一张卡。"],[171.62,179.13,97,"This is why data parallelism scales throughput so well: more GPUs means more data processed per second.","这就是数据并行能很好地提升吞吐量的原因：GPU 越多，每秒处理的数据越多。"],[180.38,183.99,98,"The second half: the same model sits on every device.","第二个方面：每个设备上都放着同一个模型。"],[184.34,190.94,98,"Every GPU holds a complete copy of all the parameters, gradients and optimizer states.","每张 GPU 都保存着全部参数、梯度和优化器状态的完整副本。"],[191.29,193.19,98,"And that's exactly the weakness.","而这恰恰是它的弱点。"],[193.54,198.55,98,"Data parallelism makes training faster, but it doesn't reduce memory per GPU at all.","数据并行让训练更快，但完全不会降低每张 GPU 的显存占用。"],[198.9,208.11,98,"If your model doesn't fit on one GPU, adding more GPUs with data parallelism won't help, because each of them still needs the whole thing.","如果你的模型一张 GPU 装不下，用数据并行加再多 GPU 也没用，因为每张卡仍然需要整个模型。"],[208.46,211.34,98,"For that, we need to split the model itself.","为此，我们需要拆分模型本身。"],[212.59,214.17,99,"That's model parallelism.","这就是模型并行。"],[214.52,218.36,99,"Instead of copying the model, we cut it into pieces.","我们不复制模型，而是把它切成几块。"],[218.71,225.87,99,"Look at the bottom row: GPU one holds the first layers, GPU two the next layers, and so on up to GPU N.","看最下面一行：GPU 一放前几层，GPU 二放接下来的几层，依此类推直到 GPU N。"],[226.22,230.95,99,"The activations flow from one GPU to the next, like an assembly line.","激活值从一张 GPU 流向下一张，就像一条流水线。"],[231.3,239.47,99,"Now each GPU only needs memory for its share of the model, so we can train models much larger than any single GPU.","现在每张 GPU 只需存放自己那部分模型，所以我们能训练远大于单张 GPU 容量的模型。"],[239.82,243.62,99,"Splitting by layers like this is often called pipeline parallelism.","像这样按层切分，通常叫做流水线并行。"],[243.97,249.37,99,"You can also split inside a layer, cutting each big weight matrix across GPUs.","你也可以在层内部切分，把每个大的权重矩阵切到多张 GPU 上。"],[249.72,253.53,99,"That's called tensor parallelism, as in Megatron-LM.","这叫做张量并行，比如 Megatron-LM 就是这样做的。"],[254.78,259.71,100,"Notice that in model parallelism there's a single copy of the data.","注意，在模型并行中，数据只有一份。"],[260.06,266.41,100,"The whole batch goes into GPU one, and its outputs are passed along to GPU two, and so on down the line.","整个 batch 先进入 GPU 一，它的输出再传给 GPU 二，依次往下传。"],[266.76,271.35,100,"So the roles are reversed compared with data parallelism.","所以和数据并行相比，角色正好反了过来。"],[271.7,276.09,100,"In data parallelism, the model is replicated and the data is split.","在数据并行中，模型被复制，数据被拆分。"],[276.44,280.82,100,"In model parallelism, the data is shared and the model is split.","在模型并行中，数据是共享的，模型被拆分。"],[281.17,285.39,100,"Keep that symmetry in mind; it makes the trade-offs easy to remember.","记住这种对称性，就很容易记住它们各自的取舍。"],[286.64,289.09,101,"Let's watch the split happen piece by piece.","我们来一块一块地看这个切分过程。"],[289.44,294.67,101,"The first chunk of the model, the first couple of layers circled in red, goes to GPU one.","模型的第一块，也就是红圈圈出的前几层，放到 GPU 一上。"],[295.02,301.21,101,"GPU one receives the input data, runs these layers, and sends its output activations to the next GPU.","GPU 一接收输入数据，运行这几层，然后把输出的激活值发送给下一张 GPU。"],[302.46,305.22,102,"The next chunk of layers goes to GPU two.","下一块层放到 GPU 二上。"],[305.57,310.92,102,"GPU two can't start until GPU one has passed along its activations.","在 GPU 一把激活值传过来之前，GPU 二无法开始。"],[311.27,316.54,102,"In the backward pass, gradients flow the opposite way, from GPU two back to GPU one.","在反向传播中，梯度朝相反方向流动，从 GPU 二回到 GPU 一。"],[316.89,323.34,102,"You can already see a problem: while GPU two is working, GPU one may be sitting idle, waiting.","你已经能看到一个问题：GPU 二在工作时，GPU 一可能闲着在等待。"],[323.69,325.92,102,"This is called the pipeline bubble.","这就叫流水线气泡。"],[326.27,336.32,102,"Techniques like GPipe reduce it by splitting each batch into micro-batches, so different GPUs can work on different micro-batches at the same time.","像 GPipe 这样的技术通过把每个 batch 拆成多个微批次来减少气泡，让不同的 GPU 能同时处理不同的微批次。"],[337.57,344.26,103,"And so on, until the last chunk of the model lands on GPU N, which produces the final output and the loss.","依此类推，直到模型的最后一块落在 GPU N 上，由它产生最终输出和损失。"],[344.61,348.56,103,"Together, the N GPUs hold exactly one copy of the model.","这 N 张 GPU 加起来正好保存一份模型。"],[348.91,353.09,103,"So the total model size you can train grows roughly with the number of GPUs.","所以你能训练的模型总规模大致随 GPU 数量增长。"],[353.44,362.28,103,"The price is that activations must travel between GPUs at every boundary, in both directions, and GPUs may wait on each other.","代价是激活值必须在每个边界处于 GPU 之间双向传输，而且 GPU 之间可能互相等待。"],[362.63,367.27,103,"That's the communication cost we flagged at the very beginning of the lecture.","这就是我们在本讲一开始就提到的通信开销。"],[368.52,370.09,104,"Let's put the two side by side.","我们把两者放在一起比较。"],[370.44,375.1,104,"Data parallelism splits the data and keeps the same model on every device.","数据并行拆分数据，并在每个设备上保留同一个模型。"],[375.45,383.69,104,"It's easy to implement and keeps GPUs busy, but you store N copies of the model, so it doesn't help if the model is too big.","它容易实现，能让 GPU 保持忙碌，但要存 N 份模型副本，所以模型太大时它帮不上忙。"],[384.04,389.43,104,"Model parallelism splits the model and moves activations through the devices.","模型并行拆分模型，让激活值在设备之间传递。"],[389.78,392.94,104,"It lets you fit huge models with a single copy.","它只用一份副本就能装下巨大的模型。"],[393.29,399.28,104,"But it's harder to parallelize well, and it suffers from load balancing problems and pipeline bubbles.","但它更难做好并行，还存在负载均衡问题和流水线气泡。"],[399.63,407.68,104,"In practice, training a large LLM uses both at once, plus tensor parallelism, which is sometimes called 3D parallelism.","实际上，训练大型 LLM 会同时使用这两种并行，再加上张量并行，有时被称为 3D 并行。"],[408.03,416.27,104,"But there's a clever middle ground that gets most of the memory benefit of model parallelism, while keeping the simplicity of data parallelism.","不过还有一个巧妙的折中方案，它能获得模型并行的大部分显存收益，同时保留数据并行的简单性。"],[416.62,417.7,104,"That's ZeRO.","那就是 ZeRO。"],[418.95,426.99,105,"Data parallelism is simple but wastes memory with N full copies; model parallelism saves memory but is hard to balance.","数据并行简单，但 N 份完整副本浪费显存；模型并行节省显存，但难以均衡负载。"],[427.34,432.08,105,"ZeRO, from Microsoft's DeepSpeed team, asks a simple question.","来自微软 DeepSpeed 团队的 ZeRO 提出了一个简单的问题。"],[432.43,436.61,105,"In data parallelism, do all those copies really need to be complete?","在数据并行中，所有这些副本真的都需要是完整的吗？"],[436.96,442.53,105,"To answer it, we first need to understand exactly what's taking up memory during training.","要回答这个问题，我们首先需要搞清楚训练时到底是什么在占用显存。"],[443.78,451.83,106,"Let's take a step back and look at what happens when we train one layer with mixed precision, the recipe we saw earlier in the quantization section.","我们退一步，看看用混合精度训练一层时会发生什么，也就是我们之前在量化部分见过的方法。"],[452.18,456.62,106,"Start at the bottom left: we keep master weights in FP32.","从左下角开始：我们用 FP32 保存主权重。"],[456.97,463.68,106,"Before each step, we convert them to half precision, in the float-to-half box.","每一步之前，我们在 float2half 这个框里把它们转成半精度。"],[464.03,469.9,106,"We use those FP16 weights for the forward pass, producing FP16 activations.","我们用这些 FP16 权重做前向传播，得到 FP16 的激活值。"],[470.25,476.89,106,"In the backward pass, we compute activation gradients and weight gradients, also in FP16.","在反向传播中，我们计算激活梯度和权重梯度，同样是 FP16。"],[477.24,484.44,106,"Finally, the weight gradients go into the weight update, the green box, which updates the FP32 master weights.","最后，权重梯度进入绿色的权重更新框，用来更新 FP32 的主权重。"],[484.79,488.99,106,"So for every parameter, we're holding several versions in memory at once.","所以对每个参数，我们在显存里同时保存了好几个版本。"],[489.34,497.01,106,"FP16 weights, FP16 gradients, FP32 master weights, plus the optimizer's own state.","FP16 权重、FP16 梯度、FP32 主权重，再加上优化器自己的状态。"],[497.36,498.66,106,"Let's count the bytes.","我们来数一数字节。"],[499.91,501.68,107,"Time for some accounting.","来算一笔账。"],[502.03,505.57,107,"Say the model has Phi parameters, and we train it with Adam.","假设模型有 Phi 个参数，我们用 Adam 来训练。"],[505.92,511.11,107,"Each step, we have to store the FP16 parameters, two bytes each, so two Phi.","每一步，我们都要存 FP16 参数，每个两字节，所以是二 Phi。"],[511.46,514.61,107,"The FP16 gradients take another two Phi.","FP16 梯度又占二 Phi。"],[514.96,522.86,107,"Then come Adam's optimizer states in FP32: a master copy of the parameters, the momentum, and the variance.","然后是 FP32 的 Adam 优化器状态：参数的主副本、动量和方差。"],[523.21,526.79,107,"Each of those is four bytes, so twelve Phi in total.","每项四字节，总共十二 Phi。"],[527.14,533.71,107,"On top of that, there are residual states like activations, temporary buffers and memory fragmentation.","除此之外，还有残余状态，比如激活值、临时缓冲区和显存碎片。"],[534.06,538.35,107,"That's sixteen bytes per parameter, before activations.","不算激活值，每个参数就要十六字节。"],[538.7,547.37,107,"Look at the GPT-2 example: one point five billion parameters fit in three gigabytes in FP16, but training needs at least twenty-four gigabytes.","看 GPT-2 的例子：十五亿参数用 FP16 存只要 3 GB，但训练至少需要 24 GB。"],[547.72,554.74,107,"And notice that the biggest chunk, twelve of the sixteen bytes, is the optimizer state, not the model itself.","注意，最大的一块，十六字节中的十二字节，是优化器状态，而不是模型本身。"],[555.99,564.38,108,"Let's do this for a model my group trained: HuatuoGPT-7B, our medical LLM, which you may remember from Lecture nine.","我们用课题组训练的一个模型来算一下：HuatuoGPT-7B，我们的医疗大模型，你们可能在第九讲还记得它。"],[564.73,570.14,108,"The parameters in FP16: seven billion times two bytes, fourteen gigabytes.","FP16 参数：七十亿乘以两字节，14 GB。"],[570.49,574.21,108,"The gradients in FP16: another fourteen gigabytes.","FP16 梯度：又是 14 GB。"],[574.56,586.15,108,"Then AdamW's states in FP32: the master weights take twenty-eight gigabytes, the first moment m another twenty-eight, and the second moment v another twenty-eight.","然后是 FP32 的 AdamW 状态：主权重 28 GB，一阶矩 m 再 28 GB，二阶矩 v 又是 28 GB。"],[586.5,594.85,108,"Add it up, and you get one hundred twelve gigabytes just for the training states, before any activations, buffers or fragmentation.","加起来，光训练状态就有 112 GB，还没算激活值、缓冲区和碎片。"],[595.2,600.1,108,"That's more than a single eighty-gigabyte A100 or H100.","这已经超过了一张 80 GB 的 A100 或 H100。"],[600.45,606.97,108,"So even a small seven-billion-parameter model can't be fully fine-tuned on one GPU with plain Adam.","所以即使是一个七十亿参数的“小”模型，也无法在一张 GPU 上用普通 Adam 做全量微调。"],[607.32,613.67,108,"This is exactly why we need LoRA, which we just saw, or ZeRO, which comes next.","这正是我们需要 LoRA，也就是刚刚讲过的，或者 ZeRO，也就是接下来要讲的，的原因。"],[614.92,619.47,109,"ZeRO's insight is almost embarrassingly simple.","ZeRO 的洞见简单得几乎让人难以置信。"],[619.82,626.97,109,"In plain data parallelism, every GPU stores the same optimizer states, the same gradients, and the same weights.","在普通数据并行中，每张 GPU 都存着相同的优化器状态、相同的梯度和相同的权重。"],[627.32,633.06,109,"That's pure redundancy: with four GPUs, you're storing four identical copies of everything.","这纯粹是冗余：用四张 GPU，你就把所有东西存了四份一模一样的副本。"],[633.41,639.45,109,"ZeRO, short for Zero Redundancy Optimizer, removes that redundancy in three stages.","ZeRO 是 Zero Redundancy Optimizer，零冗余优化器的缩写，它分三个阶段消除这种冗余。"],[639.8,648.05,109,"ZeRO-1 shards the optimizer states, so each GPU keeps only its quarter of the biggest part, the twelve bytes per parameter.","ZeRO-1 切分优化器状态，这样每张 GPU 只保存最大那部分，也就是每参数十二字节的四分之一。"],[648.4,651.43,109,"ZeRO-2 also shards the gradients.","ZeRO-2 还切分梯度。"],[651.78,658.24,109,"ZeRO-3 also shards the weights themselves, gathering them on the fly when a layer needs them.","ZeRO-3 连权重本身也切分，在某一层需要时再即时收集。"],[658.59,664.08,109,"At that point, memory per GPU scales like one over the number of GPUs.","到这一步，每张 GPU 的显存就与 GPU 数量成反比。"],[664.43,670.36,109,"Look at the red line, for a seven-point-five-billion-parameter model on sixty-four GPUs.","看这行红字，一个七十五亿参数的模型，用六十四张 GPU。"],[670.71,683.33,109,"That's one hundred twenty gigabytes per GPU with plain data parallelism, thirty-one point four with ZeRO-1, sixteen point six with ZeRO-2, and just one point nine with ZeRO-3.","普通数据并行每张 GPU 要 120 GB，ZeRO-1 是 31.4 GB，ZeRO-2 是 16.6 GB，而 ZeRO-3 只要 1.9 GB。"],[683.68,686.54,109,"That's the power of not storing the same thing twice.","这就是“不重复存储同一份东西”的威力。"],[687.79,692.24,110,"This is the original figure from the ZeRO paper, with the formulas.","这是 ZeRO 论文中的原图，附带了公式。"],[692.59,700.27,110,"Psi is the number of parameters, and K is the optimizer-state multiplier, which is twelve for mixed-precision Adam.","Psi 是参数数量，K 是优化器状态的倍数，对混合精度 Adam 来说是十二。"],[700.62,703.39,110,"N-d is the data-parallel degree.","N-d 是数据并行的并行度。"],[703.74,709.0,110,"The baseline stores two plus two plus K, times Psi, on every GPU.","基线在每张 GPU 上存储二加二加 K，再乘以 Psi。"],[709.35,715.29,110,"P-os shards the optimizer states, so only the K Psi term is divided by N-d.","P-os 切分优化器状态，所以只有 K Psi 这一项除以 N-d。"],[715.64,721.45,110,"P-os-plus-g also divides the gradients, and P-os-plus-g-plus-p divides everything.","P-os+g 还把梯度也除掉，而 P-os+g+p 把所有东西都除掉。"],[721.8,733.36,110,"With Psi equal to seven point five billion and sixty-four GPUs, you get the one hundred twenty, thirty-one point four, sixteen point six and one point nine gigabytes we just saw.","当 Psi 等于七十五亿、用六十四张 GPU 时，就得到我们刚才看到的 120、31.4、16.6 和 1.9 GB。"],[733.71,735.2,110,"What about communication?","那通信呢？"],[735.55,742.08,110,"Stages one and two have the same communication volume as normal data parallelism, so they're essentially free.","第一和第二阶段的通信量与普通数据并行相同，所以基本上是免费的。"],[742.43,749.53,110,"Stage three costs about one point five times as much, because weights must be gathered during both the forward and backward passes.","第三阶段的通信量大约是一点五倍，因为在前向和反向传播中都要收集权重。"],[749.88,752.95,110,"That's usually a good trade when memory is the limit.","当显存是瓶颈时，这通常是划算的交换。"],[754.2,756.04,111,"And here's what that buys you.","来看看这能给你带来什么。"],[756.39,764.95,111,"This table shows memory per GPU in gigabytes for seven-point-five-billion, one-hundred-twenty-eight-billion and one-trillion-parameter models.","这张表显示了七十五亿、一千二百八十亿和一万亿参数模型的每卡显存，单位是 GB。"],[765.3,771.0,111,"Going down the rows, we increase the number of data-parallel GPUs from one to one thousand twenty-four.","从上往下，数据并行的 GPU 数量从一增加到一千零二十四。"],[771.35,772.63,111,"Look at the bold numbers.","看加粗的数字。"],[772.98,784.29,111,"For the seven-point-five-billion model, full ZeRO-3 brings it down to thirty gigabytes with just four GPUs, so it fits on four thirty-two-gigabyte V100s.","对七十五亿参数的模型，完整的 ZeRO-3 只用四张 GPU 就降到 30 GB，所以四张 32 GB 的 V100 就能放下。"],[784.64,791.08,111,"A one-hundred-twenty-eight-billion model gets down to thirty-two gigabytes per GPU with sixty-four GPUs.","一千二百八十亿参数的模型，用六十四张 GPU 可以降到每卡 32 GB。"],[791.43,800.36,111,"And even a one-trillion-parameter model reaches about fifteen point six gigabytes per GPU with one thousand twenty-four GPUs.","甚至一万亿参数的模型，用一千零二十四张 GPU 也能降到每卡约 15.6 GB。"],[800.71,809.26,111,"These numbers don't include activations, but the trend is the point: more GPUs, bigger models, with no change to your model code.","这些数字不包括激活值，但重点在于趋势：GPU 越多，模型越大，而且模型代码不用改。"],[809.61,817.31,111,"That's why DeepSpeed ZeRO, and PyTorch FSDP, which implements the same idea, are standard tools today.","这就是为什么 DeepSpeed ZeRO，以及实现了同样思想的 PyTorch FSDP，如今都是标准工具。"],[817.66,819.66,111,"And that completes efficient training.","高效训练部分到此结束。"],[820.01,825.4,111,"Now let's move to the part that matters most for the cost of using LLMs every day: inference.","现在我们进入对日常使用 LLM 的成本影响最大的部分：推理。"]]},{"n":8,"title":"Inference Bottlenecks, the KV Cache and PagedAttention","blurb":"Prefill versus decode, why serving is memory-bound, how the KV cache grows with every token, and how PagedAttention borrows virtual memory to stop wasting it.","file":"lecture11_part8.mp4","poster":"lecture11_part8.jpg","duration":541.8,"first":112,"last":120,"slides":[{"n":112,"title":"5 Efficient Inference","t":0.8},{"n":113,"title":"Why Inference Efficiency Matters","t":32.35},{"n":114,"title":"Two Phases of LLM Inference","t":88.41},{"n":115,"title":"Why is LLM Serving Hard?","t":154.4},{"n":116,"title":"5.2 The KV Cache","t":228.64},{"n":117,"title":"What is the KV Cache?","t":254.65},{"n":118,"title":"The KV Cache Grows with Every Token","t":339.36},{"n":119,"title":"KV Cache Optimization","t":402.24},{"n":120,"title":"PagedAttention: Virtual Memory for the KV Cache","t":465.15}],"sents":[[0.8,6.9,112,"We've made training cheaper with PEFT, and fit huge models with distributed training and ZeRO.","我们用 PEFT 让训练更便宜，用分布式训练和 ZeRO 装下了巨大的模型。"],[7.25,13.46,112,"But training happens once, while inference runs billions of times, every time anyone sends a prompt.","但训练只发生一次，而推理要运行数十亿次，每当有人发送一个提示就运行一次。"],[13.81,18.31,112,"And decoding is memory-bound, so the battle is for memory and bandwidth.","而且解码受限于内存，所以要争夺的是显存和带宽。"],[18.66,21.81,112,"In Part five, we'll first see why inference is hard.","在第五部分，我们先看看推理为什么难。"],[22.16,30.95,112,"Then we'll study the KV cache, speculative decoding, FlashAttention, and finally a full serving system, vLLM.","然后学习 KV 缓存、推测解码、FlashAttention，最后是一个完整的推理服务系统 vLLM。"],[32.2,35.2,113,"Why does inference efficiency matter so much?","为什么推理效率如此重要？"],[35.55,41.28,113,"Because training is a one-time cost, while inference runs millions of times a day for a popular model.","因为训练是一次性成本，而对于一个热门模型，推理每天要运行数百万次。"],[41.63,46.75,113,"For most companies, the total cost of serving soon exceeds the cost of training.","对大多数公司来说，推理服务的总成本很快就会超过训练成本。"],[47.1,49.17,113,"There are three bottlenecks to remember.","有三个瓶颈需要记住。"],[49.52,56.79,113,"First, memory bandwidth: for every token we generate, we have to read all the model weights from GPU memory.","第一，内存带宽：每生成一个 token，都要从 GPU 显存读取全部模型权重。"],[57.14,62.56,113,"Second, the KV cache, which grows with both sequence length and batch size.","第二，KV 缓存，它随序列长度和 batch 大小增长。"],[62.91,70.51,113,"Third, autoregressive decoding is sequential: you can't produce token ten until you've produced token nine.","第三，自回归解码是串行的：没生成第九个 token，就无法生成第十个。"],[70.86,76.58,113,"The goal is simple to state: serve more users, with lower latency, at lower cost.","目标说起来很简单：以更低的延迟、更低的成本服务更多用户。"],[76.93,82.9,113,"Systems like vLLM, TensorRT-LLM and SGLang are built to do exactly that.","vLLM、TensorRT-LLM 和 SGLang 这样的系统正是为此而构建的。"],[83.25,87.01,113,"By the end of this part, you'll understand the main tricks inside them.","学完这一部分，你就会理解它们内部的主要技巧。"],[88.26,93.32,114,"It helps to split inference into two phases, because they have very different bottlenecks.","把推理分成两个阶段来看会很有帮助，因为它们的瓶颈截然不同。"],[93.67,96.72,114,"The prefill phase processes your whole prompt.","预填充阶段处理整个提示。"],[97.07,103.15,114,"All the input tokens are known, so we can run them through the model in parallel, just like in training.","所有输入 token 都是已知的，所以可以像训练时一样并行地送入模型。"],[103.5,107.61,114,"We compute and store the KV cache for every prompt token.","我们为每个提示 token 计算并存储 KV 缓存。"],[107.96,113.53,114,"Because there's lots of parallel work, this phase is compute-bound: the GPU cores are busy.","因为有大量并行工作，这个阶段是计算受限的：GPU 核心很忙。"],[113.88,118.53,114,"The decode phase then generates the answer one token at a time.","接着，解码阶段一次一个 token 地生成回答。"],[118.88,124.46,114,"Each step reads all the model weights and the entire KV cache, but produces just one token.","每一步都要读取全部模型权重和整个 KV 缓存，却只产生一个 token。"],[124.81,130.78,114,"That's a lot of memory reading for very little arithmetic, so this phase is memory-bandwidth-bound.","大量的内存读取只换来很少的计算，所以这个阶段受限于内存带宽。"],[131.13,138.12,114,"Here's the key insight at the bottom: during decoding, the GPU's compute units sit mostly idle, waiting for memory.","底部是关键洞见：解码时，GPU 的计算单元大部分时间都闲着，在等内存。"],[138.47,142.72,114,"GPU utilization can be as low as one to five percent.","GPU 利用率可能低至百分之一到百分之五。"],[143.07,153.0,114,"Most of the inference tricks we'll see, like batching many requests, speculative decoding, and shrinking the KV cache, are ways of doing more useful work per byte read.","我们将看到的大多数推理技巧，比如批处理多个请求、推测解码、缩小 KV 缓存，都是为了让每读一个字节做更多有用的工作。"],[154.25,158.61,115,"Serving LLMs to many users at once adds more challenges.","同时为许多用户提供 LLM 服务，还会带来更多挑战。"],[158.96,160.78,115,"First, the memory footprint.","第一，显存占用。"],[161.13,171.02,115,"LLaMA-70B needs about one hundred forty gigabytes just for its weights in FP16, which is already two GPUs.","LLaMA-70B 光是 FP16 权重就需要约 140 GB，这已经是两张 GPU 了。"],[171.37,177.09,115,"And then the KV cache grows with sequence length, batch size, layers and heads.","然后 KV 缓存还会随序列长度、batch 大小、层数和头数增长。"],[177.44,185.12,115,"Second, requests vary wildly: one user sends ten tokens, another sends one hundred thousand.","第二，请求差异巨大：一个用户发十个 token，另一个发十万个。"],[185.47,192.75,115,"And you don't know in advance how long each answer will be, so you can't pre-allocate the right amount of memory.","而且你事先不知道每个回答会有多长，所以无法预先分配合适的显存。"],[193.1,196.71,115,"Third, there's a tension between latency and throughput.","第三，延迟和吞吐量之间存在矛盾。"],[197.06,205.63,115,"Each user wants a fast first token, while the provider wants to pack as many users as possible onto each GPU.","每个用户都希望首个 token 来得快，而服务商希望每张 GPU 上塞进尽可能多的用户。"],[205.98,208.38,115,"And fourth, memory fragmentation.","第四，显存碎片。"],[208.73,214.35,115,"If you naively reserve memory for the maximum possible length, most of it sits empty.","如果你简单地按最大可能长度预留显存，大部分都会空着。"],[214.7,223.24,115,"Measurements in the vLLM paper found that existing systems wasted roughly sixty to eighty percent of KV cache memory this way.","vLLM 论文的测量发现，现有系统以这种方式浪费了大约百分之六十到八十的 KV 缓存显存。"],[223.59,227.24,115,"Keep that number in mind; PagedAttention will fix it.","记住这个数字，PagedAttention 会解决它。"],[228.49,234.67,116,"We've seen why inference is hard: decoding is memory-bound, and memory is tight.","我们已经看到推理为什么难：解码受限于内存，而显存很紧张。"],[235.02,238.97,116,"The single biggest memory consumer during serving is the KV cache.","推理服务中最大的显存消耗者就是 KV 缓存。"],[239.32,246.95,116,"Caching keys and values saves a huge amount of recomputation, but the cache itself becomes the problem.","缓存 key 和 value 省去了大量重复计算，但缓存本身却成了问题。"],[247.3,253.25,116,"This sub-section explains what the KV cache is, how big it gets, and how we tame it.","这一小节讲解 KV 缓存是什么、它会变得多大，以及我们如何驾驭它。"],[254.5,261.22,117,"Recall the attention formula: softmax of Q times K-transpose over the square root of d, times V.","回忆一下注意力公式：Q 乘以 K 转置再除以根号 d，做 softmax，再乘以 V。"],[261.57,266.98,117,"When we generate token by token, at each step only the new token produces a new query.","当我们逐个生成 token 时，每一步只有新 token 产生一个新的 query。"],[267.33,272.73,117,"But that query must attend to the keys and values of all previous tokens.","但这个 query 必须关注之前所有 token 的 key 和 value。"],[273.08,278.96,117,"Those old keys and values don't change, so recomputing them every step would be a huge waste.","那些旧的 key 和 value 不会变，所以每一步都重新计算它们是巨大的浪费。"],[279.31,283.52,117,"Instead, we compute them once and cache them. That's the KV cache.","所以我们只计算一次并缓存起来。这就是 KV 缓存。"],[283.87,293.49,117,"The size per token per layer is two, for K and V, times the number of KV heads, times the head dimension, times the bytes per number.","每个 token 每层的大小是：二，代表 K 和 V，乘以 KV 头数，乘以头维度，再乘以每个数的字节数。"],[293.84,298.78,117,"Multiply by the number of layers and the number of tokens, and it grows fast.","再乘以层数和 token 数，它增长得很快。"],[299.13,312.05,117,"The slide's example uses LLaMA-2-70B dimensions: eighty layers, sixty-four heads of size one hundred twenty-eight, in FP16, for four thousand ninety-six tokens.","幻灯片的例子用的是 LLaMA-2-70B 的尺寸：八十层，六十四个维度为一百二十八的头，FP16，四千零九十六个 token。"],[312.4,317.69,117,"The result is about ten point seven gigabytes, for a single sequence.","结果是大约 10.7 GB，这只是一个序列。"],[318.04,326.3,117,"One detail worth knowing: LLaMA-2-70B actually uses grouped-query attention, with only eight key-value heads.","有一个值得了解的细节：LLaMA-2-70B 实际上用的是分组查询注意力，只有八个 key-value 头。"],[326.65,333.93,117,"That cuts the cache by eight times compared with having all sixty-four, down to about one point three gigabytes.","与六十四个头全都保留相比，缓存减少了八倍，降到约 1.3 GB。"],[334.28,337.96,117,"That's the GQA idea from Part two, paying off directly.","这就是第二部分讲的 GQA 思想带来的直接回报。"],[339.21,344.72,118,"This slide shows the KV cache growing as we generate: The cat sat on the mat.","这一页展示了在生成 The cat sat on the mat 时 KV 缓存的增长过程。"],[345.07,349.04,118,"Each new token adds one more key and one more value, in every layer.","每个新 token 都会在每一层增加一个 key 和一个 value。"],[349.39,354.15,118,"And the red memory bar on the right grows by one block per token.","右边红色的显存条每个 token 增长一格。"],[354.5,357.73,118,"Nothing ever gets removed while the request is alive.","只要请求还在，就不会删除任何东西。"],[358.08,360.67,118,"The formula in the box is the one to remember.","框里的公式是需要记住的。"],[361.02,368.69,118,"KV bytes per token equals two, times layers, times KV heads, times head dimension, times bytes per number.","每个 token 的 KV 字节数等于二，乘以层数，乘以 KV 头数，乘以头维度，再乘以每个数的字节数。"],[369.04,379.24,118,"For OPT-13B, that's about eight hundred kilobytes per token, so a single two-thousand-forty-eight-token request needs about one point six gigabytes.","对 OPT-13B 来说，每个 token 约 800 KB，所以一个两千零四十八 token 的请求就需要约 1.6 GB。"],[379.59,388.02,118,"Now the key sentence in red: with dozens of requests running at once, it's the cache, not the weights, that limits the batch size.","现在看红色的关键句：当几十个请求同时运行时，限制 batch 大小的是缓存，而不是权重。"],[388.37,392.75,118,"The weights are shared by all requests; the cache is per request.","权重被所有请求共享，而缓存是每个请求各自一份。"],[393.1,400.84,118,"So if we want to serve more users per GPU, we need to manage the KV cache much more cleverly.","所以，如果想让每张 GPU 服务更多用户，就需要更聪明地管理 KV 缓存。"],[402.09,403.43,119,"What can we do about it?","我们能做些什么呢？"],[403.78,405.02,119,"Look at the problem first.","先看问题。"],[405.37,414.72,119,"For a LLaMA-70B-class model with four K context and a batch of thirty-two, the KV cache alone can be around forty gigabytes.","对一个 LLaMA-70B 级别的模型，上下文 4K、batch 为三十二时，光 KV 缓存就可能约 40 GB。"],[415.07,418.42,119,"That's as much as many GPUs have in total.","这相当于很多 GPU 的全部显存。"],[418.77,421.17,119,"There are two kinds of solutions on this slide.","这一页上有两类解决方案。"],[421.52,426.71,119,"The first kind makes each token's cache smaller, by changing the architecture.","第一类通过改变架构，让每个 token 的缓存变小。"],[427.06,437.58,119,"That's GQA, which shares KV heads across groups of query heads, used in LLaMA-2 and 3, Mistral and Qwen2.","也就是 GQA，让一组 query 头共享 KV 头，LLaMA-2 和 3、Mistral 和 Qwen2 都在用。"],[437.93,445.92,119,"Then MQA, with a single KV head, and MLA from DeepSeek, which stores a compressed low-rank latent.","还有只用一个 KV 头的 MQA，以及 DeepSeek 的 MLA，它存储的是压缩后的低秩隐向量。"],[446.27,449.82,119,"You saw all three in Part two, and now you see why they matter.","这三种你们在第二部分都见过，现在你们明白它们为什么重要了。"],[450.17,455.49,119,"The second kind doesn't change the model at all, but manages the memory better.","第二类完全不改模型，而是更好地管理显存。"],[455.84,462.25,119,"That's PagedAttention, the core of vLLM, which borrows an idea from operating systems.","这就是 PagedAttention，vLLM 的核心，它借鉴了操作系统的思想。"],[462.6,463.75,119,"Let's look at it.","我们来看看。"],[465.0,471.96,120,"PagedAttention, from Kwon and colleagues at Berkeley, borrows virtual memory from operating systems.","PagedAttention 由伯克利的 Kwon 等人提出，它借鉴了操作系统中的虚拟内存。"],[472.31,479.0,120,"Top left is the old way: each request gets one contiguous chunk, reserved for the maximum possible length.","左上角是旧方法：每个请求分到一整块连续的显存，按最大可能长度预留。"],[479.35,484.71,120,"Most of it stays empty, and that's where the sixty to eighty percent waste comes from.","其中大部分都空着，这就是百分之六十到八十浪费的来源。"],[485.06,492.14,120,"PagedAttention instead cuts the KV cache into small fixed-size blocks, here four tokens each.","PagedAttention 则把 KV 缓存切成固定大小的小块，这里每块四个 token。"],[492.49,499.35,120,"Request A's text, Four score and seven years ago our fathers brought forth, fills logical blocks zero, one and two.","请求 A 的文本 Four score and seven years ago our fathers brought forth 填满了逻辑块零、一和二。"],[499.7,507.24,120,"A block table maps each logical block to any free physical block on the GPU: zero goes to seven, one to one, and two to three.","块表把每个逻辑块映射到 GPU 上任意空闲的物理块：零映射到七，一映射到一，二映射到三。"],[507.59,511.86,120,"They don't need to be contiguous, just like pages in an operating system.","它们不需要连续，就像操作系统中的内存页一样。"],[512.21,520.33,120,"New blocks are allocated only when needed, so the only waste is the unfilled part of the last block, under four percent.","新块只在需要时才分配，所以唯一的浪费是最后一块中没填满的部分，不到百分之四。"],[520.68,522.34,120,"There's a bonus on the right.","右边还有一个额外的好处。"],[522.69,531.11,120,"Two requests or two samples that share the same prompt can point to the same physical block, tracked with a reference count.","共享同一提示的两个请求或两个样本，可以指向同一个物理块，用引用计数来跟踪。"],[531.46,534.28,120,"And they copy it only when they diverge.","只有在它们分叉时才复制。"],[534.63,539.97,120,"The result was two to four times higher throughput than earlier serving systems.","结果是吞吐量比之前的推理服务系统高两到四倍。"]]},{"n":9,"title":"Speculative Decoding: Draft, Verify, Stay Exact","blurb":"A small model drafts several tokens and the big model verifies them in one pass; a worked example of rejection sampling shows why it is faster yet exact.","file":"lecture11_part9.mp4","poster":"lecture11_part9.jpg","duration":825.5,"first":121,"last":137,"slides":[{"n":121,"title":"5.3 Speculative Decoding","t":0.8},{"n":122,"title":"Speculative Decoding","t":30.39},{"n":123,"title":"Speculative Sampling: Easy vs. Hard Tokens","t":97.36},{"n":124,"title":"Speculative Sampling: Use Parallel Verification","t":141.66},{"n":125,"title":"Speculative Decoding in Action","t":198.47},{"n":126,"title":"Why It Is Faster — and Why It Is Exact","t":274.36},{"n":127,"title":"Speculative Sampling - Algorithm","t":348.08},{"n":128,"title":"Speculative Sampling - Algorithm","t":398.11},{"n":129,"title":"Speculative Sampling - Algorithm","t":434.97},{"n":130,"title":"Speculative Sampling - Rejection Sampling","t":468.39},{"n":131,"title":"Speculative Sampling - Rejection Sampling","t":512.74},{"n":132,"title":"Speculative Sampling - Rejection Sampling","t":547.04},{"n":133,"title":"Speculative Sampling - Rejection Sampling","t":580.37},{"n":134,"title":"Speculative Sampling - Rejection Sampling","t":611.55},{"n":135,"title":"Speculative Sampling - #tokens generated in one pass","t":667.72},{"n":136,"title":"Speculative Sampling - Wall Time","t":708.81},{"n":137,"title":"Speculative Sampling - Wall Time","t":752.5}],"sents":[[0.8,6.28,121,"PagedAttention made memory use efficient, so we can batch many requests together.","PagedAttention 让显存使用变得高效，于是我们可以把很多请求放在一起批处理。"],[6.63,13.01,121,"But each single request is still slow, because the big model generates one token per forward pass.","但每个单独的请求仍然很慢，因为大模型每次前向传播只生成一个 token。"],[13.36,20.6,121,"Speculative decoding attacks that directly: guess several tokens cheaply, then let the big model check them all in one pass.","推测解码直接解决这个问题：先便宜地猜几个 token，再让大模型一次性把它们全部检查一遍。"],[20.95,28.99,121,"And the remarkable part is that it gives exactly the same output distribution as the big model, so there's no loss in quality.","了不起的是，它给出的输出分布与大模型完全相同，所以质量没有任何损失。"],[30.24,32.38,122,"Here's the whole idea on one slide.","这一页概括了整个思想。"],[32.73,42.69,122,"It was proposed independently by Leviathan and colleagues at Google, and by Chen and colleagues at DeepMind, both in two thousand twenty-three.","它由谷歌的 Leviathan 等人和 DeepMind 的 Chen 等人分别独立提出，都在 2023 年。"],[43.04,51.28,122,"The problem: autoregressive decoding produces one token per forward pass of the large model, and each pass is memory-bound.","问题在于：自回归解码时，大模型每次前向传播只产生一个 token，而每次传播都受限于内存。"],[51.63,58.03,122,"The idea: take a small, fast draft model, and let it propose K tokens, one after another.","思路是：用一个小而快的草稿模型，让它一个接一个地提出 K 个 token。"],[58.38,63.19,122,"Then run the large target model once on all K tokens in parallel, to check them.","然后让大的目标模型对这 K 个 token 并行地运行一次，来检查它们。"],[63.54,72.48,122,"Accept the ones the target model agrees with, and at the first disagreement, reject and resample from a corrected distribution.","接受目标模型认可的 token，在第一个不一致处拒绝，并从修正后的分布中重新采样。"],[72.83,82.56,122,"The result is typically a two to three times speedup, with no quality loss; it's mathematically equivalent to sampling from the big model.","结果通常是二到三倍的加速，且没有质量损失；它在数学上等价于从大模型采样。"],[82.91,93.17,122,"Newer variants like Medusa, EAGLE and lookahead decoding drop the separate draft model, and predict multiple tokens from the big model itself.","Medusa、EAGLE 和 lookahead decoding 等较新的变体去掉了单独的草稿模型，直接从大模型本身预测多个 token。"],[93.52,95.96,122,"Let's build up the intuition step by step.","我们一步一步建立直觉。"],[97.21,101.48,123,"Key idea number one: not all tokens are equally hard.","关键思想一：并不是所有 token 都一样难。"],[101.83,106.55,123,"Take the sentence: Geoffrey Hinton did his PhD at the University.","看这句话：Geoffrey Hinton did his PhD at the University。"],[106.9,111.89,123,"Predicting the next word, of, is trivially easy. Any small model can do it.","预测下一个词 of 非常容易，任何小模型都能做到。"],[112.24,119.62,123,"Using a one-hundred-billion-parameter model for that is like hiring a professor to tell you what comes after thank.","用一个一千亿参数的模型来做这件事，就像请一位教授来告诉你 thank 后面接什么。"],[119.97,125.15,123,"But the word after University of is Edinburgh, which requires real world knowledge.","但 University of 后面的词是 Edinburgh，这需要真正的世界知识。"],[125.5,127.29,123,"That's where you need the big model.","这时你才需要大模型。"],[127.64,133.71,123,"So the dream is: let a small model handle the easy tokens, and only use the big model for the hard ones.","所以理想情况是：让小模型处理简单的 token，只在难的 token 上用大模型。"],[134.06,137.85,123,"The problem is that we don't know in advance which tokens are easy.","问题是，我们事先不知道哪些 token 是简单的。"],[138.2,140.26,123,"That's where key idea two comes in.","这就需要关键思想二了。"],[141.51,145.46,124,"Key idea number two: a Transformer can check many tokens at once.","关键思想二：Transformer 可以一次检查很多个 token。"],[145.81,156.77,124,"If you give the big model a whole sequence, at the University of Toronto, it computes the probability of every position in a single forward pass, exactly as in training.","如果你把整个序列 at the University of Toronto 交给大模型，它会在一次前向传播中算出每个位置的概率，和训练时完全一样。"],[157.12,163.49,124,"And because decoding is memory-bound, checking five tokens costs about the same wall-clock time as generating one.","而且因为解码受限于内存，检查五个 token 的实际耗时和生成一个差不多。"],[163.84,168.16,124,"So suppose the small model guessed: at the University of Toronto.","假设小模型猜的是：at the University of Toronto。"],[168.51,173.87,124,"The big model reads it all at once and sees that at the University of is fine.","大模型一次读完，发现 at the University of 没有问题。"],[174.22,181.95,124,"But it assigns a low probability to Toronto, because it knows Hinton did his PhD at Edinburgh.","但它给 Toronto 的概率很低，因为它知道 Hinton 是在 Edinburgh 读的博士。"],[182.3,186.39,124,"So we keep the good prefix and fix only the wrong token.","所以我们保留正确的前缀，只修正那个错误的 token。"],[186.74,192.66,124,"Put the two ideas together: the small model drafts quickly, and the big model verifies in parallel.","把两个思想结合起来：小模型快速起草，大模型并行验证。"],[193.01,197.07,124,"Now let's see the exact rule for accepting or rejecting.","现在我们来看接受或拒绝的具体规则。"],[198.32,202.68,125,"Let's run a full worked example, with the prefix My.","我们来完整地演算一个例子，前缀是 My。"],[203.03,207.43,125,"The small draft model p proposes four tokens, one at a time.","小的草稿模型 p 一个接一个地提出四个 token。"],[207.78,215.67,125,"Dogs with probability zero point eight, love with zero point seven, chasing with zero point nine, and after with zero point eight.","dogs 的概率是 0.8，love 是 0.7，chasing 是 0.9，after 是 0.8。"],[216.02,217.88,125,"That's four cheap forward passes.","这是四次廉价的前向传播。"],[218.23,227.77,125,"Then the large target model q scores all four positions in one forward pass: zero point nine, zero point eight, zero point eight, and zero point three.","然后大的目标模型 q 在一次前向传播中给四个位置打分：0.9、0.8、0.8 和 0.3。"],[228.12,234.29,125,"Now compare. For dogs and love, q is at least p, so we accept immediately.","现在来比较。对 dogs 和 love，q 不小于 p，所以直接接受。"],[234.64,244.62,125,"For chasing, q is zero point eight and p is zero point nine, so we accept with probability q over p, about zero point eight nine.","对 chasing，q 是 0.8，p 是 0.9，所以以 q 除以 p 的概率接受，约为 0.89。"],[244.97,254.97,125,"For after, q is only zero point three against p's zero point eight, so we'd accept with probability zero point three eight, and here it's rejected.","对 after，q 只有 0.3，而 p 是 0.8，所以接受概率是 0.38，这里它被拒绝了。"],[255.32,264.36,125,"Instead, we resample that position from a corrected distribution, the normalized max of zero and q minus p, and we get toys, shown in red.","于是我们从修正后的分布，也就是 max(0, q 减 p) 归一化后的分布中，对这个位置重新采样，得到红色的 toys。"],[264.71,272.96,125,"Result: four new tokens, dogs love chasing toys, for four cheap passes and one big pass, instead of four big passes.","结果：用四次廉价传播加一次大模型传播，得到了四个新 token：dogs love chasing toys，而不是四次大模型传播。"],[274.21,277.34,126,"Let's summarize why this is both faster and exact.","我们来总结一下，为什么它既更快又精确。"],[277.69,281.76,126,"The timeline at the top compares wall-clock time for five tokens.","上方的时间线比较了生成五个 token 的实际耗时。"],[282.11,284.85,126,"Standard decoding needs five large passes.","标准解码需要五次大模型传播。"],[285.2,292.52,126,"Speculative decoding needs four tiny passes and one large check, which typically gives a two to three times speedup.","推测解码只需四次小模型传播加一次大模型检查，通常能带来二到三倍的加速。"],[292.87,300.73,126,"Why faster? Because decoding is memory-bound, one pass of the big model costs about the same whether it processes one token or five.","为什么更快？因为解码受限于内存，大模型一次传播处理一个 token 还是五个 token，耗时差不多。"],[301.08,306.34,126,"Easy tokens like of and the are usually guessed correctly by the small model.","像 of 和 the 这样的简单 token，小模型通常都能猜对。"],[306.69,314.42,126,"So the speedup grows with the acceptance rate: the better the draft model matches the target, the more tokens per big pass.","所以加速比随接受率增长：草稿模型与目标模型越匹配，每次大模型传播得到的 token 越多。"],[314.77,322.6,126,"Why lossless? The acceptance rule is: accept token x with probability min of one and q over p.","为什么无损？接受规则是：以 min(1, q/p) 的概率接受 token x。"],[322.95,328.17,126,"If it's rejected, sample from the normalized max of zero and q minus p.","如果被拒绝，就从 max(0, q 减 p) 归一化后的分布中采样。"],[328.52,333.97,126,"You can prove that these two steps together produce exactly the distribution q.","可以证明，这两步合起来恰好得到分布 q。"],[334.32,339.85,126,"So the output looks statistically identical to sampling from the big model alone.","所以输出在统计上与只用大模型采样完全相同。"],[340.2,346.68,126,"DeepSeek-V3's multi-token prediction can also be used in this way, as a built-in drafter.","DeepSeek-V3 的多 token 预测也可以这样使用，充当内置的草稿模型。"],[347.93,354.32,127,"Now let's go through the algorithm more formally, following a nice example from a popular tutorial.","现在我们更形式化地过一遍算法，沿用一个热门教程中的好例子。"],[354.67,365.76,127,"The draft model M-p could be Llama-2-7B-chat, and the target model M-q could be Llama-2-70B-chat.","草稿模型 M-p 可以是 Llama-2-7B-chat，目标模型 M-q 可以是 Llama-2-70B-chat。"],[366.11,370.12,127,"Same family, same tokenizer, but ten times different in size.","同一个家族，同一个分词器，但规模相差十倍。"],[370.47,375.74,127,"We start from a prefix p-f, and choose K equal to five.","我们从前缀 pf 开始，取 K 等于五。"],[376.09,380.99,127,"Step one: run the draft model autoregressively for K steps.","第一步：让草稿模型自回归地运行 K 步。"],[381.34,393.49,127,"It produces distribution p-one from the prefix and samples x-one, then p-two from the prefix plus x-one and samples x-two, and so on until x-five.","它从前缀得到分布 p1 并采样 x1，再从前缀加 x1 得到 p2 并采样 x2，依此类推直到 x5。"],[393.84,396.71,127,"These are five cheap passes of the small model.","这是小模型的五次廉价传播。"],[397.96,403.77,128,"Step two: run the target model once, on the prefix plus all five drafted tokens.","第二步：在前缀加上全部五个草稿 token 上，运行一次目标模型。"],[404.12,411.29,128,"In one forward pass, it gives us q-one through q-six: the big model's distribution at every position.","一次前向传播就给出 q1 到 q6：大模型在每个位置上的分布。"],[411.64,414.01,128,"Notice there are six, not five.","注意，这里是六个，而不是五个。"],[414.36,420.98,128,"The last one, q-six, is the distribution for the token after x-five, which we get for free.","最后一个 q6 是 x5 之后那个 token 的分布，我们白白得到了它。"],[421.33,429.44,128,"So after this step we have, for each drafted token, both the small model's probability p and the big model's probability q.","所以这一步之后，对每个草稿 token，我们都同时有小模型的概率 p 和大模型的概率 q。"],[429.79,433.57,128,"That's all we need for the accept or reject decision.","这就是做接受或拒绝决定所需的全部信息。"],[434.82,437.43,129,"Here are the actual numbers for our example.","这是我们例子中的具体数字。"],[437.78,441.59,129,"The draft model proposed: dogs love chasing after cars.","草稿模型提出的是：dogs love chasing after cars。"],[441.94,448.27,129,"Its p values are zero point eight, zero point seven, zero point nine, zero point eight, and zero point seven.","它的 p 值分别是 0.8、0.7、0.9、0.8 和 0.7。"],[448.62,457.82,129,"The target model's q values for those same tokens are zero point nine, zero point eight, zero point eight, zero point three, and zero point eight.","目标模型对同样这些 token 给出的 q 值是 0.9、0.8、0.8、0.3 和 0.8。"],[458.17,462.45,129,"Before moving on, take a moment and guess: which tokens will be accepted?","在继续之前，先花点时间猜一猜：哪些 token 会被接受？"],[462.8,466.99,129,"Look especially at after, where the two models disagree strongly.","尤其注意 after，两个模型在这里分歧很大。"],[468.24,470.01,130,"The rule has two cases.","规则分两种情况。"],[470.36,479.33,130,"Case one: if q of x is at least p of x, the big model likes this token at least as much as the small model did, so we accept it for sure.","情况一：如果 q(x) 不小于 p(x)，说明大模型对这个 token 的偏好不低于小模型，所以一定接受。"],[479.68,488.52,130,"Case two: if q is less than p, the small model was over-confident, so we accept with probability q over p.","情况二：如果 q 小于 p，说明小模型过于自信，所以以 q/p 的概率接受。"],[488.87,489.8,130,"Let's apply it.","我们来应用一下。"],[490.15,495.24,130,"Dogs: q is zero point nine and p is zero point eight, so accept.","dogs：q 是 0.9，p 是 0.8，接受。"],[495.59,499.95,130,"Love: zero point eight versus zero point seven, accept.","love：0.8 对 0.7，接受。"],[500.3,505.6,130,"Chasing: q is zero point eight and p is zero point nine, so this is case two.","chasing：q 是 0.8，p 是 0.9，所以属于情况二。"],[505.95,511.34,130,"We accept it with probability zero point eight over zero point nine, about eighty-nine percent.","我们以 0.8 除以 0.9 的概率接受它，大约百分之八十九。"],[512.59,517.92,131,"For chasing, an eighty-nine percent chance is high, so most of the time we'll accept it.","对 chasing 来说，百分之八十九的概率很高，所以大多数时候我们会接受它。"],[518.27,527.81,131,"In practice, we draw a uniform random number between zero and one, and if it's below zero point eight nine, we keep the token.","实际操作中，我们在零到一之间抽一个均匀随机数，如果它小于 0.89，就保留这个 token。"],[528.16,530.45,131,"Notice the intuition behind case two.","注意情况二背后的直觉。"],[530.8,536.54,131,"The small model was a bit too sure about chasing, but the big model still finds it quite likely.","小模型对 chasing 有点过于自信，但大模型仍然认为它相当可能。"],[536.89,545.64,131,"So we accept it most of the time, and the occasional rejection exactly corrects for the small model's over-confidence.","所以我们大多数时候接受它，而偶尔的拒绝恰好纠正了小模型的过度自信。"],[546.89,548.16,132,"Now look at after.","现在看 after。"],[548.51,553.41,132,"The draft model gave it zero point eight, but the big model only zero point three.","草稿模型给它 0.8，而大模型只给 0.3。"],[553.76,560.53,132,"So the acceptance probability is zero point three over zero point eight, about thirty-eight percent.","所以接受概率是 0.3 除以 0.8，约百分之三十八。"],[560.88,562.65,132,"Most likely, we'll reject it.","最有可能的是，我们会拒绝它。"],[563.0,569.71,132,"And here's an important detail: once a token is rejected, everything after it is thrown away too.","这里有一个重要细节：一旦某个 token 被拒绝，它之后的所有 token 也都被丢弃。"],[570.06,575.9,132,"Cars was generated assuming after came before it, so it's no longer valid.","cars 是在假定前面是 after 的情况下生成的，所以它不再有效。"],[576.25,578.97,132,"We stop checking at the first rejection.","在第一次拒绝处，我们就停止检查。"],[580.22,585.02,133,"So we've rejected after. What do we put in position four instead?","我们拒绝了 after。那第四个位置放什么呢？"],[585.37,594.17,133,"We don't need to call the big model again, because we already have its full distribution q-four at that position, from the single verification pass.","我们不需要再调用大模型，因为在那一次验证传播中，我们已经得到了它在这个位置上的完整分布 q4。"],[594.52,599.03,133,"So we can sample a replacement token from the big model's distribution there.","所以我们可以从大模型在这里的分布中采样一个替代 token。"],[599.38,605.31,133,"But there's one subtlety: if we sample directly from q-four, the result would be slightly biased.","但有一个微妙之处：如果直接从 q4 采样，结果会有轻微偏差。"],[605.66,610.15,133,"The next slide explains why, and what to sample from instead.","下一页解释原因，以及应该从什么分布中采样。"],[611.4,612.87,134,"Here's the subtlety.","微妙之处在这里。"],[613.22,621.88,134,"We only reach this point when the draft token was rejected, and rejection happens more often where p was too high compared with q.","只有当草稿 token 被拒绝时我们才会走到这一步，而拒绝更常发生在 p 相对 q 过高的地方。"],[622.23,625.78,134,"So to correct for that, we don't sample from q itself.","所以为了纠正这一点，我们不直接从 q 采样。"],[626.13,634.37,134,"Instead, we sample from the adjusted distribution: q minus p, keeping only the positive part, then renormalized.","而是从调整后的分布中采样：q 减 p，只保留正的部分，再重新归一化。"],[634.72,639.31,134,"Look at the picture. The red curve is p, and the orange curve is q.","看这张图。红色曲线是 p，橙色曲线是 q。"],[639.66,643.3,134,"The shaded region is where q is above p.","阴影区域就是 q 高于 p 的地方。"],[643.65,650.29,134,"These are exactly the tokens the draft model under-proposed, so the correction puts its probability mass there.","这些正是草稿模型提议得不够的 token，所以修正把概率质量放在这里。"],[650.64,660.45,134,"Accepting with probability min of one and q over p, and otherwise sampling from the positive part of q minus p, gives exactly the distribution q.","以 min(1, q/p) 的概率接受，否则从 q 减 p 的正部分中采样，合起来恰好得到分布 q。"],[660.8,666.32,134,"That's the mathematical guarantee: no loss in accuracy at all, only a gain in speed.","这就是数学上的保证：准确率毫无损失，只有速度上的提升。"],[667.57,670.47,135,"How many tokens do we get per big-model pass?","每次大模型传播能得到多少个 token？"],[670.82,674.81,135,"In the worst case, the very first draft token is rejected.","最坏情况下，第一个草稿 token 就被拒绝了。"],[675.16,682.48,135,"We still get one token, sampled from the corrected distribution, so we're never worse off than normal decoding in tokens per big pass.","我们仍然能从修正后的分布中采样得到一个 token，所以按每次大模型传播的 token 数算，永远不会比普通解码差。"],[682.83,686.31,135,"In the best case, all K draft tokens are accepted.","最好情况下，K 个草稿 token 全部被接受。"],[686.66,695.38,135,"And we also get a bonus token, sampled from the big model's distribution after the last position: the q-six we saw earlier.","而且我们还能额外得到一个 token，从大模型在最后位置之后的分布中采样，也就是之前看到的 q6。"],[695.73,699.0,135,"That's K plus one tokens for a single big pass.","这样一次大模型传播就得到 K 加一个 token。"],[699.35,707.41,135,"In our example, we got three accepted tokens plus one resampled token, so four tokens from one big pass.","在我们的例子中，有三个被接受的 token 加一个重新采样的 token，所以一次大模型传播得到四个 token。"],[708.66,711.1,136,"This picture shows wall-clock time.","这张图展示的是实际耗时。"],[711.45,719.64,136,"Yellow is processing the prompt, purple blocks are big-model passes, and the thin light-blue slivers are the cheap draft passes.","黄色是处理提示，紫色块是大模型传播，细细的浅蓝色条是廉价的草稿传播。"],[719.99,725.09,136,"The bottom row is ordinary decoding: one big pass per token, a long chain.","最下面一行是普通解码：每个 token 一次大模型传播，形成一条长链。"],[725.44,731.38,136,"With K equal to three and K equal to seven, many tokens are accepted per big pass.","当 K 等于三和 K 等于七时，每次大模型传播都有很多 token 被接受。"],[731.73,737.11,136,"So the number of big passes shrinks, and the whole generation finishes much sooner.","所以大模型传播的次数减少，整个生成过程提早很多完成。"],[737.46,739.83,136,"But larger K isn't always better.","但 K 并不是越大越好。"],[740.18,746.56,136,"If the draft model drifts away from the target, later tokens get rejected, and the draft work is wasted.","如果草稿模型偏离了目标模型，后面的 token 会被拒绝，草稿的工作就白费了。"],[746.91,751.1,136,"So K is a trade-off, which the next slide quantifies.","所以 K 是一个权衡，下一页会给出量化结果。"],[752.35,756.82,137,"Here are the empirical results from the two original papers.","这是两篇原始论文中的实验结果。"],[757.17,762.68,137,"DeepMind's table, top left, uses a seventy-billion-parameter Chinchilla target.","左上角是 DeepMind 的表格，目标模型是七百亿参数的 Chinchilla。"],[763.03,774.63,137,"Speculative sampling roughly halves the time per token, from fourteen point one milliseconds to around seven on summarization, and to five point seven on HumanEval.","推测采样把每个 token 的耗时大约减半：在摘要任务上从 14.1 毫秒降到 7 毫秒左右，在 HumanEval 上降到 5.7 毫秒。"],[774.98,778.92,137,"That's a speedup of one point nine to two point five times.","加速比是一点九到二点五倍。"],[779.27,785.97,137,"And look at the result column: the quality scores are essentially unchanged, just as the theory promised.","再看结果那一列：质量分数基本不变，和理论保证的一样。"],[786.32,789.02,137,"They recommend K around three to four.","他们推荐 K 取三到四左右。"],[789.37,798.39,137,"Google's table, bottom right, uses T5 models for translation and summarization, with gamma being K and alpha the acceptance rate.","右下角是谷歌的表格，用 T5 模型做翻译和摘要，gamma 就是 K，alpha 是接受率。"],[798.74,803.38,137,"Speedups range from about one point four to three point four times.","加速比大约在一点四倍到三点四倍之间。"],[803.73,810.22,137,"They're highest when the acceptance rate is high, for example with greedy decoding at temperature zero.","接受率高时加速最大，比如温度为零的贪心解码。"],[810.57,812.82,137,"Google recommends K from three to seven.","谷歌推荐 K 取三到七。"],[813.17,820.39,137,"The bottom line: speculative decoding reliably gives about two to three times speedup, for free in quality.","结论是：推测解码稳定地带来约二到三倍的加速，而且不损失质量。"],[820.74,823.63,137,"Today it's built into most serving frameworks.","如今它已内置在大多数推理服务框架中。"]]},{"n":10,"title":"FlashAttention: Tiling and the Online Softmax","blurb":"Attention is limited by memory traffic, not arithmetic: the GPU memory hierarchy, tiling into SRAM, the online softmax step by step, and why IO-awareness gives the speedup.","file":"lecture11_part10.mp4","poster":"lecture11_part10.jpg","duration":967.8,"first":138,"last":154,"slides":[{"n":138,"title":"5.4 FlashAttention","t":0.8},{"n":139,"title":"Standard Attention: The Problem Is Memory Traffic","t":29.61},{"n":140,"title":"FlashAttention: The Idea in One Slide","t":108.0},{"n":141,"title":"FlashAttention: GPU Memory Hierarchy","t":177.58},{"n":142,"title":"FlashAttention: Tile, Compute On-Chip, Never Store N × N","t":242.06},{"n":143,"title":"Online Softmax: Softmax Without Seeing the Whole Row","t":320.0},{"n":144,"title":"FlashAttention Step by Step: Notation","t":400.72},{"n":145,"title":"FlashAttention Step by Step: Split Blocks (1)","t":446.17},{"n":146,"title":"FlashAttention Step by Step: Split Blocks (2)","t":484.61},{"n":147,"title":"FlashAttention Step by Step: Softmax Reduction (1)","t":525.42},{"n":148,"title":"FlashAttention Step by Step: Softmax Reduction (2)","t":577.57},{"n":149,"title":"FlashAttention Step by Step: Softmax Reduction (3)","t":636.17},{"n":150,"title":"FlashAttention Step by Step: Numerically Stable Softmax","t":686.32},{"n":151,"title":"FlashAttention Step by Step: Putting It Together","t":741.07},{"n":152,"title":"Where the Speedup Comes From: IO, Not FLOPs","t":788.49},{"n":153,"title":"FlashAttention: Summary","t":853.13},{"n":154,"title":"Remark: Huawei Ascend Chips Are Bounded by Memory Bandwidth","t":913.12}],"sents":[[0.8,5.0,138,"Speculative decoding reduced the number of expensive passes.","推测解码减少了昂贵传播的次数。"],[5.35,9.32,138,"Now we zoom into a single pass, and into attention itself.","现在我们放大到单次传播，聚焦注意力本身。"],[9.67,13.51,138,"Remember the question from our contents slide: where does the time go?","还记得目录页上的那个问题吗：时间都花到哪里去了？"],[13.86,18.65,138,"For attention, the surprising answer is memory traffic, not arithmetic.","对注意力来说，令人意外的答案是内存读写，而不是算术运算。"],[19.0,24.17,138,"FlashAttention computes attention tile by tile inside fast on-chip memory.","FlashAttention 在快速的片上内存中逐块计算注意力。"],[24.52,28.21,138,"And it's probably the most important kernel in modern LLMs.","它可能是现代 LLM 中最重要的一个算子。"],[29.46,34.0,139,"To understand FlashAttention, you need a picture of the GPU's memory.","要理解 FlashAttention，你需要对 GPU 的内存有个整体印象。"],[34.35,46.38,139,"On the left is HBM, the GPU's main memory: big, forty to eighty gigabytes on an A100, but relatively slow, at about two terabytes per second.","左边是 HBM，GPU 的主存：容量大，A100 上有 40 到 80 GB，但相对较慢，约每秒 2 TB。"],[46.73,54.1,139,"On the right is SRAM, the on-chip memory: tiny, only around twenty megabytes, but roughly ten times faster.","右边是 SRAM，片上内存：很小，只有约 20 MB，但快了大约十倍。"],[54.45,57.38,139,"Now follow standard attention, step by step.","现在一步一步跟着标准注意力走一遍。"],[57.73,68.8,139,"One: read Q and K from HBM, compute S equals Q times K-transpose, and write the N by N matrix S back to HBM.","第一步：从 HBM 读取 Q 和 K，计算 S 等于 Q 乘 K 转置，再把 N 乘 N 的矩阵 S 写回 HBM。"],[69.15,75.83,139,"Two: read S back, compute the softmax, and write the N by N matrix P to HBM.","第二步：把 S 读回来，计算 softmax，再把 N 乘 N 的矩阵 P 写入 HBM。"],[76.18,80.67,139,"Three: read P and V, compute the output O, and write it.","第三步：读取 P 和 V，计算输出 O，再写回去。"],[81.02,83.01,139,"The problem is in the red box.","问题就在红框里。"],[83.36,91.13,139,"With eight thousand tokens, S and P each hold sixty-four million numbers per head, and we write them out and read them back.","在八千个 token 时，S 和 P 每个头各有六千四百万个数，我们要把它们写出去再读回来。"],[91.48,99.23,139,"Q, K and V are small, N by d. It's the N by N intermediates that cause the traffic.","Q、K、V 都很小，是 N 乘 d 的。造成大量读写的是那些 N 乘 N 的中间结果。"],[99.58,106.6,139,"And since GPUs compute much faster than they move memory, attention spends most of its time waiting on HBM.","而且 GPU 计算比搬运数据快得多，所以注意力的大部分时间都在等 HBM。"],[107.85,114.69,140,"Here's FlashAttention in one slide, from Tri Dao and colleagues at Stanford, in two thousand twenty-two.","这一页概括了 FlashAttention，由斯坦福的 Tri Dao 等人在 2022 年提出。"],[115.04,119.77,140,"The problem: standard attention is quadratic in both compute and memory.","问题：标准注意力在计算和显存上都是平方复杂度。"],[120.12,124.84,140,"The key insight: the real bottleneck is memory reads and writes, not compute.","关键洞见：真正的瓶颈是内存读写，而不是计算。"],[125.19,127.03,140,"The solution has two parts.","解决方案有两部分。"],[127.38,134.82,140,"Tiling: split Q, K and V into blocks small enough to fit in SRAM, and compute attention block by block.","分块：把 Q、K、V 切成足够小、能放进 SRAM 的块，逐块计算注意力。"],[135.17,147.08,140,"Kernel fusion: do the matrix multiply, the softmax and the multiplication by V all inside one GPU kernel, so the N by N matrix never has to be written to HBM.","算子融合：在一个 GPU 算子里完成矩阵乘、softmax 和乘以 V，这样 N 乘 N 的矩阵就永远不用写入 HBM。"],[147.43,154.67,140,"The tricky part is that softmax needs the whole row to normalize, and the online softmax trick solves that, as we'll see.","难点在于 softmax 需要整行才能归一化，而在线 softmax 技巧解决了这个问题，我们后面会看到。"],[155.02,161.56,140,"The result: two to four times faster, and memory drops from N squared to linear in N.","结果：速度快二到四倍，显存从 N 的平方降到 N 的线性。"],[161.91,165.5,140,"That's a big reason why context windows grew so quickly.","这是上下文窗口增长得如此之快的重要原因。"],[165.85,169.59,140,"And it's exact attention, not an approximation.","而且它是精确的注意力，不是近似。"],[169.94,176.18,140,"FlashAttention-2 and 3 refine it further for newer GPUs, like the H100.","FlashAttention-2 和 3 针对 H100 等更新的 GPU 做了进一步优化。"],[177.43,181.62,141,"This slide puts the hardware picture and the original algorithm together.","这一页把硬件图景和原始算法放在了一起。"],[181.97,185.12,141,"Look at the pyramid on the right, the memory hierarchy.","看右边的金字塔，也就是存储层次结构。"],[185.47,191.94,141,"At the top, GPU SRAM: about nineteen terabytes per second, but only twenty megabytes.","顶层是 GPU SRAM：约每秒 19 TB，但只有 20 MB。"],[192.29,200.31,141,"In the middle, GPU HBM: about one point five terabytes per second, and forty gigabytes on this A100.","中间是 GPU HBM：约每秒 1.5 TB，这块 A100 上有 40 GB。"],[200.66,205.15,141,"At the bottom, CPU main memory: huge, but much slower.","底层是 CPU 主存：容量巨大，但慢得多。"],[205.5,207.9,141,"Each level down is bigger and slower.","每往下一层，容量更大，速度更慢。"],[208.25,212.98,141,"Now look at Algorithm zero at the top, the standard attention implementation.","现在看上方的 Algorithm 0，也就是标准注意力的实现。"],[213.33,220.63,141,"The highlighted parts are every time it writes S or P to HBM and reads them back. Those are exactly the expensive trips.","高亮部分就是每次把 S 或 P 写入 HBM 再读回的地方。这些正是代价高昂的往返。"],[220.98,227.25,141,"And the small table at the bottom gives you the punchline in advance, which we'll come back to.","底部的小表格提前给出了结论，我们稍后会再回来看。"],[227.6,234.1,141,"FlashAttention actually does a bit more arithmetic, but far fewer HBM reads and writes, and it runs much faster.","FlashAttention 实际上多做了一点计算，但 HBM 读写少得多，运行也快得多。"],[234.45,240.66,141,"The design principle is IO-awareness: count the bytes you move, not just the FLOPs.","设计原则是 IO 感知：要计算搬运了多少字节，而不只是浮点运算次数。"],[241.91,243.23,142,"Tiling works like this.","分块是这样工作的。"],[243.58,253.3,142,"Split the queries into blocks Q-one, Q-two and Q-three, and the keys and values into blocks K-one V-one, K-two V-two, and K-three V-three.","把 query 切成 Q1、Q2、Q3 三块，把 key 和 value 切成 K1V1、K2V2、K3V3 三块。"],[253.65,259.15,142,"The N by N score matrix becomes a grid of tiles, S-one-one to S-three-three.","N 乘 N 的分数矩阵变成一个由 S11 到 S33 组成的网格。"],[259.5,264.73,142,"The crucial point is written under the grid: these scores are never stored in HBM.","关键一点写在网格下方：这些分数永远不会存入 HBM。"],[265.08,268.87,142,"Each tile lives briefly in SRAM, and disappears.","每个块只在 SRAM 中短暂存在，然后就消失了。"],[269.22,271.63,142,"Follow query block Q-one across the row.","沿着这一行跟踪 query 块 Q1。"],[271.98,280.43,142,"We load K-one and V-one, compute the tile S-one-one, and keep a running maximum m, a running sum l, and a partial output.","我们加载 K1 和 V1，计算块 S11，并保存一个运行最大值 m、一个运行总和 l 和一个部分输出。"],[280.78,288.65,142,"Then K-two and V-two arrive: we may find a new maximum, so we rescale the old sum and the old partial output, and add the new terms.","然后 K2 和 V2 到来：可能出现新的最大值，于是我们重新缩放旧的总和和旧的部分输出，再加上新的项。"],[289.0,296.17,142,"Same again for block three. After the last block, O-one is exact, and it's written to HBM exactly once.","第三块也一样。处理完最后一块后，O1 就是精确的，并且只写入 HBM 一次。"],[296.52,304.51,142,"So what changed? Memory is now linear in N, because there's no S or P in HBM.","那么变化在哪里？显存现在与 N 成线性关系，因为 HBM 里没有 S 或 P。"],[304.86,309.51,142,"Traffic is small, and the result is exactly the same as standard attention.","读写量很小，结果与标准注意力完全相同。"],[309.86,314.92,142,"And for the backward pass, it simply recomputes the S tiles instead of storing them.","在反向传播中，它直接重新计算 S 块，而不是把它们存起来。"],[315.27,318.6,142,"Recomputing is cheaper than reading from memory.","重新计算比从内存读取更便宜。"],[319.85,323.82,143,"The trick that makes tiling possible is the online softmax.","让分块成为可能的技巧是在线 softmax。"],[324.17,332.68,143,"Normally softmax needs the whole row, because you divide by the sum over all entries, and for numerical stability you also subtract the row max.","通常 softmax 需要整行，因为要除以所有元素的和，而且为了数值稳定，还要减去这一行的最大值。"],[333.03,336.01,143,"So how can we do it one block at a time?","那么，怎样才能一次只处理一块呢？"],[336.36,344.83,143,"Here's a tiny example. A row of four scores arrives in two blocks: first two and one, then four and three.","来看一个小例子。一行四个分数分两块到达：先是二和一，然后是四和三。"],[345.18,347.82,143,"After block one, the running max is two.","处理完第一块后，运行最大值是二。"],[348.17,356.12,143,"And the running sum is e to the zero plus e to the minus one, which is one point three six eight.","运行总和是 e 的零次方加 e 的负一次方，等于 1.368。"],[356.47,359.47,143,"When block two arrives, the new max is four.","当第二块到来时，新的最大值是四。"],[359.82,370.69,143,"So we rescale the old sum by e to the power two minus four, and add the new block's terms, e to the zero plus e to the minus one. That gives one point five five three.","于是我们把旧的总和乘以 e 的二减四次方，再加上新块的项，e 的零次方加 e 的负一次方，得到 1.553。"],[371.04,374.92,143,"Check: if you'd seen the whole row at once, the max is four.","验证一下：如果一次看到整行，最大值是四。"],[375.27,386.77,143,"And the sum is e to the minus two, plus e to the minus three, plus e to the zero, plus e to the minus one, which is also one point five five three. Identical.","总和是 e 的负二次方、负三次方、零次方和负一次方之和，同样是 1.553。完全一致。"],[387.12,390.07,143,"The formulas at the bottom are the general rule.","底部的公式是一般规则。"],[390.42,396.1,143,"Two numbers per row, the running max and the running sum, are enough to merge blocks exactly.","每行只需两个数，运行最大值和运行总和，就足以精确地合并各个块。"],[396.45,399.32,143,"And the partial output gets rescaled the same way.","部分输出也以同样的方式重新缩放。"],[400.57,407.71,144,"The next several slides walk through the actual FlashAttention algorithm from the paper, step by step, with a picture.","接下来几页会结合图示，一步一步讲解论文中实际的 FlashAttention 算法。"],[408.06,415.85,144,"Don't worry about memorizing it; the goal is to see that the ideas we just discussed map directly onto the pseudo-code.","不用担心要记住它；目的是让你看到我们刚才讨论的思想如何直接对应到伪代码上。"],[416.2,422.6,144,"First, the notation. Q, K and V are N by d matrices in HBM.","首先是符号。Q、K、V 是存放在 HBM 中的 N 乘 d 矩阵。"],[422.95,429.33,144,"S is the N by N score matrix in the middle, in purple, which we'll never fully materialize.","S 是中间紫色的 N 乘 N 分数矩阵，我们永远不会完整地把它算出来存下。"],[429.68,435.82,144,"O is the output, l is the running softmax sum for each row, and m is the running max for each row.","O 是输出，l 是每行 softmax 的运行总和，m 是每行的运行最大值。"],[436.17,439.01,144,"M is the size of the on-chip SRAM.","M 是片上 SRAM 的大小。"],[439.36,444.77,144,"The algorithm initializes O to zero, l to zero, and m to minus infinity.","算法把 O 初始化为零，l 初始化为零，m 初始化为负无穷。"],[446.02,449.37,145,"The first step is to split everything into blocks.","第一步是把所有东西切成块。"],[449.72,454.59,145,"The block sizes are chosen so that everything fits into SRAM of size M.","块的大小要选得让所有东西都能放进大小为 M 的 SRAM。"],[454.94,465.6,145,"The key and value block size, B-c, is about M over four d, and the query block size, B-r, is the minimum of that and d.","key 和 value 的块大小 Bc 约为 M 除以 4d，query 的块大小 Br 取它与 d 中的较小值。"],[465.95,473.19,145,"So Q is divided into T-r row blocks, and K and V into T-c column blocks.","于是 Q 被分成 Tr 个行块，K 和 V 被分成 Tc 个列块。"],[473.54,479.75,145,"O, l and m are split along with Q, because they're all per-row quantities.","O、l 和 m 跟着 Q 一起切分，因为它们都是按行计算的量。"],[480.1,483.21,145,"The dashed groupings in the picture show these blocks.","图中的虚线分组表示的就是这些块。"],[484.46,486.32,146,"Let's watch one tile in action.","我们来看一个块是怎么运作的。"],[486.67,491.82,146,"We pick one block of rows of Q, and one block of columns from K and V.","我们取 Q 的一个行块，以及 K 和 V 的一个列块。"],[492.17,498.48,146,"Following the red arrows, the Q block times the K block gives a small tile of S, the purple square.","顺着红色箭头，Q 块乘以 K 块得到 S 的一个小块，也就是那个紫色方块。"],[498.83,506.17,146,"After softmax-style exponentiation, it's multiplied by the V block, giving a contribution to the corresponding rows of O.","经过 softmax 式的指数运算后，再乘以 V 块，就得到对 O 中相应行的一个贡献。"],[506.52,513.03,146,"That contribution is then merged into the O stored in HBM, using l and m.","然后利用 l 和 m，把这个贡献合并到 HBM 中存储的 O 里。"],[513.38,519.06,146,"Notice the outer loop goes over K and V blocks, and the inner loop goes over Q blocks.","注意，外层循环遍历 K 和 V 块，内层循环遍历 Q 块。"],[519.41,524.02,146,"Only one small tile is ever in SRAM at a time.","SRAM 中任何时候都只有一个小块。"],[525.27,529.53,147,"Now the softmax reduction, the highlighted lines of the algorithm.","接下来是 softmax 归约，也就是算法中高亮的那几行。"],[529.88,537.34,147,"Inside each tile, on chip, we compute S-i-j equals Q-i times K-j transposed.","在每个块内部，在片上计算 Sij 等于 Qi 乘以 Kj 的转置。"],[537.69,548.37,147,"Then we compute the row-wise max of this tile, m-tilde, exponentiate the scores relative to it to get P-tilde, and compute the row-wise sum, l-tilde.","然后计算这个块的逐行最大值 m-tilde，以它为基准对分数取指数得到 P-tilde，再计算逐行总和 l-tilde。"],[548.72,551.76,147,"Then we merge with what we had before.","接着与之前的结果合并。"],[552.11,556.13,147,"The new max is the max of the old m and the tile's m-tilde.","新的最大值是旧 m 与这个块的 m-tilde 中的较大者。"],[556.48,562.72,147,"The new l is the old l and the tile's l-tilde, each rescaled to the new max, then added.","新的 l 是把旧 l 和这个块的 l-tilde 分别按新的最大值重新缩放后再相加。"],[563.07,569.62,147,"And we update O-i with the same rescaling, then write O, l and m back.","再用同样的缩放更新 Oi，然后把 O、l 和 m 写回去。"],[569.97,576.17,147,"This is exactly the online softmax from a few slides ago, now written for blocks.","这正是前几页讲的在线 softmax，只不过现在是按块来写的。"],[577.42,582.27,148,"Let's see why this works with formulas, for a single query row, Q-i.","我们用公式来看看，对单个 query 行 Qi，为什么这样可行。"],[582.62,585.7,148,"The top formula is just ordinary attention.","上面的公式就是普通的注意力。"],[586.05,599.81,148,"The output O-i is a weighted sum of all values, V-one to V-N, where each weight is e to the Q-i K-j transposed, divided by the sum over all positions.","输出 Oi 是所有 value，从 V1 到 VN 的加权和，每个权重是 e 的 Qi 乘 Kj 转置次方，再除以所有位置的总和。"],[600.16,604.27,148,"The problem is that denominator: it involves all N keys.","问题在于那个分母：它涉及全部 N 个 key。"],[604.62,606.82,148,"The bottom formula is the online version.","下面的公式是在线版本。"],[607.17,609.95,148,"Start with O-one, using only the first key.","从只用第一个 key 的 O1 开始。"],[610.3,621.22,148,"Then, for each new key j, take the previous output O-j-minus-one, and multiply it by the old denominator over the new denominator, which corrects the normalization.","然后对每个新的 key j，取上一步的输出 O(j-1)，乘以旧分母除以新分母，以修正归一化。"],[621.57,629.57,148,"Then add the new term, e to the Q-i K-j transposed, times V-j, over the new denominator.","再加上新的一项：e 的 Qi 乘 Kj 转置次方乘以 Vj，除以新分母。"],[629.92,634.77,148,"After processing all N keys, you get exactly the full softmax output.","处理完全部 N 个 key 之后，就得到与完整 softmax 完全相同的输出。"],[636.02,638.16,149,"This slide shows the algebra behind it.","这一页展示了背后的代数推导。"],[638.51,649.13,149,"Each term in the full output can be rewritten as the same term computed with a partial denominator, multiplied by a correction ratio: the partial denominator over the full one.","完整输出中的每一项，都可以改写成用部分分母计算的同一项，再乘以一个修正比例：部分分母除以完整分母。"],[649.48,652.9,149,"These ratios telescope, so we can update step by step.","这些比例可以逐项相消，所以我们能一步一步地更新。"],[653.25,660.14,149,"Written compactly at the bottom, with l-i-j as the running sum of exponentials up to position j.","底部是紧凑的写法，其中 lij 是到位置 j 为止的指数运行总和。"],[660.49,672.17,149,"O-j equals O-j-minus-one times l-j-minus-one over l-j, plus e to the S-i-j, times V-j, over l-j.","Oj 等于 O(j-1) 乘以 l(j-1) 除以 lj，再加上 e 的 Sij 次方乘以 Vj 除以 lj。"],[672.52,677.95,149,"And l-j is l-j-minus-one plus e to the S-i-j.","而 lj 等于 l(j-1) 加上 e 的 Sij 次方。"],[678.3,684.92,149,"So we only ever carry one output vector and one running sum per row. No N by N matrix needed.","所以每行只需维护一个输出向量和一个运行总和，根本不需要 N 乘 N 的矩阵。"],[686.17,689.86,150,"There's one more practical detail: numerical stability.","还有一个实际细节：数值稳定性。"],[690.21,697.27,150,"Exponentials of large scores overflow, so in practice softmax always subtracts the row max first.","大分数的指数会溢出，所以实践中 softmax 总是先减去这一行的最大值。"],[697.62,701.92,150,"The online version therefore also tracks a running max, m.","因此在线版本还要跟踪一个运行最大值 m。"],[702.27,703.5,150,"Look at the red box.","看红框。"],[703.85,709.42,150,"When a new score arrives, the new max is the max of the old max and the new score.","当一个新分数到来时，新的最大值是旧最大值与新分数中的较大者。"],[709.77,719.28,150,"The running sum l is the old sum, rescaled by e to the old max minus the new max, plus e to the new score minus the new max.","运行总和 l 等于旧总和乘以 e 的旧最大值减新最大值次方，再加上 e 的新分数减新最大值次方。"],[719.63,724.21,150,"And the output is rescaled the same way, and then the new value is added.","输出也以同样方式重新缩放，然后加上新的值。"],[724.56,731.15,150,"The red arrow links this update to the write steps of the algorithm, in the red box at the top.","红色箭头把这个更新与上方红框中算法的写回步骤联系起来。"],[731.5,739.67,150,"It's the same formula as the online softmax example, with the numbers two, one, four and three, that we did earlier.","这与我们之前用二、一、四、三这几个数做的在线 softmax 例子是同一个公式。"],[740.92,746.12,151,"This slide puts everything together, with the update rule connected to each memory block.","这一页把所有内容整合在一起，并把更新规则与每个存储块联系起来。"],[746.47,747.94,151,"Follow the dashed arrows.","顺着虚线箭头看。"],[748.29,753.1,151,"The inner loop runs down over the query rows, marked by the red arrow on the left.","内层循环沿着 query 的行往下走，由左边的红色箭头标出。"],[753.45,761.58,151,"For each row Q-i and each key-value block, we compute the increment to O, the new contribution, shown in the small box.","对每一行 Qi 和每个 key-value 块，我们计算 O 的增量，也就是新的贡献，显示在这个小框里。"],[761.93,770.71,151,"Then we combine it with the old O, old l and old m from HBM, using the update rule in the red box.","然后用红框中的更新规则，把它与 HBM 中旧的 O、l 和 m 结合起来。"],[771.06,775.0,151,"And we write the new O, l and m back.","再把新的 O、l 和 m 写回去。"],[775.35,781.85,151,"So the only things that live across iterations are O, l and m, all of size proportional to N.","所以在迭代之间保留下来的只有 O、l 和 m，它们的大小都与 N 成正比。"],[782.2,787.09,151,"Everything N by N exists only as small temporary tiles in SRAM.","所有 N 乘 N 的东西都只以小的临时块的形式存在于 SRAM 中。"],[788.34,789.82,152,"Does it actually pay off?","它真的有效吗？"],[790.17,798.96,152,"The evidence comes from Figure one of the FlashAttention paper: GPT-2 medium attention, forward plus backward, on an A100.","证据来自 FlashAttention 论文的图一：GPT-2 medium 的注意力，前向加反向，在 A100 上。"],[799.31,801.75,152,"Look at the three pairs of bars.","看这三组柱子。"],[802.1,812.84,152,"FLOPs: FlashAttention actually does more arithmetic, seventy-five point two billion versus sixty-six point six, because it recomputes attention scores in the backward pass.","浮点运算：FlashAttention 实际上做了更多计算，752 亿对 666 亿，因为它在反向传播中重新计算注意力分数。"],[813.19,822.28,152,"HBM reads and writes: forty point three gigabytes for standard attention, versus only four point four for FlashAttention, about nine times less.","HBM 读写：标准注意力是 40.3 GB，而 FlashAttention 只有 4.4 GB，大约少了九倍。"],[822.63,829.69,152,"Runtime: forty-one point seven milliseconds versus seven point three, about five point seven times faster.","运行时间：41.7 毫秒对 7.3 毫秒，大约快了 5.7 倍。"],[830.04,836.21,152,"This is the single most important lesson of FlashAttention, and maybe of this whole inference section.","这是 FlashAttention 最重要的一课，也许也是整个推理部分最重要的一课。"],[836.56,839.55,152,"More arithmetic, fewer bytes, faster.","更多的计算，更少的字节，更快的速度。"],[839.9,844.27,152,"On modern GPUs, moving data is the bottleneck, not computing.","在现代 GPU 上，瓶颈是搬运数据，而不是计算。"],[844.62,851.73,152,"Remember our opening question: where does the time go? Here's the clearest answer: it goes to bytes moved.","还记得我们开头的问题吗：时间都花到哪里去了？这就是最清楚的答案：花在搬运字节上。"],[852.98,855.32,153,"To summarize the algorithm in one picture.","用一张图来总结这个算法。"],[855.67,863.05,153,"The outer loop, in red, goes over blocks of K and V; the inner loop, in blue, goes over blocks of Q.","红色的外层循环遍历 K 和 V 的块；蓝色的内层循环遍历 Q 的块。"],[863.4,870.27,153,"Each block is copied into SRAM, the tile is computed on chip, and only the output is written back to HBM.","每个块被复制到 SRAM，在片上完成计算，只有输出被写回 HBM。"],[870.62,876.4,153,"Three words to remember: split blocks, update softmax, and IO complexity.","要记住三个词：分块、更新 softmax，以及 IO 复杂度。"],[876.75,885.12,153,"The number of HBM accesses is on the order of N squared d squared over M, where M is the SRAM size.","HBM 的访问次数是 N 平方乘 d 平方除以 M 的量级，其中 M 是 SRAM 的大小。"],[885.47,891.14,153,"Compare that with the order of N d plus N squared for standard attention.","与之相比，标准注意力是 N 乘 d 加 N 平方的量级。"],[891.49,898.13,153,"For typical head dimensions and SRAM sizes, that's many times fewer memory accesses.","对于典型的头维度和 SRAM 大小，这意味着内存访问次数少很多倍。"],[898.48,902.76,153,"And remember, the answer is exact, not approximate.","记住，结果是精确的，不是近似的。"],[903.11,911.72,153,"Today, FlashAttention or its descendants are used in virtually every serious training and inference framework.","如今，几乎每个正经的训练和推理框架都在使用 FlashAttention 或它的后继版本。"],[912.97,917.7,154,"A short remark that connects this to our own situation in China.","做一个简短的说明，把这些内容和我们在中国的实际情况联系起来。"],[918.05,925.29,154,"Huawei's Ascend NPUs, like the Ascend nine one zero in the picture, are increasingly used for training and serving LLMs here.","华为的昇腾 NPU，比如图中的昇腾 910，在国内越来越多地用于训练和部署大模型。"],[925.64,932.87,154,"Like GPUs, and arguably even more so, they tend to be bounded by memory bandwidth rather than raw compute.","和 GPU 一样，甚至可以说更甚，它们往往受限于内存带宽，而不是原始算力。"],[933.22,937.92,154,"So everything we just learned about IO-awareness applies directly.","所以我们刚学到的 IO 感知的思想可以直接用上。"],[938.27,948.62,154,"And it raises a research question: how should we design model architectures that are friendly to this hardware, rather than just copying designs tuned for NVIDIA GPUs?","这也引出了一个研究问题：我们应该如何设计对这种硬件友好的模型架构，而不是照搬为英伟达 GPU 调优的设计？"],[948.97,952.73,154,"That's hardware-software co-design, and it's a very active area.","这就是软硬件协同设计，是一个非常活跃的领域。"],[953.08,962.09,154,"And a small advertisement: my group has access to a large Ascend cluster, on the order of a thousand to ten thousand NPU chips.","再打个小广告：我们课题组可以使用一个大型昇腾集群，规模在一千到一万张 NPU 芯片的量级。"],[962.44,965.94,154,"If you're interested in working on this, please email me.","如果你有兴趣做这方面的工作，欢迎给我发邮件。"]]},{"n":11,"title":"Serving with vLLM and the Road Ahead","blurb":"How a real serving engine fits together: scheduler, continuous and ragged batching, memory sharing for sampling and beam search, preemption, then an outlook on the next 10x and group discussion.","file":"lecture11_part11.mp4","poster":"lecture11_part11.jpg","duration":848.0,"first":155,"last":168,"slides":[{"n":155,"title":"5.5 Serving Systems: vLLM","t":0.8},{"n":156,"title":"vLLM Architecture Overview","t":28.34},{"n":157,"title":"Static vs. Continuous Batching","t":93.79},{"n":158,"title":"Continuous Batching","t":168.0},{"n":159,"title":"Continuous Batching","t":220.23},{"n":160,"title":"Ragged Batching for Continuous Batching","t":266.43},{"n":161,"title":"Memory Sharing: Parallel Sampling","t":321.21},{"n":162,"title":"Memory Sharing: Beam Search","t":384.27},{"n":163,"title":"Preemption and Swapping","t":436.58},{"n":164,"title":"6 Outlook","t":510.47},{"n":165,"title":"Outlook (2026): Where the Next 10× Comes From","t":533.82},{"n":166,"title":"Future Remarks: Hybrid Efficiency","t":642.05},{"n":167,"title":"Group Discussions","t":696.36},{"n":168,"title":"Acknowledgement","t":755.1}],"sents":[[0.8,8.94,155,"We've now seen the building blocks: a smaller KV cache, paged memory, speculative decoding, and FlashAttention.","我们已经看过了各个组成部分：更小的 KV 缓存、分页内存、推测解码和 FlashAttention。"],[9.29,17.08,155,"The last sub-section shows how they come together in a real serving system, using vLLM as the example.","最后一个小节以 vLLM 为例，展示它们如何在一个真实的推理服务系统中组合在一起。"],[17.43,26.94,155,"The theme is an operating-system view of LLM serving: pages for memory, scheduling for batches, and sharing between requests.","主题是用操作系统的视角看 LLM 推理服务：用分页管理内存，用调度管理批次，并在请求之间共享。"],[28.19,38.5,156,"vLLM, from Berkeley, is one of the most widely used open-source serving engines, and it's a good mental model of how such systems are organized.","来自伯克利的 vLLM 是最广泛使用的开源推理引擎之一，也是理解这类系统如何组织的一个很好的心智模型。"],[38.85,40.47,156,"It has four main components.","它有四个主要组件。"],[40.82,46.76,156,"The scheduler decides, at every iteration, which requests run on the GPU.","调度器在每一次迭代中决定哪些请求在 GPU 上运行。"],[47.11,52.27,156,"It uses first-come-first-served with preemption, which we'll come back to.","它采用带抢占的先来先服务策略，我们稍后会再讲。"],[52.62,57.94,156,"The KV cache manager, or block manager, is the PagedAttention memory manager.","KV 缓存管理器，也叫块管理器，就是 PagedAttention 的内存管理器。"],[58.29,64.38,156,"It allocates and frees physical blocks, and keeps a block table for every active sequence.","它负责分配和释放物理块，并为每个活跃序列维护一张块表。"],[64.73,71.57,156,"The workers execute the model's forward pass on one or more GPUs, using PagedAttention kernels.","工作进程在一张或多张 GPU 上执行模型的前向传播，使用 PagedAttention 算子。"],[71.92,79.07,156,"And the tokenizer and sampler turn text into tokens, and pick the output tokens.","分词器和采样器负责把文本转成 token，并挑选输出的 token。"],[79.42,88.24,156,"If you've taken an operating systems course, this should look familiar: a scheduler, a memory manager with page tables, and processes.","如果你上过操作系统课，这些应该很眼熟：调度器、带页表的内存管理器，还有进程。"],[88.59,92.39,156,"Next, let's see how the scheduler batches requests.","接下来我们看看调度器如何对请求进行批处理。"],[93.64,100.11,157,"This picture shows the most important scheduling idea in LLM serving: continuous batching.","这张图展示了 LLM 推理服务中最重要的调度思想：连续批处理。"],[100.46,105.99,157,"Top: static batching. Four requests, A to D, start together in four slots.","上方是静态批处理。A 到 D 四个请求在四个槽位中同时开始。"],[106.34,109.83,157,"A finishes after three steps, and C after two.","A 在三步后结束，C 在两步后结束。"],[110.18,115.22,157,"But their slots sit idle until the longest request, B, finishes at step seven.","但它们的槽位一直闲置，直到最长的请求 B 在第七步结束。"],[115.57,119.29,157,"Only then can new requests E, F and G start.","只有到那时，新的请求 E、F、G 才能开始。"],[119.64,124.67,157,"Look at all the white idle cells: that's wasted GPU time, and new users are waiting.","看这些白色的空闲格子：这是浪费的 GPU 时间，而且新用户还在等待。"],[125.02,128.89,157,"Bottom: continuous batching, introduced by the Orca system.","下方是连续批处理，由 Orca 系统提出。"],[129.24,132.64,157,"The scheduler works per iteration, not per batch.","调度器按迭代工作，而不是按批次工作。"],[132.99,142.61,157,"As soon as A finishes, E takes its slot; as soon as C finishes, F starts; and when D finishes, G starts.","A 一结束，E 就占用它的槽位；C 一结束，F 就开始；D 结束时，G 开始。"],[142.96,146.32,157,"No idle slots, and new requests start immediately.","没有空闲槽位，新请求立即开始。"],[146.67,159.39,157,"The gain can be dramatic: an Anyscale benchmark reported up to twenty-three times higher throughput compared with static batching, combined with PagedAttention's memory management.","收益可能非常显著：Anyscale 的基准测试报告，结合 PagedAttention 的内存管理，吞吐量比静态批处理最高提升二十三倍。"],[159.74,166.6,157,"This works so well precisely because PagedAttention lets requests come and go without fragmenting memory.","它之所以效果这么好，正是因为 PagedAttention 让请求可以随进随出而不产生内存碎片。"],[167.85,172.74,158,"These figures from the Hugging Face blog show the same idea at the token level.","这些来自 Hugging Face 博客的图在 token 层面展示了同样的思想。"],[173.09,177.79,158,"On the left, batched generation: two prompts of different lengths are padded to the same length.","左边是批量生成：两个不同长度的提示被填充到相同长度。"],[178.14,184.03,158,"When one sequence finishes, it keeps producing end-of-sequence tokens while the other is still going.","当一个序列结束后，它会继续产生结束符 token，而另一个序列还在生成。"],[184.38,187.47,158,"That's marked in red as a waste of compute.","这被红色标注为计算浪费。"],[187.82,193.53,158,"On the right, dynamic batching: when one request finishes, a new prompt is inserted immediately.","右边是动态批处理：一个请求结束后，立即插入一个新的提示。"],[193.88,196.85,158,"The catch, also marked in red, is padding.","问题在于填充，同样用红色标出。"],[197.2,204.5,158,"The new prompt and the old sequence have very different lengths, so naive batching needs a lot of pad tokens.","新提示和旧序列的长度相差很大，所以简单的批处理需要大量填充 token。"],[204.85,213.51,158,"So continuous batching has clear benefits: no batch bubble from waiting for the slowest request, higher GPU utilization, and lower average latency.","所以连续批处理有明显的好处：没有等待最慢请求造成的批次气泡，GPU 利用率更高，平均延迟更低。"],[213.86,218.83,158,"But we need a way to avoid that padding, which is what ragged batching solves.","但我们需要一种方法来避免填充，这正是 ragged batching，不规则批处理，要解决的问题。"],[220.08,222.12,159,"To restate the contrast once more.","再来重申一下两者的对比。"],[222.47,230.49,159,"In static batching, the batch is fixed until every request in it is done, so short requests wait for long ones.","在静态批处理中，批次一直固定，直到其中每个请求都完成，所以短请求要等长请求。"],[230.84,241.0,159,"In continuous, iteration-level batching, after every decode step the scheduler checks which requests have finished, removes them, and inserts new ones.","在连续的、迭代级别的批处理中，每个解码步之后，调度器检查哪些请求已完成，移除它们并插入新的请求。"],[241.35,245.07,159,"Each request enters and exits the batch independently.","每个请求独立地进入和退出批次。"],[245.42,246.97,159,"Think of it like a restaurant.","可以把它想象成一家餐厅。"],[247.32,254.05,159,"Static batching seats a whole group, and won't seat anyone else at the table until the slowest eater is finished.","静态批处理让一整桌客人入座，直到吃得最慢的人吃完，才让别人坐这张桌子。"],[254.4,259.42,159,"Continuous batching gives each seat to the next customer as soon as someone leaves.","连续批处理则是一有人离开，就把座位让给下一位顾客。"],[259.77,265.03,159,"The kitchen, which is the GPU, stays busy, and customers wait less.","厨房，也就是 GPU，一直保持忙碌，顾客等待的时间也更短。"],[266.28,269.07,160,"Ragged batching removes the padding problem.","不规则批处理消除了填充问题。"],[269.42,278.16,160,"Instead of stacking prompts into a rectangle with pad tokens, we simply concatenate them into one long sequence, as on the left.","我们不再用填充 token 把提示堆成一个矩形，而是像左边那样，直接把它们拼接成一个长序列。"],[278.51,285.92,160,"Prompt zero, Who ate the pie, is followed directly by prompt one, I am sure this project.","提示零 Who ate the pie 后面直接接着提示一 I am sure this project。"],[286.27,293.13,160,"Then, as on the right, we use an attention mask, so that each prompt only attends to its own tokens.","然后像右边那样，用一个注意力掩码，让每个提示只关注自己的 token。"],[293.48,299.87,160,"The green cells are allowed attention, and you can see two separate triangles, one per prompt.","绿色格子表示允许的注意力，你可以看到两个独立的三角形，每个提示一个。"],[300.22,306.44,160,"The off-diagonal blocks are all false: tokens of prompt zero never interact with tokens of prompt one.","非对角线上的块全是 false：提示零的 token 与提示一的 token 永远不会交互。"],[306.79,311.71,160,"No padding, no wasted compute, and the GPU sees one big batch.","没有填充，没有浪费的计算，GPU 看到的是一个大批次。"],[312.06,319.81,160,"Combined with paged KV memory, this is how modern engines keep GPUs full, with requests of very different lengths.","结合分页的 KV 内存，现代推理引擎就是这样在请求长度差异很大的情况下让 GPU 保持满载的。"],[321.06,325.83,161,"Paging has another big benefit beyond less fragmentation: memory sharing.","除了减少碎片，分页还有另一个大好处：内存共享。"],[326.18,331.79,161,"A common use case is generating several completions for the same prompt, say four.","一个常见的场景是为同一个提示生成多个补全，比如四个。"],[332.14,342.16,161,"You see this when a chatbot offers multiple drafts, or in RL post-training, as in Lecture six, where we sample many responses per prompt.","当聊天机器人提供多个草稿时会遇到这种情况，在第六讲的强化学习后训练中也是如此，我们会为每个提示采样很多回答。"],[342.51,350.45,161,"The naive approach copies the prompt's KV cache four times: four identical copies, four times the memory.","简单的做法是把提示的 KV 缓存复制四份：四份一模一样的副本，四倍的显存。"],[350.8,357.77,161,"With PagedAttention, all four sequences simply point their block tables at the same physical blocks for the prompt.","用 PagedAttention，四个序列只需让各自的块表指向提示所在的同一批物理块。"],[358.12,362.3,161,"And a reference counter records how many sequences share each block.","再用一个引用计数器记录每个块被多少个序列共享。"],[362.65,367.12,161,"When the sequences start to diverge, only the block that differs gets copied.","当序列开始分叉时，只复制不同的那个块。"],[367.47,372.69,161,"This is copy-on-write, exactly what an operating system does when a process forks.","这就是写时复制，正是操作系统在进程 fork 时所做的事情。"],[373.04,376.46,161,"So the prompt's KV cache can be up to N times smaller.","所以提示的 KV 缓存最多可以缩小到 N 分之一。"],[376.81,382.87,161,"For long prompts, like a big document or a long system prompt, that's a huge saving.","对于长提示，比如一份大文档或一段很长的系统提示，这能节省大量显存。"],[384.12,385.9,162,"Beam search benefits even more.","束搜索受益更多。"],[386.25,392.21,162,"Remember from earlier lectures: beam search keeps the top K candidate sequences at each step.","回忆一下之前的课：束搜索在每一步保留前 K 个候选序列。"],[392.56,400.16,162,"Traditionally, each beam keeps a full copy of its KV cache, even though beams usually share a long common prefix.","传统做法中，每个束都保存一份完整的 KV 缓存，尽管各个束通常共享很长的公共前缀。"],[400.51,407.42,162,"With PagedAttention, beams share the blocks of their common prefix, and only divergent tokens need new blocks.","用 PagedAttention，各个束共享公共前缀的块，只有分叉出来的 token 才需要新块。"],[407.77,412.13,162,"When a beam is pruned, we just decrement the reference counts of its blocks.","当一个束被剪掉时，我们只需把它的块的引用计数减一。"],[412.48,416.27,162,"And a physical block is freed only when its count reaches zero.","物理块只有在引用计数降到零时才会被释放。"],[416.62,422.4,162,"That's garbage collection with reference counting, another idea straight out of systems programming.","这就是基于引用计数的垃圾回收，又一个直接来自系统编程的思想。"],[422.75,428.5,162,"The savings for beam search are large, typically fifty to seventy percent of the KV memory.","束搜索节省的显存很可观，通常是 KV 显存的百分之五十到七十。"],[428.85,435.18,162,"The exact number depends on the beam width, and on how long the beams keep sharing a prefix.","具体数字取决于束宽，以及各个束共享前缀的时间有多长。"],[436.43,442.95,163,"What happens if the GPU still runs out of memory, for example when many long answers are being generated at once?","如果 GPU 显存仍然不够用，比如同时生成很多长回答时，会发生什么？"],[443.3,449.11,163,"vLLM handles this the way an operating system handles too many processes: preemption.","vLLM 像操作系统处理进程过多那样来处理：抢占。"],[449.46,458.63,163,"Option one is swapping: move some requests' KV blocks from GPU memory to CPU memory, and swap them back when there's room.","方案一是换出：把部分请求的 KV 块从 GPU 显存移到 CPU 内存，等有空间时再换回来。"],[458.98,463.46,163,"That's just like an operating system swapping memory pages to disk.","这就像操作系统把内存页换出到磁盘一样。"],[463.81,471.71,163,"Option two is recomputation: throw the KV blocks away entirely, and recompute them when the request resumes.","方案二是重新计算：把 KV 块彻底丢掉，等请求恢复时再重新计算。"],[472.06,480.94,163,"That costs extra compute, but since recomputing a prompt is a fast prefill pass, it's often reasonable, and it needs no CPU memory.","这会多花一些计算，但由于重新计算提示只是一次很快的预填充，通常是可以接受的，而且不需要 CPU 内存。"],[481.29,490.21,163,"Which request gets preempted? With first-come-first-served, it's the most recently arrived one, so earlier requests always make progress.","哪个请求会被抢占？在先来先服务策略下，是最晚到达的那个，这样较早的请求总能向前推进。"],[490.56,493.32,163,"That keeps things fair, and avoids starvation.","这保证了公平，也避免了饥饿。"],[493.67,503.74,163,"That completes our tour of efficient inference: a smaller KV cache, paged memory, speculative decoding, FlashAttention and continuous batching.","高效推理之旅到此结束：更小的 KV 缓存、分页内存、推测解码、FlashAttention 和连续批处理。"],[504.09,509.07,163,"Together, they make serving many times cheaper than a naive implementation.","它们合在一起，让推理服务比简单实现便宜许多倍。"],[510.32,516.29,164,"We've now covered the whole stack: architectures, compression, training, and inference systems.","我们现在已经讲完了整个技术栈：架构、压缩、训练和推理系统。"],[516.64,518.48,164,"To close, let's look ahead.","最后，我们来展望一下未来。"],[518.83,525.97,164,"The big trend is that hardware, algorithms and systems are now designed together, rather than separately.","大趋势是：硬件、算法和系统如今是协同设计的，而不是各自独立设计。"],[526.32,532.42,164,"And the question every lab is asking is: what will make tokens another ten times cheaper next?","每个实验室都在问的问题是：接下来，什么能让 token 再便宜十倍？"],[533.67,539.98,165,"Here's my view of where the next ten-times improvement may come from, as of two thousand twenty-six.","这是我对截至 2026 年，下一个十倍提升可能来自哪里的看法。"],[540.33,546.3,165,"Some of these are vendor claims or very recent work, so treat the specific numbers with care.","其中有些是厂商的说法或非常新的工作，所以对具体数字要谨慎看待。"],[546.65,549.45,165,"First, sparse attention is now in production.","第一，稀疏注意力已经投入生产使用。"],[549.8,557.85,165,"DeepSeek-V3.2 uses a lightweight indexer to select the top-k most relevant past tokens for each query.","DeepSeek-V3.2 用一个轻量级索引器，为每个 query 选出最相关的前 k 个历史 token。"],[558.2,565.68,165,"And DeepSeek-V4 mixes compressed and sparse attention, to reach million-token contexts.","而 DeepSeek-V4 混合使用压缩注意力和稀疏注意力，达到百万 token 的上下文。"],[566.03,569.0,165,"Second, linear and hybrid attention.","第二，线性注意力和混合注意力。"],[569.35,580.06,165,"Models such as Qwen3-Next, Kimi Linear and Nemotron-H mix Gated DeltaNet or Mamba layers, whose state doesn't grow with length, with a few full attention layers.","Qwen3-Next、Kimi Linear 和 Nemotron-H 等模型把状态不随长度增长的 Gated DeltaNet 或 Mamba 层，与少量全注意力层混合在一起。"],[580.41,583.67,165,"So for most layers, the KV cache stops growing.","所以对大多数层来说，KV 缓存不再增长。"],[584.02,595.61,165,"Third, low-bit everything: FP8 training is now standard, and FP4 formats like NVFP4 are arriving for inference on the newest GPUs, Blackwell and Rubin.","第三，全面低比特：FP8 训练已成标准，而 NVFP4 这样的 FP4 格式正在最新的 Blackwell 和 Rubin GPU 上用于推理。"],[595.96,602.8,165,"Vendors claim around ten times lower cost per token for large MoE models, but that claim is unverified.","厂商声称大型 MoE 模型的每 token 成本可降低约十倍，但这一说法尚未得到验证。"],[603.15,612.1,165,"Fourth, disaggregated serving: prefill and decode, and sometimes even attention and FFN, run on different GPUs.","第四，分离式推理服务：预填充和解码，有时甚至注意力和 FFN，分别在不同的 GPU 上运行。"],[612.45,618.65,165,"The KV cache is sent over fast networks, as in llm-d and Mooncake.","KV 缓存通过高速网络传输，比如 llm-d 和 Mooncake。"],[619.0,624.4,165,"Fifth, efficient reasoning: for reasoning models, thinking tokens dominate the cost.","第五，高效推理：对推理模型来说，思考 token 占了成本的大头。"],[624.75,631.75,165,"So thinking budgets, adaptive effort, multi-token prediction and speculative decoding all matter.","所以思考预算、自适应投入、多 token 预测和推测解码都很重要。"],[632.1,636.08,165,"The red line sums it up: the frontier is co-design.","红色这句话做了总结：前沿在于协同设计。"],[636.43,640.65,165,"Notice how every row connects to something we covered today.","注意，每一行都与我们今天讲过的内容有关。"],[641.9,650.11,166,"One more future direction is hybrid efficiency: combining several of today's techniques in one method, because they're largely complementary.","另一个未来方向是混合效率：把今天讲的几种技术结合到一个方法中，因为它们在很大程度上是互补的。"],[650.46,653.09,166,"QLoRA combines quantization with LoRA.","QLoRA 把量化和 LoRA 结合在一起。"],[653.44,662.62,166,"The frozen base model is stored in four bits, and you train LoRA adapters on top, which lets you fine-tune quite large models on a single GPU.","冻结的基座模型用四比特存储，在其上训练 LoRA 适配器，这让你能在单张 GPU 上微调相当大的模型。"],[662.97,671.69,166,"LongLoRA combines LoRA with an efficient sparse attention pattern during fine-tuning, to extend a model's context length cheaply.","LongLoRA 在微调时把 LoRA 与高效的稀疏注意力模式结合，低成本地扩展模型的上下文长度。"],[672.04,680.43,166,"QMoE combines MoE with extreme quantization, compressing trillion-parameter MoE models to under one bit per parameter.","QMoE 把 MoE 与极端量化结合，把万亿参数的 MoE 模型压缩到每个参数不到一比特。"],[680.78,689.59,166,"The general lesson: don't think of quantization, sparsity, low-rank adaptation and efficient attention as competing options.","一般性的经验是：不要把量化、稀疏、低秩适配和高效注意力看作相互竞争的选项。"],[689.94,691.69,166,"The best systems stack them.","最好的系统会把它们叠加起来使用。"],[692.04,694.96,166,"That's a good mindset for your own projects too.","这对你们自己的项目来说也是一种很好的思路。"],[696.21,698.82,167,"Now it's time for some discussion.","现在是讨论时间。"],[699.17,705.35,167,"Take a few minutes to think about one or two of these questions, ideally together with your classmates.","花几分钟思考其中一两个问题，最好和你的同学一起讨论。"],[705.7,711.44,167,"First: of all the techniques today, which one would help your final project most, and why?","第一：在今天讲的所有技术中，哪一个对你的期末项目帮助最大，为什么？"],[711.79,719.76,167,"For example, would you use QLoRA to fine-tune, four-bit quantization to serve, or vLLM to speed up evaluation?","比如，你会用 QLoRA 来微调，用四比特量化来部署，还是用 vLLM 来加速评测？"],[720.11,725.53,167,"Second: we said the real bottleneck is often moving bytes, not doing arithmetic.","第二：我们说过，真正的瓶颈往往是搬运字节，而不是做算术。"],[725.88,732.71,167,"Pick one method from today, like GQA, FlashAttention, PagedAttention or speculative decoding.","从今天的内容中挑一个方法，比如 GQA、FlashAttention、PagedAttention 或推测解码。"],[733.06,740.68,167,"Then explain which of our four costs it reduces: FLOPs, bytes moved, bytes stored, or communication.","然后解释它降低了我们四种成本中的哪一种：浮点运算、搬运的字节、存储的字节，还是通信。"],[741.03,750.44,167,"Third, a bigger question: as models get cheaper to run, will that make AI more equal, or will the biggest players simply build even bigger models?","第三，一个更大的问题：随着模型运行成本降低，AI 会变得更加平等，还是最大的玩家只会造出更大的模型？"],[750.79,753.7,167,"Think back to the slide about the productivity gap.","回想一下关于生产力差距的那一页。"],[754.95,758.03,168,"These are the resources I drew on for today.","这些是我今天参考的资料。"],[758.38,770.41,168,"Especially Song Han's efficient ML course at MIT, the LLM-Shearing project, and several excellent video tutorials, including the one I used for speculative decoding.","特别是 MIT 韩松老师的高效机器学习课程、LLM-Shearing 项目，以及几个优秀的视频教程，包括我讲推测解码时用到的那个。"],[770.76,773.85,168,"I'd encourage you to look at them if you want to go deeper.","如果你想深入学习，我鼓励你去看看。"],[774.2,780.06,168,"Let me wrap up. The one question for today was: where does the time and memory go?","我来总结一下。今天的核心问题是：时间和显存都花到哪里去了？"],[780.41,787.45,168,"We saw that the answer is often not FLOPs, but bytes: bytes moved, bytes stored, and bytes communicated.","我们看到，答案往往不是浮点运算，而是字节：搬运的字节、存储的字节和通信的字节。"],[787.8,793.11,168,"Architectures like GQA, MLA and MoE make each token cheaper.","GQA、MLA 和 MoE 这样的架构让每个 token 更便宜。"],[793.46,798.82,168,"Compression with quantization, pruning and distillation shrinks trained models.","量化、剪枝和蒸馏这些压缩方法让训练好的模型变小。"],[799.17,803.21,168,"LoRA, ZeRO and parallelism make training feasible.","LoRA、ZeRO 和并行让训练变得可行。"],[803.56,811.65,168,"And the KV cache, PagedAttention, speculative decoding, FlashAttention and continuous batching make serving fast and cheap.","而 KV 缓存、PagedAttention、推测解码、FlashAttention 和连续批处理让推理服务又快又便宜。"],[812.0,816.37,168,"The horse can run fast on very little food, if you're clever about it.","只要方法得当，马儿可以吃得很少，却跑得很快。"],[816.72,818.79,168,"This was our last regular lecture.","这是我们最后一次常规课程。"],[819.14,825.11,168,"Next time, in Lecture twelve, we'll have a guest lecture on LLM applications and the future.","下一次，第十二讲，我们会有一场关于大模型应用与未来的嘉宾讲座。"],[825.46,830.1,168,"It's a chance to see how all of this is used in the real world, and where the field is going.","这是一个了解这些技术在现实世界中如何应用、以及这个领域将走向何方的好机会。"],[830.45,836.55,168,"Finally, good luck with your final projects. Many of you will use exactly the tools from today.","最后，祝大家期末项目顺利。你们很多人都会用到今天讲的这些工具。"],[836.9,841.84,168,"Start early, keep experiments small and cheap, and enjoy building something of your own.","尽早开始，让实验保持小而省，享受亲手打造属于自己的东西的过程。"],[842.19,846.11,168,"Thank you all for a great semester of lectures. Goodbye!","感谢大家这学期的陪伴。再见！"]]}]};
